UID:32v5qbhdf74t6rs9vgjdi6ou9h@google.com
CREATED:20170903T151902Z
DESCRIPTION:"In the somewhat crowded scene of Tuareg guitarists\, Mdou stan
 ds apart from his peers. One of the few original singer/songwriters willing
  to experiment and push the boundaries of the genre\, his unconventional st
 yles have won him accolades both in Niger and abroad.\n\nMdou Moctar hails 
 from Abalak\, in the Azawagh desert of Niger. He taught himself the guitar 
 at a young age on a homemade instrument. Inspired by returning Ishumar\, Md
 ou traveled the road to Libya where he traveled and worked odd jobs. As cha
 nce had\, he would meet some of the now famous guitarists and further his m
 usical studies. He returned home with a guitar and a dream.\n\nRising to th
 e status as local celebrity\, in 2008 he traveled to Nigeria to record his 
 first album “Anar” – a psychedelic electronic album of Tuareg guitar\, beca
 me an instant success throughout the mp3 networks of West Africa. “Tahoulti
 ne\,” one of the standout tracks\, was later featured on the compilation “M
 usic from Saharan Cellphones.”\n\nIn 2013\, he released his first internati
 onal album\, “Afelan\,” rocking and raw sessions recorded live at his homet
 own in Niger. This was followed by the 2014 vinyl release of “Anar.” In 201
 5\, he starred in the first ever Tuareg language film\, a fictional story o
 f the struggle of a guitarist trying to make it against all odds in Agadez.
  The film continues to be screened at festivals around the world.\n\nHe has
  toured throughout Europe and North America."\n\nhttp://thebishopbar.com\nh
 ttps://www.facebook.com/events/1856522244664042/\nhttp://sahelsounds.com/md
 ou-moctar
LAST-MODIFIED:20170903T151902Z
LOCATION:The Bishop 
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Mdou Moctar  18+
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
