DESCRIPTION:21+ BENEFIT FOR FOOD NOT BOMBS\n"Join us for a night of great m
 usic and dancing to benefit Food Not Bombs and the Bloomington Solidarity N
 etwork!\n\n~featuring~\n\nExWo - these badass jazz gals took btown by storm
  last year with their totally groovable & super fun tunage. is it neo-soul?
  is it jazz? is it funk? you decide. i think i saw them do an outkast cover
  once omg for real don't miss em.\n\nDoozie - newish local pop-punkish grou
 p\, they came out w this super rad demo ep this year and i personally canno
 t wait to rock out to these angsty upbeat songs! https://dooziedoozie.bandc
 amp.com/releases\n\nOnce we're all warmed up and groovin'\, local wonders D
 J EVAN L and GINNYPEP & SKELETON BONE will bring down the house with a dive
 rse mix of danceable tunes - some hip hop\, some 80s hits\, some house? you
 'll have to come find out whats up their sleeves this time!\n\nAt midnight\
 , DJ GOOD PEOPLE will take it away with their bi-monthly\, no cover dance p
 arty! (but u should still donate 2 the causes if u can!)\n\nplease bring $5
 -10 CASH for these great local causes:\n\nFOOD NOT BOMBS is a totally rad (
 and totally broke) group of folks who make meals for those experiencing hom
 elessness or food insecurity every sunday using rescued\, donated and upcyc
 led food! feel free to bring any non-perishables\, spices\, cooking oils\, 
 utensils\, containers\, anything u don't need and wanna donate!\n\nBLOOMING
 TON SOLIDARITY NETWORK is a volunteer-run organization dedicated to fightin
 g for the rights and against the abuse of tenants and workers.\n\n21+ NO HA
 RASSMENT TOLERATED. be cool y'all"\n\nhttps://www.facebook.com/events/12854
 83848130531/\nhttp://backdoorbloomington.com
LAST-MODIFIED:20160908T132726Z
LOCATION:The Back Door
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:ExWo / Doozie / Ginnypep & Skeleton Bone / DJ Evan 21+
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
