  by Cardinal Stage Company\n\nSpiced with sweet transvestites\, mad scienti
 sts\, and a big chunk of Meat Loaf\, The Rocky Horror Picture Show is a cul
 t phenomenon unlike any film or musical you’ve ever seen! The party begins 
 with a “de-virginization ritual” a half hour before each screening (trust u
 s – it doesn’t hurt). This initiation ceremony is fun for newbies and veter
 ans alike.\n\nTHIS IS A SCREENING.\n\nEvent Host: Oriana Perón\n\nFriday\, 
 October 27\, 2017\n11:30 pm: “De-virginization” ritual\nMidnight: First Scr
 eening\n\nSaturday\, October 28\, 2017\n11:30 pm: “De-virginization” ritual
 \nMidnight: Second Screening\n\nTICKETS:\n$15 with costume and $20 without 
 costume.\nProp bags available for $5. Prop bags can be pre-purchased or pur
 chased at the door with cash only.\n\nFIND TICKETS AT:\ncardinalstage.org\n
 812.336.9300\nCardinal Stage Company Box Office (900 S Walnut St.)\nBCT Box
  Office (114 E. Kirkwood Ave.)\n\nProceeds from this event will benefit Car
 dinal's Education and Outreach programs including the IU Credit Union Educa
 tion Initiative\, the Cardinal for Kids series of plays for young audiences
 \, and the Student Matinee Program for local high school students. For more
  information about these vital programs\, please visit cardinalstage.org/ou
 treach. \n\nMore info at cardinalstage.org.\nhttps://www.facebook.com/event
 s/349743332144855/
