BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Let's Go! Bloomington
DTSTART:20160918T000000Z
DTEND:20160918T033000Z
DTSTAMP:20260905T041548Z
UID:a8aodjl3g6j7juk1h5rb9s775k@google.com
CREATED:20160823T192714Z
DESCRIPTION:$15 \n\nFrom the FB Event Page:\n\nBoth line ups of Bloomington
  punk rock legends THE GIZMOS share the stage for the first time!\n\nTHE GI
 ZMOS (1976)\nTHE GIZMOS (1979)\nSWIM TEAM (Cincinnatti)\nLAFFING GAS (Bloom
 ington HC)\nDJ Donovan spinning punk rock all night long\nCOME THIRSTY\, WE
 'LL SELL YOU CHEAP BEER!!!!\n@ the VOID\n$15 at the door\n(pre sale tix ava
 ilable at LANDLOCKED for $14)\nDoors and DJs at 8\, music starts at 9\n\nTH
 E GIZMOS are probably the most enduring gem in the crown of Indiana punk hi
 story\, and this is probably your only chance to see both incarnations on t
 he same night. The first\, "classic\," 1976\, "proto-punk" line up was a ho
 dge podge of fanzine rock and roll nerds who converged in Bloomington\, and
  under the guidance of GULCHER RECORDS recorded songs like "Muff Divin' in 
 Wilkie South\," "Human Garbage Disposal\," and "Gimme Back My Foreskin." Th
 e group disbanded after 3 shows and 1 collaberation with Johnny "Cougar" Me
 llencamp. The 2nd line up (let's refer to it as the Dale Lawrence era\, sha
 ll we?) picked up the freak flag and let it keep on flying. If songs like "
 The Midwest Can Be All Right\," "Pay\," and "Dead Astronaut" don't get your
  teenage blood pumpin' then you better check your pulse\, you're either dea
 d or completely square.\n\nSWIM TEAM channels the Breeders and X Ray Spex i
 nto a more grungified product\, while LAFFING GAS likes their brand of hard
 core just a little weird around the edges.\n\nCome early\, stay late!\n\nPo
 st your fav GIZMOS paraphenilia below\, let's get ready to party\n\nhttp://
 thevoidbloomington.tumblr.com\nhttps://www.facebook.com/events/288580554842
 729/?notif_t=plan_user_invited&notif_id=1471980250912094
LAST-MODIFIED:20160823T192714Z
LOCATION:The Void
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:The Gizmos / Swim Team / Laffing Gas
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
