DESCRIPTION:<p><span style="color: rgb(0\, 0\, 0)\;"><em>"In               
                                    a postcard-perfect                      
                             seaside village in                             
                      1910\, an eccentric (to                               
                    put it mildly)                                          
         leisure-class family                                               
    whiles away the                                                  summer.
  But something                                                  troubling i
 s afoot:                                                  what’s behind the
                                                   string of tourists       
                                            gone mysteriously               
                                    missing?</em></span></p><br><span style=
 "color: rgb(0\, 0\, 0)\;"><em>Former&nbsp\;enfant                          
                           terrible&nbsp\;Bruno                             
                      Dumont continues his                                  
                 surprising foray into                                      
             farce—which began with                                         
          2014’s acclaimed&nbsp\;Li’l                                       
              Quinquin—with                                                 
  this surreal\, oddball                                                  mi
