DESCRIPTION:<div class="js-xd-read-more-toggle-view read-more__toggle-view"
 ><div class="js-xd-read-more-contents l-mar-top-3" data-automation="listing
 -event-description"><p><span>Integrating Harm Reduction and Case Management
  </span></p><p><span>10:00 to 3:00 (lunch break from 12:00-1:00)</span><br>
 <br><span>Training Overview: This half-day training outlines an integrated 
 approach to conducting case management for people who use drugs. This cours
 e details how to facilitate an integrated prevention counseling session. Cr
 itical counseling skills and concepts are explored in depth and role plays 
 offer multiple opportunities to practice delivering case management and cou
 nseling for people who use drugs. </span><br><br><span>Training Objectives:
  By the end of this training\, participants will be able to: </span><br><sp
 an>• Identify three applications of harm reduction principles to case manag
 ement\; </span><br><span>• Describe three ways that people who use drugs be
 nefit from harm reduction case management\; </span><br><span>• Demonstrate 
 three effective case management strategies in working with people who use d
 rugs\;</span><br><span>• Identify four common case management needs for peo
 ple who use drugs.</span></p>&nbsp\;<a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=h
 ttps%3A%2F%2Fwww.eventbrite.com%2Fe%2Fharm-reduction-and-case-management-ti
 ckets-43767311206&amp\;sa=D&amp\;usd=2&amp\;usg=AFQjCNGfau0OxxLi_HvuxddS71j
 tI-SpCA" target="_blank">https://www.eventbrite.com/e/harm-reduction-and-ca
 se-management-tickets-43767311206</a>
LAST-MODIFIED:20180315T104517Z
LOCATION:Monroe County Public Library
