DTEND:20170405T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20260905T041548Z
UID:kh6lenhambnc3sco592cbfv6f8@google.com
CREATED:20170319T122051Z
DESCRIPTION:$6 suggested donation. \n\n"On April 4th\, movie theaters acros
 s the country will be participating collectively in a single-day screening 
 of the film adaptation of George Orwell's 1984. This date was chosen becaus
 e it's the day George Orwell's protagonist Winston Smith begins rebelling a
 gainst his oppressive government by keeping a forbidden diary.\n\nWe at the
  Cicada Cinema strongly believe in supporting the National Endowment for th
 e Arts and see any attempt to defund or eliminate that program as an attack
  on free speech and creative expression through entertainment. This event p
 rovides a chance for communities around the country to show their unity and
  have their voices heard. We are excited to represent Bloomington's screeni
 ngs of the film 1984.\n\nThe late John Hurt co-stars with Richard Burton (i
 n his final screen appearance) in this grim\, impressive\, and powerful ver
 sion of George Orwell’s dystopian classic. Music by the Eurythmics. 113 min
 .\n\nPlease join us on Tuesday\, April 4th at The Void (1607 S. Rogers) in 
 a national day of protest."\n\nSreening times:\n7pm and 9:30pm\n\nhttps://w
 ww.facebook.com/events/1496453897054815/\nhttp://thevoidbloomington.tumblr.
 com\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20170319T122139Z
LOCATION:The Void
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Cicada Cinema Screening: 1984
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
