CREATED:20170409T144532Z
DESCRIPTION:English Grad Solidarity Coalition have recently discovered that
  political scientist and author Charles Murray is coming to speak at IU on 
 April 11th. This became a concern immediately to us as Murray is designated
  as a white nationalist by the Southern Poverty Law Center and argues viole
 nt\, non-scientific claims against non-white racial groups in his famous bo
 ok\, The Bell Curve. We condemn IU’s decision to invite this speaker and su
 pport this letter to President Michael McRobbie\, penned by Rafael Khachatu
 rian and Mike Kovanda from the Political Science Department.\n\nAs a group 
 dedicated to the protection of disenfranchised graduate students within and
  outside our department\, EGSC plans to (alongside the letter) organize a r
 ally at 6PM outside President’s Hall (Franklin Hall\, by Sample Gates) to v
 oice our concerns and disapproval of IU’s invitation of Murray and Murray’s
  hateful viewpoints themselves. We have attached here also the flyer of the
  event and encourage people to reserve tickets to the event and not show up
 /show up to the protest as a statement against the talk. We encourage every
 one to participate in whatever way they can!\n\nEGSC\n\nThe Letter: https:/
