BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Let's Go! Bloomington
DTSTART:20180328T173000Z
DTEND:20180328T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20260905T041548Z
UID:7jkshacbvcso5v1sbcjpkav3ed@google.com
CREATED:20180315T105948Z
DESCRIPTION:<br><div class="js-xd-read-more-toggle-view read-more__toggle-v
 iew"><div class="js-xd-read-more-contents l-mar-top-3" data-automation="lis
 ting-event-description"><p><span>Training Overview: This half-day training 
 will discuss the application of harm reduction in substance use treatment p
 rograms and settings. Harm reduction is a set of practical strategies that 
 reduce negative consequences of drug use and improve the quality of the cli
 ent’s life based on harm reduction principles. This approach can be challen
 ging for providers trained in traditional substance use treatment methods b
 ut can provide additional tools to assist clients in moving towards their r
 ecovery goals. Harm reduction principles incorporate a spectrum of strategi
 es including safer and managed use\, as well as abstinence. This approach h
 elps providers effectively meet their clients where they are and assist the
 m in moving towards their recovery goals. Participants will develop an unde
 rstanding of the principles of harm reduction\, participate in activities d
 esigned to assist them in exploring attitudes and beliefs about harm reduct
 ion\, and develop practical skills and interventions that can be used in th
 eir work. </span><br><br><span>Training Objectives: By the end of this trai
 ning participants will be able to: </span><br><span>• Define three principl
 es of harm reduction in relation to substance use treatment\; </span><br><s
 pan>• Identify three key attributes that support applying harm reduction ap
 proaches and principles\; </span><br><span>• Identify four challenges and b
 arriers to treatment and recovery that people who use drugs face\;</span><b
 r><span>• Explore how harm reduction can protect and reengage people who ex
 perience relapse during substance use treatment and their recovery journey\
 ; </span><br><span>• Identify three strategies to engage participants in su
 bstance use treatment and optimize their recovery goals.</span></p><p><span
 >Free.<br></span></p><p><span>Presented by the Indiana Recovery Alliance.<b
 r><a href="http://indianarecoveryalliance.org/">http://indianarecoveryallia
 nce.org/</a><br></span></p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20180315T105948Z
LOCATION:Monroe County Public Library
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Workshop: Incorporating Harm Reduction Into Substance Use Treatment
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
