DESCRIPTION:"<span style="color: rgb(85\, 86\, 90)\; font-family: azo-sans-
 web\, sans-serif\; font-size: 17px\;">13 year-old Jane has always had troub
 le making choices. Looking for an escape\, she seeks refuge in the classic 
 '80s video game\, "The Oregon Trail" — where the choices are clear\, the re
 sults are sure\, and there's always another life to live (after everyone di
 es of dysentery). But as time blurs\, the boundaries between game and reali
 ty become hazy\, until Jane finds herself leaping headfirst into the world 
 of The Oregon Trail\, where she's forced to confront the choices she's made
 \, connect with her family\, keep her oxen safe\, and ford the river of lif
 e."</span><br><span style="color: rgb(85\, 86\, 90)\; font-family: azo-sans
 -web\, sans-serif\; font-size: 17px\;">$10-$20</span><br>http://newplays.or
 g/
LAST-MODIFIED:20180227T014838Z
LOCATION:Bloomington Playwrights Project
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:A Play: The Oregon Trail
TRANSP:OPAQUE
