DTSTART:20170701T003000Z
DTEND:20170701T033000Z
DTSTAMP:20260905T041548Z
UID:mn9ivug96ahtk2ho23oukvo3t4@google.com
CREATED:20170524T221507Z
DESCRIPTION:AS BAD AS THEY\na play by Bella Bravo\n\nIn AS BAD AS THEY\, Ca
 leb Ternin decides to quit using\, leaving his sister Jordan to decipher th
 e fine line between her impulse to help and her impulse to control. This pl
 ay is set in present-day Bloomington\, Indiana—in the midst of the Midwest’
 s opioid-heroin epidemic.\n\nThe play opens on the estranged lives of the T
 ernin siblings\, reuniting on the most dangerous day for an addict—the date
  of release from state custody. On this day\, the dosage that Caleb handled
  two weeks before could cause his death.\n\n. . . And it's a comedy.\n\nfea
 turing........................William McHenry\, Janelle Beasley\, Michael B
 arton\, Charlie Jones\, Miles Grimmer\, Cody St. Clair\, Natalie Bainter\, 
 Courtney Foster\, Kim Naeseth\, and Brandon Schaaf\n\n.....................
 ...Music by Jon Meador\, Costumes by Morgan Eldridge\, Props by Wendy Lee S
 pacek\, Sets by Alan Crenshaw\, and Lighting by Bella Bravo\n\nrun time ~90
  minutes\n w 10-minute intermission\n\n$5-10 suggested donation$ ~~ go to b
 enefit Courage to Change\, a peer-run\, sober-living and low-barrier halfwa
 y house in Bloomington\n\nhttps://www.facebook.com/events/1435438603181746/
LAST-MODIFIED:20170524T221507Z
LOCATION:The Blockhouse
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:As Bad As They (a play)
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
