BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Let's Go! Bloomington
DTSTART:20170314T230000Z
DTEND:20170315T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20260905T041548Z
UID:9jpjieubtegntedag0qse60ih8@google.com
CREATED:20170218T044731Z
DESCRIPTION:From FB:\n\nBloomington Anarchist Black Cross presents five sho
 rt films on militant resistance to the AIDS crisis.\n\nIn the Tradition of 
 Stonewall (1994\, 29 min)\nA short documentary on the unpermitted breakaway
  march organized by ACT UP on the 25th anniversary of Stonewall.\n\nHolding
  Steady Without Screaming (1995\, 11 min)\nA short film subtitled "I Can't 
 Scream Because I Have to Hold the Camera Steady"\n\n...by any means necessa
 ry (1994\, 6 min)\nAn angry experimental film based on a text by Kiki Mason
 .\n\nThe Ashes Action (1996\, 29 min)\nA short documentary on the October 1
 1\, 1992 action in which individuals held a Political Funeral for those los
 t to AIDS\, throwing the ashes of friends and lovers on the White House law
 n.\n\nDavid Wojnarowicz (1994\, 2 min)\nA short piece on queer desire in a 
 time of plague\, from the No Alternative home video.\n\nAfterwards\, we wil
 l write letters to gay Black anarchist prisoner Michael Kimble. You can wri
 te Michael at:\nMichael Kimble #138017\n3700 Holman Unit\nAtmore\, AL 36503
 \n\nThe Anarchist Movie Night is a free monthly film series on freedom and 
 subversion. Showing documentaries\, features\, cult films\, and experimenta
 l shorts of an anarchic sort.\n\nMore info on movie nights and other events
  here: http://bloomingtonabc.noblogs.or/\nhttp://boxcarbooks.org\nhttps://w
 ww.facebook.com/events/1836134643318430/
LAST-MODIFIED:20170218T044731Z
LOCATION:Boxcar Books
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Anarchist Movie Night: Militant Resistance to the AIDs Crisis
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
