CREATED:20171210T144643Z
DESCRIPTION:<br>&nbsp\;On Tuesday\, December 20 at 7:00 p.m.\, the Shalom C
 ommunity Center\, the First United Methodist Church\, and other interfaith 
 leaders will join in a national movement to memorialize people who have exp
 erienced homelessness and passed away in the last year.<br><br>&nbsp\;The s
 ervice will take place in the sanctuary of the First United Methodist Churc
 h at <strong>219 E 4th St</strong> in Bloomington. First started 14 years a
 go\, the National Homeless Persons’ Memorial Service is held around the cou
 ntry on or close to the first day of winter and the longest night of the ye
 ar. Its purpose is to bring attention to the tragedy of homelessness and to
  honor those who have died during the past year.<br><br><a href="http://sha
 lomcommunitycenter.org/">http://shalomcommunitycenter.org/</a>
LAST-MODIFIED:20171210T144643Z
LOCATION:First United Methodist Church
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Annual Homeless Persons Memorial Service
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
