DESCRIPTION:<span style="color: rgb(75\, 79\, 86)\; font-family: &quot\;SF 
 Optimized&quot\;\, system-ui\, -apple-system\, system-ui\, &quot\;.SFNSText
 -Regular&quot\;\, sans-serif\; letter-spacing: -0.12px\; background-color: 
 rgb(255\, 255\, 255)\;">"Ina Diane Archer considers film history\, preserva
 tion and digital production as a continuum that extends into her art/filmma
 king practices. She humorously confronts social/cultural issues past and pr
 esent via cinema\, but the subtext is often based in personal narrative. Ar
 cher uses commercial films as material and appropriation and montage as str
 ategies to negotiate the difficult relationship of marginalized people to m
 edia representations trying to draw parallels between contemporary methods 
 and those of the past both thematically and self-reflexively with her use o
 f digital media. Her interest in montage extends into the arrangement of sc
 reens and objects within her film and video installations. Archer will inse
 rt herself with R.W. Fassbinder or Richard Widmark or she will appear AS Ro
 bert Evans or Richard Harris\, in scenarios that have otherwise excluded he
 r\, hoping\, playfully\, to interrogate the seductive pleasures and power o
 f cinema\, to “de-canonize” the familiar narratives of film history and to 
 complicate\, accepted cinematic representations."</span><br style="color: r
