BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Let's Go! Bloomington
DTSTART:20160826T220000Z
DTEND:20160827T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20260905T041548Z
UID:8bvf6d2flcfvqeuphikn7iddc8@google.com
CREATED:20160823T184631Z
DESCRIPTION:Free! https://www.facebook.com/events/189506958129057/\nFrom th
 e FB page:\n"Join us for a closing reception of Bill Bass: Visible Objects 
 on Friday August 26th from 6 - 8 pm at Breezeway Gallery.\n\nVisible Object
 s is an installation of basic physical materials and forms that have been m
 anipulated and expanded to emphasize various overlooked aspects of their na
 ture. Each object (a pillar\, a rock\, and a fragmented cinderblock) has be
 en appropriated from its original purpose\, augmented\, and recontextualize
 d into an art space in order to prompt a reexamination of it. In a reality 
 built on perception\, it is vital to continuously redefine and re-interpret
  the most basic objects\, materials\, and forms\, so as to expand not just 
 our understanding of them\, but also\, the realities they are used to const
 ruct.\n\nBill Bass (b. 1990 in New York) is a visual artist currently based
  in Bloomington\, Indiana. He received a BA from the University of Notre Da
 me where he studied studio art and philosophy and is currently working towa
 rds an MFA in Photography at Indiana University. Though his current work de
 als with photography and the digital image\, Bass’s practice is interdiscip
 linary and often includes different mediums. His work has been exhibited na
 tionally and is featured widely on the Internet.\n\nBreezeway Gallery is a 
 project space located between the Indiana University Art Museum and Indiana
  University’s Henry Radford Hope School of Fine Arts in Bloomington\, India
 na. Breezeway Gallery is curated by IU Art History MA student James Payne a
 nd Jenna Beasley under the advisement of IU Art History Professor Jeffrey S
 aletnik."
LAST-MODIFIED:20160823T184631Z
LOCATION:Breezeway Gallery
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Art : Bill Bass - Visible Objects
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
