DTSTART:20170208T000000Z
DTEND:20170208T020000Z
DTSTAMP:20260905T041548Z
UID:3n7ser73cj0d0ettevfsebdn28@google.com
CREATED:20170128T053831Z
DESCRIPTION:Free! All Ages! \n\nFrom FB:\n\nThis session's reading…\n'Cuban
  Anarchism: The History of a Movement’ by Frank Fernández\n\n“Read and Revo
 lt” is a reading group that facilitates discussions about this society and 
 the potential for liberation from an anarchist perspective. Discussions tak
 e place the first and third Tuesdays of each month at Boxcar Books\, starti
 ng at 7 PM. All are invited!\n\nA free printout of the text for each upcomi
 ng session will be provided at Boxcar Books for two weeks beforehand.\n\nTh
 e text can also be found online. It’s a long one this time\, so maybe start
  reading it sooner rather than later! http://theanarchistlibrary.org/librar
 y/frank-fernandez-cuban-anarchism-the-history-of-a-movement\n\n“Because of 
 its worker orientation\, we’re also dealing here with the first steps towar
 d what in the years to come would be known as anarchosyndicalism. Havana at
  this time had a workers’ organization of the first rank\, clearly the equa
 l of the Federación Regional Española. According to the well known Cuban hi
 storian\, Moreno Fraginals\, ‘The workers’ movement in Havana was the most 
 developed and the most class conscious in all of Latin America.’”\n\nhttps:
 //www.facebook.com/events/662505037264601/\nhttp://boxcarbooks.org\n\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20170128T053831Z
LOCATION:Boxcar Books
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:R&R discussion group: Cuban Anarchism
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
