DESCRIPTION:Hacking has an infamous beginning. However the more we move our
  lives and information online\, we need to safeguard our data. This has cre
 ated the need for Information Security as a career and a way of life.<br><b
 r>Hackers view the world with a critical lens. Where you see a IoT light th
 at you can turn on and off with your phone\, we see a potential botnet due 
 to lack of security updates. Where you see wireless networks\, we see (and 
 pentest) insecurity and data leakage.<br><br>This is a meetup to discuss (i
 n)security in all its forms. We are willing to have an open dialogue\, so w
 e all can learn.<br><br>3pm Free<br>All Ages<br><a href="https://www.reddit
 .com/r/bloomington/comments/bxh0f9/2600_hacking_meet_up_bloomington/" targe
 t="_blank">Event page</a>
LAST-MODIFIED:20190606T153631Z
LOCATION:College Mall Food Court 
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:2600 Hacking Meet-up
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
