DESCRIPTION:<html-blob>The Kinsey Institute is thrilled to present Blood Ba
 by\, a series of performances and participatory explorations of queer famil
 ies and parenthood\, gender\, and Earthly belonging\, created by visiting i
 nterdisciplinary performance artist Meg Foley. <br><br>Blood Baby has two p
 arts: Communion and Touch Library. Communion is a performance\, while Touch
  Library invites visitors to physically touch and experience some of the ma
 terials used by Meg and her collaborators.<br>Communion<br>November 10\, 11
 \, 12 at 5pm<br>Stewart's Hideaway\, Dunn Woods<br>&nbsp\;<br>Touch Library
 <br>November 10\, 11\, 12 at 6pm<br>Lindley Hall\, third floor\, Reading Ro
 om and Beebe Gallery<br>&nbsp\;<br>Touch Library Open Hours<br>November 12\
 , 12:30–3:30pm<br>Lindley Hall\, third floor\, Reading Room and Beebe Galle
 ry<br>Free. Mask Encouraged. All Ages</html-blob>
LAST-MODIFIED:20221107T184750Z
