DESCRIPTION:From the website:<br><p><i>The Passion of Joan of Arc</i>&nbsp\
 ;with live music written and performed by George Sarah featuring electronic
 s\, voices\, and strings</p><p>The critically acclaimed 1928 silent film by
 &nbsp\;Carl Dreyer&nbsp\;is brought to life with a haunting new score perfo
 rmed live which re-imagines the classic film (with a new 2018 restoration) 
 with a modern urgency. Combining electronic music with four voice choir and
  string quartet\, L.A. composer&nbsp\;George Sarah&nbsp\;has crafted a movi
 ng and an unforgettable visual and auditory experience. After being commiss
 ioned by Los Angeles Grand Performances to compose a live score for&nbsp\;<
 i>The Passion of Joan of Arc</i>&nbsp\;(<i>La Passion de Jeanne d’Arc</i>)\
 , Sarah has been performing this piece throughout the U.S.</p><p>George Sar
 ah&nbsp\;is an electronic composer and multi-instrumentalist. Born in Seoul
 \, South Korea\, he moved to the USA at the age of five. He has garnered cr
 itical acclaim for his unique brand of electronic acoustic music bridging t
 he normally discrete musical worlds of electronic and classical as well as 
 Americana and folk music. <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=COOcrSSV
 nEI"><b>Trailer</b></a><br></p><p>&nbsp\;8:pm $20. All Ages</p><p><a href="
 https://buskirkchumley.org/event/george_sarah_presents_the_passion_of_joan_
 of_arc/" id="ow423" __is_owner="true">Event page</a><br></p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20220925T153530Z
LOCATION:Buskirk-Chumley Theater
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Passion of Joan of Arc w/ live orchestration by George Sarah 
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
