DTSTART:20090318T000000Z
DTEND:20090318T030000Z
DTSTAMP:20260905T041548Z
UID:d1d1osmg601eh86k999fpp3m6c@google.com
CREATED:20090310T173023Z
DESCRIPTION:The Cinemat\, 123 S Walnut St\, Bloomington\, IN\n\nTuesday\, M
 arch 17\, 2009 8:00 PM\n\nCost: $5\n\n\n\nParis resident and Baltimore nati
 ve Dick Turner brings his eclectic experimental/pop/cabaret show to Bloomin
 gton for a stop on his world tour. Opening the show will be DMC +1\, featur
 ing locals David Miller (trumpet)\, Marty Belcher (saxes)\, Chris Rall (sax
 ) and Ian Yeager (electronics).\n\n\n\nTurner will perform songs from his P
 OPCYCLE\, his ever-growing collection of unusual\, often humorous and somet
 imes psychologically complex songs. These songs\, having such titles as "Ch
 inese Butterfly"\, "Daddy's Gun" and "Empty Pens"\, were composed to repres
 ent the unending variety of the human experience\, from the mundane to the 
 sublime\, from the absurd to questions of death and the ultimate goals of o
 ur existence.\n\n\nHis performances are marked by an intense theatricality 
 as he accompanies himself on his trombone while singing to his arrangements
 .\n\n\n\nDick Turner’s myspace page:\n\n\n\nhttp://www.myspace.com/turnerdi
 ck/\n\n\n\nFrom Turner:\n\n\n\nI do a sort of theatrical experimental/pop c
 abaret act. That is\, that's how I think people experience it. I composed c
 lassical music for a long time and then\, more or less out of the blue\, be
 gan writing songs. Now I write songs that seem to me to be in different sty
 les and hope\, by combining them in a set\, to create the feeling of develo
 pment\, without harmonic "digressions". (So\, in order to illustrate this\,
  in my songs above you have a Disco song "Let's have an Orgy" a Country son
 g "Chinese Butterfly"\, an experimental song "Box"\, a sort of psychologica
 l song called "I caught you going through my pockets"\, etc...) This was my
  working hypothesis\, in truth I just do whatever I feel like doing. I deci
 ded to write songs about anything dealing with life\, that is from the "ban
 al" to the "sublime" - my reason was \, by presenting a variety of songs\, 
 to give a picture of the overall life experience as it has so far revealed 
 itself to me. A second reason I started to write songs\, and to perform the
 m myself\, was to be able to present concerts with greater frequency than I
  did as a composer\, when I'd need to assemble groups of players\, rehearse
 \, rent concert halls\, etc. So I decided to sing and to play trombone solo
 s to pre-recorded music on a CD. This allows me to give concerts more regul
 arly\, even if I do miss playing with other musicians.\n\n\n\nFor more info
 rmation\, contact Marty Belcher at mbelcher53@hotmail.com
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T050834Z
LOCATION:Cinemat
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:DICK TURNER
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
