DESCRIPTION:Indian Jewelry\nHorns of Happiness (Weathering Alterations LP R
 elease Party)\nApache Dropout\nMonday\, October 5\n9 p.m.\n@ THE BISHOP\n$F
 IVE\n\n---------------------------------------\nINDIAN JEWELRY\nhttp://www.
 myspace.com/indianjewelry\n\nHad Indian Jewelry been conceived at the time\
 , they would have no doubt been the soundtrack to the David Lynch flick Wil
 d at Heart. They are the burning heart of Bobby Peru. They are the true Sca
 ry Spice. They come to you from The Black Hole of Calcutta\, Texas. They ar
 e not to be taken lightly. They are Beyond Thunderdome.\n\n----------------
 -----------------------\nHORNS OF HAPPINESS\nhttp://www.myspace.com/thehorn
 sofhappiness\n\nThis is the life project of Aaron Deer and a multitude of r
 ad humans - namely one drummer Shelly Harrison\, whose art installation "Do
 n't Rain on My Parade" served as the inspiration for Weathering Alterations
 \, the St. Ives LP that we will be partying for on the night of this show. 
 Have you been inspired lately? You wanna be?\n\n---------------------------
 ------------\nAPACHE DROPOUT\nhttp://www.myspace.com/apachedropout\n\nThis 
 the forefront of Bloomington's heavy-psych-underground. Apache Dropout's "A
 ll I'm Gonna Do Is Laugh" is my contender for Bloomington's Song of Year. Y
 ou'll never care to give a fuck ever again.\nAcid casualties\, this is your
  cure (?).\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T050811Z
LOCATION:The Bishop
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Indian Jewelry
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
