DESCRIPTION:From the Cicada Site:<br>Warren Beatty stars in this French New
  Wave-inspired drama directed by Arthur Penn (2 years before his 1967 maste
 rpiece <em>Bonnie and Clyde</em>). Beatty is a neurotic nightclub comedian 
 suffering from what seems to be an acute persecution complex after accumula
 ting a number of large gambling debts. Filmed in the gritty back alleys of 
 Chicago\, this hard-to-classify movie is truly a product of its time. It's 
 as if mad scientist mixed in equal parts film noir plot\, American iconogra
 phy\, and goofy new-wave editing\, with a dash of Charles Eames art. Plus\,
  this is all set to a bed of hip jazz improvisation by Stan Getz!<br>&nbsp\
 ;<br>8:pm $7 21+<br><a href="https://cicadacinema.com/products/mickey-one-n
 ovember-4-upland-wood-shop-8pm" id="ow3672" __is_owner="true">Event page</a
 >
