DESCRIPTION:​Join Black Lives Matter Bloomington for our Juneteenth Celebra
 tion &amp\; help with their Summer Necessity Drive<br><br>WEDNESDAY JUNE 19
 th 2019<br>6:00pm to 9:00pm<br>at the Banneker Community Center ​<br>WITH: 
 Food Trucks\, Music\, Info Tables\, &amp\; Kids Reading &amp\; Activities C
 orner! <br><br>Juneteenth is the oldest nationally celebrated commemoration
  of the ending of slavery in the United States. It commemorates African Ame
 rican freedom\, with an emphasis on education and achievement. Sometimes a 
 day\, a week\, or even the entire month is marked with celebrations\, guest
  speakers\, picnics and family gatherings. It is a time for reflection\, re
 joicing\, assessment\, self-improvement\, and for planning the afro-future.
 <br><br>#BLM B-town's celebration of Juneteenth is a part of their communit
 y outreach and coalition initiatives. They seek to educate\, engage and enj
 oy the town and community. <br><br>Music by DJ Jada Bee playing Prince and 
 80's/90's Tunes<br>&amp\; <br>Info tables from all of the organizations BLM
 's Necessity Drive supports:  Middle Way House\, Indiana Recovery Alliance\
 , &amp\; All-Options Pregnancy Resource Center (MORE TBA) <br><br>WITH a Ju
 neteenth Kids book story corner\, coloring pages &amp\; craft area!<br><br>
 COME celebrate Freedom DAY and give to the Necessity Drive<br><br>6pm <br>A
 ll Ages<br><a href="https://www.facebook.com/events/606380759880360/" id="o
 w2275" __is_owner="true">Event page</a>
LAST-MODIFIED:20190606T155445Z
LOCATION:Banneker Community Center
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Juneteenth Celebration & Summer Necessity Drive Drop Off
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
