 , Architecture and Design. Centering around the theme of empathy\, each stu
 dent has worked closely with collaborators of diverse backgrounds\, highlig
 hting topics such as gender and sexuality\, racial discrimination\, mental 
 health\, social change\, and immigration among others. This exhibition invi
 tes us to create a dialogue through the ability of understanding and the po
 wer of connection.</span><span><br></span><br><span>6pm Free</span><br><spa
 n>All Ages</span><br><span><a href="https://www.instagram.com/p/B72Xz9op54p
