DTSTART:20101106T180000Z
DTEND:20101106T213000Z
DTSTAMP:20260905T041548Z
UID:rddapjandma1go7rpqh38m9gl4@google.com
CREATED:20101027T181854Z
DESCRIPTION:Facebook Event: http://www.facebook.com/home.php#!/event.php?ei
 d=157802767591467\n\nThe Lodge\n101 E. 6th Street\nBloomington\, IN\n\nMark
  you calendars!!!!!\nBlaise Zekalo and Athobob Modeste Douoning will be tea
 ching Ivory Coast Drum and Dance Workshops!\nDrum @ 2pm\nDance @ 3:30pm\n\n
 ...Both Blaise and Athobob are professional Ivorian artists who have perfor
 med and shared their music and dance culture with audiences as members of N
 ational Troupes and Ballets from the Ivory Coast. With much enthusiasm\, th
 ey will be sharing their knowledge and talents with Dr. Djo Bi Productions 
 and the community of Bloomington (and beyond\, for those of you out-of-town
 ers)!\n\nDRUM WORKSHOP:\nThere will be an hour-and-fifteen minute hand drum
  workshop with Blaise from 2:00 ~ 3:15 p.m.\nParticipate in meaningful musi
 c communication in a group setting! All levels are welcome.\nThere will be 
 something for all drummers ~ from working on and refining tone\, slap\, bas
 s to catching and developing techniques on traditional Ivory Coast rhythms.
  Drum rental available for $5. Please call ahead (812.339.2070) to be sure 
 we have a drum for you.\n\nDANCE WORKSHOP:\nAt 3:30 p.m. Atho will teach a 
 two-hour African dance workshop.\nMove your body to the sounds of live Ivor
 y Coast Drumming! All levels are welcome.\nBring a friend\, your bare feet\
 , and be ready to smile as you learn traditional Ivory Coast dance movement
 s.\n\nCome out and support West African Culture and the West African Artist
 s who bring their talents to us!\n$20 for one class or take both for $35.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T050848Z
LOCATION:The Lodge
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Ivory Coast Drum and Dance Workshop
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
