DESCRIPTION:\nCheck back here for more info as it comes in! These are not t
 he only local businesses who are having Black Friday Events\, so watch arou
 nd town for more and ask your favorite stores if they are having Black Frid
 ay Events.\n\nBarefoot Kids\n615 W. Kirkwood\nWe will be having a big ‘Blac
 k Friday’ sale the day after Thanksgiving\, Nov. 26 – BIG sales on toys plu
 s in-store give-aways.\n...Also we are planning a holiday in-store Bobbie L
 ancaster performance\, DTBD.\n\nBikesmiths\n112 S. College\nContinuation of
  its annual $50\,000 sale every Nov. 15. This sale runs from Nov. 15 throug
 h $50\,000 of sales and always goes through Christmas (and typically into t
 he first week of the new year).\nEverything in our store is at least 10% of
 f\, some things more (including bikes\, everything).\n\nThe Bishop\, Fri.\,
  Nov. 26\, 9pm $5\, 18+\ncorner of 4th and Walnut\nAfter you finish shoppin
 g\, stop by the Bishop and relax with an old-time SQUARE DANCE w/ live musi
 c from JOE FULTON & FRIENDS and dance caller MICHAEL ISMERIO\n\nBoxcar Book
 s\n408 E. 6th\nBoxcar Books is closed on "black friday" in observance of "b
 uy nothing day"\, a worldwide protest against over-consumption.\n\nBy Hand 
 Gallery\n101 W. Kirkwood\, Suite #109\nThe day after Thanksgiving we will b
 e open late for the tree lighting and will serve hot apple cider.\n\nThe Co
 medy Attic\, corner of 4th and Walnut\nA crowd favorite in Bloomington\, Wa
 rrenB. Hall returns to The Comedy Attic this Thanksgiving weekend! Warren i
 s fresh off his appearance on Comics Unleashed and The Bob & Tom Show!\n\n\
 nHoliday Market\, Shower’s Bldg. 401 N. Morton\, Nov. 26-27\nVisit LFI Memb
 er Sadly Harmless and pick up some of her original calendars\, coffee mugs 
 or prints! See the above list to see other things often available at the Ho
 liday Market.\n\nLandlocked Music\, Nov. 26-28\n202 N. Walnut\nGive the gif
 t of music! Landlocked's Black Friday Celebration runs from Friday Nov. 26 
 - Sunday Nov. 28. Amazing limited edition releases made for independent ret
 ail ONLY from the likes of U2\, Tom Petty\, Bob Dylan\, Jimi Hendrix\, Bruc
 e Springsteen\, George Harrison\, Iron & Wine\, Black Keys\, Drive By Truck
 ers\, Black Crowes\, Cee Lo Green\, Sharon Jones & the Dap-Kings and many m
 ore. You simply cannot get these at the big box retailers. Plus a huge sale
  on used vinyl and CDs. And tons of recent releases for $10 from now til th
 e end of the month.\n\nSole Sensations\n414 S. College\nOpen 10-8 (extended
  hours) on Black Friday and will have all boots\, Smartwool socks\, and Haf
 linger slippers on sale 20% off.
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T050744Z
LOCATION:Local\, Independent Business in Bloomington\, IN
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Think Local First on Black Friday!
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
