DTSTAMP:20260905T041548Z
UID:4nnjks44r2fvrp9brja0fdb27b@google.com
CREATED:20230123T175039Z
DESCRIPTION:<h3><strong>IU Cultural Studies Department</strong></h3><h3><st
 rong><i>Occult Natures </i></strong><span style="font-weight: normal\;">lec
 ture series</span></h3><h3><strong>"Queer Goblins: As If There's Any Other 
 Kind" by Sean Grattan</strong></h3><h3><strong></strong></h3><p>In 2022\, O
 xford Dictionary chose “Goblin Mode” as the word of the year. The term gobl
 in mode describes an orientation towards unkemptness that defies and reject
 s social norms and expectations. The rise in prominence of goblin mode\, an
 d subsequently the image of the goblin\, signals a kind of dishevelment to 
 narratives of heteropatriarchal capital accumulation. While thinking about 
 the surging popularity of goblins and their mode\, this presentation seeks 
 to trace the long history of the queerness of goblins. From the goblins in 
 Christina Rosetti’s “The Goblin Market” to David Bowie’s alluringly tight p
 ants\, the goblin appears as a liminal and beckoning figure\, who often emb
 odies desires that disrupt familial structures and social reproduction.</p>
 <p> 5:30pm Free 21+</p><p> <a href="https://cstudies.indiana.edu/events/012
 523-SGrattan.html">https://cstudies.indiana.edu/events/012523-SGrattan.html
 </a></p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20230123T175039Z
LOCATION:The Bishop Bar
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:"Queer Goblins: As If There's Any Other Kind" lecture 21+
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
