BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Let's Go! Bloomington
DTSTART:20081123T010000Z
DTEND:20081123T050000Z
DTSTAMP:20260905T041548Z
UID:e5qbvo2o25eu6aqs6l5uk0cl3k@google.com
CREATED:20081119T160726Z
DESCRIPTION:WIUX (99.1 FM\, pure student radio) and Spirit of '68 Promotion
 s present:\n<br><br>\nMarnie Stern (from NYC\, NY\, Kill Rock Stars Records
 )<Br>\nFound Objects (from Bloomington\, IN\, Shut Up! I Love You Records)<
 Br>\nImpure Jazz (Bloomington)<Br>\n@ The Lodge/Space 101 (above Subway\, 6
 th and Walnut\, Bloomington\, IN)\nSaturday\, November 22\n8pm\n$8\, or $5 
 with a valid IU student ID\n<Br><br>\nMARNIE STERN (Kill Rock Stars Records
 )\nhttp://www.myspace.com/marniestern1\nMarnie Stern (born March 18\, 1976)
  is an American musician\, songwriter\, and guitarist. She resides in New Y
 ork City and has garnered much acclaim for her technical skill and finger-t
 apping style of guitar play. She released her debut CD\, In Advance of the 
 Broken Arm\, in 2007 on Kill Rock Stars. It was well received by critics\, 
 and The New York Times cited it as "The year's most exciting rock 'n' roll 
 album."\nAs her label puts it: "Ok. Let's get this out of the way. Marnie S
 tern can shred. She's a better guitar player than you\, or me\, or probably
  99% of the people who have ever looked at a guitar."\nMarnie will be on to
 ur in support of her latest record\, "This Is It and I Am It and You Are It
  and So Is That..."\, which features Zach Hill of Hella on the drums.\n<Br>
 <br>\nMarnie's live band includes guitarist Mark Shippy\, who was a member 
 of the legendary U.S. Maple and is now a member of the Chicago band Miracle
  Condition.\n\n<Br><Br>\nFOUND OBJECTS\nhttp://www.myspace.com/foundobjects
 isart\n"Found Objects strikes a balance between dreamy shoegaze landscapes 
 and feedback nightmares." - SUILY Records\, the myspace\n"Simply the best N
 ASA-sponsored-music-making-\nmind-blowing-nob-twiddlers from our fair city 
 of Bloomington." - Andy G.\n<Br><br>\nIMPURE JAZZ is a young local prog-roc
 k band. We're not talkin "prog" in the dirtiest sense of the word\; you wil
 l hear no Dream Theatre-esque wankery here - you will hear no insincerity\,
  no artificiality\, no bullshit. Nay\, we are talkin progressive music here
  - We're talkin unconventional song forms and rhythmically-asymmetrical phr
 ases and instrumental wizardry. We're talkin innovative musical ideas and a
  focus on creativity while ultimately retaining the positive energy of rock
  music. Energy.\nhttp://www.myspace.com/impurejazz\n\n<Br><Br>\nhttp://www.
 spiritof68promotions.com\n<Br><br>\nhttp://www.wiux.org
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T050636Z
LOCATION:The Lodge/Space 101
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:MARNIE STERN
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
