DESCRIPTION:Zolo is one of Indiana's longest-held political prisoners\, hav
 ing been held for over 30 years\, and sentenced to death twice along the wa
 y. Celebrating the 2nd anniversary of his release\, Zolo is an artist\, wri
 ter\, and organizer who\, just as he helped so many around him while he was
  imprisoned\, is now dedicated to achieving socio-political and economic su
 ccess while helping others in the process. Based in Gary\, this will be Zol
 o's first visit to Bloomington. Join us to welcome Zolo\, hear his story. C
 elebrate the successes of the past\, and see what it means to keep fighting
 . \n\n7:pm $? \n120 E. Kirkwood
LAST-MODIFIED:20190402T131627Z
LOCATION:Ballantine Room 109
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:A Legacy of Black Liberation in Indiana w/ Zolo Agona Azania
TRANSP:OPAQUE
