BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Let's Go! Bloomington
DTSTART:20090725T010000Z
DTEND:20090725T020000Z
DTSTAMP:20260905T041548Z
UID:ihln1labhd36cudn6pu5ltbjtg@google.com
CREATED:20090721T133518Z
DESCRIPTION:SOLDIER TO CIVILIAN: The Experiences and Transitions of America
 n and German Veterans of the War in Afghanistan\nThursday\, July 23rd at 9p
 m--on the front patio!\n\nSoldier to Civilian\, a new film documenting the 
 experience of veterans of the war in Afghanistan\, will have its Bloomingto
 n premier on Thursday\, July 23 at 9PM at Boxcar Books. This event is free 
 and open to the public.\n\nA timely and provocative documentary\, Soldier t
 o Civilian features interviews with German and American soldiers who served
  in Afghanistan. Veterans give first-hand accounts of life in a war zone an
 d reflect on their experience returning to civilian life.\n\nFilmmaker Ross
  Robinson began shooting in January 2009. He traveled throughout Germany\, 
 interviewing German soldiers and reserves and striking up conversations wit
 h civilians on the street. Upon his return to the United States\, Ross inte
 rviewed American soldiers and reserves in March and April 2009.\n\nThrough 
 candid and often poignant interviews\, veterans share their perspectives on
  the daily life of a soldier\, the meaning of patriotism\, and the difficul
 t transition back to civilian life. According to Robinson\, “Several interv
 iewees said that they had never had the chance to really talk in depth to a
 nyone about their experiences and described their participation in the film
  as therapeutic.”\n\n\n\nA Midwestern native from Dillsboro\, Indiana\, Ros
 s Robinson is a 2009 graduate of DePauw University\, where he completed a d
 ouble major in Communication and German.\n\nAs a junior\, he completed cour
 se work on German mass media at Humboldt University in Berlin. While studyi
 ng abroad\, Ross also interned at the Filmbüro Potsdam\, an independent tel
 evision and film production company. A Fulbright Scholar\, Ross will return
  to Germany this fall to teach English.\n\nSolider to Civilian will be scre
 ened outdoors on the patio of Boxcar Books. Following the film screening\, 
 there will be a Q&A session with Mr. Robinson. Boxcar Books is located at 4
 08 E. 6th Street in downtown Bloomington. For more information\, contact Ro
 ss Robinson at 812.548.3139.
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T050709Z
LOCATION:Boxcar Books
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Documentary: Soldier to Civilian
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
