UID:4i9l59t0jasclmb7r2eo910ik0@google.com
CREATED:20100210T162005Z
DESCRIPTION:The Buskirk-Chumley Theater proudly presents Indie sensation Th
 e Magnetic Fields on March 5\, 2010 at 8 PM. Tickets are $27.50 (reserved s
 eating) and will be available to donors and sponsors only starting Tuesday\
 , November 17\, 2009\, 11 AM. The general public has access to the tickets 
 a full week later\, on Tuesday\, November 24\, 2009\, 11 AM.\n\nThose in th
 e know might be familiar with The Magnetic Fields and their front man Steph
 in Merrit\, who lives and works in New York City. Adept at computer music p
 rogramming and production\, Merritt records his own albums and plays almost
  everything on them with help from cellist Sam Davol\, banjo player/second 
 guitarist John Woo\, and percussionist/ pianist Claudia Gonson. The Magneti
 c Fields have released six full-length CD's between 1993 and 1999\, all on 
 Merge Records. The Charm of the Highway Strip (1994) is an electro-country 
 meditation on life on the open road.\n\nHoliday (1994) has a more euro-pop 
 sound\, with songs about escape and nightlife. Get Lost (1995) has a mixtur
 e of styles and moods\, including the intimate cabaret sound of With Whom t
 o Dance? In 1999\, the Magnetic Fields released their 3-disc set\, 69 Love 
 Songs. The album has sold 130\,000 copies worldwide\, and has brought Merri
 tt's music to the mainstream eye. In addition to Merritt's singing\, 69 Lov
 e Songs also features vocals by pianist Claudia Gonson\, as well as three a
 dditional singers\, LD Beghtol\, Dudley Klute\, and Shirley Simms. The albu
 m also included instrumental contributions of Future Bible Hero Chris Ewen\
 , and novelist Daniel Handler on accordion.\n\nIn 2002\, The Magnetic Field
 s signed a worldwide record deal with Nonesuch (Warner Brothers). Their fir
 st album for the label\, i\, was released in May\, 2004\, which was followe
 d by Distortion in 2008. We are certainly looking forward to this concert a
 nd we hope you will join us in the upcoming months as we welcome Los Lobos\
 , Aaron Neville\, Malcolm Dalglish\, Canadian Brass and local favorite Carr
 ie Newcomer.
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T050805Z
LOCATION:The Buskirk-Chumley
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:The Magnetic Fields
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
