CREATED:20190322T141908Z
DESCRIPTION:<br><span>From FB:<br><br>Hopscotch Coffee is pleased to presen
 t the final Bloomington edition of Putty Live Art Talk Show at our B-Line c
 afe on Saturday\, March 23 for an evening of televised cultural enlightenme
 nt. All are invited to be part of the studio audience for this unique spect
 acle as Putty illuminates the motivations and methods of the Bloomington cr
 eative community. In the last show in a 3-show series\, host Erin K Drew wi
 ll welcome video artist <a href="https://www.facebook.com/sarah.lasley" tar
 get="_blank"><font color="#0066cc">Sarah Lasley</font></a>\, designer <a hr
 ef="https://www.facebook.com/aaron.denton" target="_blank"><font color="#00
 66cc">Aaron Denton</font></a>\, and comedian <a href="https://www.facebook.
 com/jon.hancuff" target="_blank"><font color="#0066cc">Jon Hancuff</font></
 a>.<br><br>Putty is the brainchild of Indianapolis artist (and former Bloom
 ington resident) Erin K Drew\, an illustrator and art educator. The program
  is hosted by Drew in a late-night talk show format\, replete with musical 
 guest. The focus of the show is arts and culture\, with guests from a varie
 ty of media and backgrounds coming to talk about their work and processes. 
 <br><br>Putty is part documentary project\, part party—a playhouse and publ
 ic art piece which appropriates and distorts the talk show format. Original
 ly presented at Indy’s State Street Pub\, Putty at Hopscotch aspires to str
 ike a balance between entertainment and education\, in an environment natur
 ally attuned to studying and socializing—a lecture hall with zero credit ho
 urs but way better furniture. Over the course of three episodes\, host Erin
  K Drew will conduct long-form interviews with some of the emerging talents
  and creative magnates who have helped make Bloomington a luminary destinat
 ion for DIY culture for the last two decades of her life. <br><br><a href="
 http://sarahlasley.com/?fbclid=IwAR2kiNDKgvv2a8bDCyVq8-ntukw_raVJXeUEvYjLMR
 nzG9x1rugXJPcVdw8" target="_blank" rel="nofollow" data-lynx-uri="http://l.f
