BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Let's Go! Bloomington
DTSTART:20101023T000000Z
DTEND:20101023T020000Z
DTSTAMP:20260905T041548Z
UID:e147838888593807@facebook.com
URL:http://www.facebook.com/event.php?eid=147838888593807
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20101018T131338Z
DESCRIPTION:The Fuller Projects is pleased to announce Visual Overload by t
 he Indiana University Graduate Painting Students. This exhibition will be h
 eld Friday\, October 22\, 2010 from 8:00 pm to 10:00 pm. All events are fre
 e and open to the public.\n \nVisual Overload is a physical translation of 
 the term through the use of painting\, collage or installation. Each painte
 r presents their impression of contemporary visual culture. In addition to 
 finished works\, we’re presented with a physical trail of resources and inf
 luences that aided the artist in their process. We’re given a glimpse into 
 the painter’s train of thought without having to step into their studio.\n 
 \nThe artists in this exhibition are currently MFA painting candidates at I
 ndiana University Bloomington. Ben Cowan received his BFA in Painting from 
 the School of the Art Institute of Chicago and has shown in IL and MI. Dyla
 n Critchfield-Sales received his BFA in Painting from the Maryland Institut
 e College of Art and has shown in PA and MD. Erin Goedtel received her BFA 
 in Painting from the University of Wisconsin-Stout and has shown in CA\, WI
  and MN.Anders Johnson received his BA from North Park University in Chicag
 o and has shown in IL\, NY and Italy. David Maddy received his BA from the 
 Maryland Institute College of Art and has shown in NY\, MD and MI. Rachel W
 olfson received her BFA in Painting from the Maryland Institute College of 
 Art and has shown in MD\, Japan and Italy.\n \nThe Fuller Projects is a ven
 ue with the primary mission of providing emerging contemporary artists with
  the opportunity to propose\, create and present new work. Established in 2
 002 by Indiana University School of Fine Arts students\, The Fuller Project
 s encourages dialogue on art within the university\, the community of Bloom
 ington\, IN and beyond.\n \nThe Fuller Projects would like to thank the SoF
 A Gallery for their guidance and support.\n\nhttp://www.facebook.com/event.
 php?eid=147838888593807
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T050712Z
LOCATION:The Fuller Projects\, 525 E 9th St. (Corner of 10th and Indiana)\,
  Bloomington\, IN
SEQUENCE:21
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Visual Overload
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
