DESCRIPTION:In 1965 Norman Morrison\, a Quaker from Baltimore\, drove to th
 e Pentagon and\, in protest over the U.S. policy in Vietnam\, doused himsel
 f in kerosene and lit himself on fire. In his arms as he did this\, was his
  one-year-old daughter (who survived.) Forty years later a new father\, hau
 nted by Morrison’s act\, asks why. 
