DESCRIPTION:Join the Brown Sisters and Tim Reed for two concerts on Saturda
 y\, January 10th at 8 pm and Sunday\, January 11th at 2 pm.\n\nThe Brown Si
 sters include Lauren (20)\, Lilly (17) and Jenna (14). They have been singi
 ng around Bloomington for many years. They sing all styles of music includi
 ng folk\, jazz\, pop\, country\, gospel\, show tunes\, and even opera. They
  enjoy performing acappella\, but have performed with full orchestras and b
 ig bands. They are savvy pianist and songwriters\, and now have added guita
 r and drums to their toolbox. They have performed with the Bloomington Symp
 hony Orchestra and the Bloomington POPs\, and have performed their own conc
 erts at the Buskirk-Chumley Theater.\n\nTim is a pianist\, vocalist\, actor
 \, piano and voice teacher\, and composer. He also owns Home Shop Teams\, a
  home shopping business that has grown into 5 Midwestern states. As a singe
 r and actor he has performed over 60 roles in the U.S. and Europe. As a com
 poser he has written piano pieces and songs\, and accordion music for Ann R
 andolph's one-woman show Squeeze Box\, which has played throughout the US\,
  and in Edinburgh\, Scotland\, and ran for 3 months on Off-Broadway in 2005
 . Lauren and Lilly are his piano students\, and he and Lauren are now writi
 ng partners. All three girls will be performing his compostions for this sh
 ow. He feels blessed and fortunate to be collaborating with the Brown famil
 y! \n\nTickets will be $10 general admission or $5 for kids 12 and under.  
 Tickets will be available at www.bloomingtonarts.info by Wednesday\, Septem
 ber 17th.
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T051743Z
LOCATION:The Waldron Auditorium
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:The Brown Sisters and Tim Reed
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
