CREATED:20090218T051755Z
DESCRIPTION:“4 cell” is an exhibition of new work by artist\, writer\, and 
 sound maker Jeremy Kennedy. As the title may imply\, this show playfully ex
 plores cell phone culture. Kennedy is no stranger to exhibiting work in Blo
 omington\, but this event profiles recent work which steps away from his no
 rmal output. The focal point of “4 cell” is a series of sculptural pieces w
 hich utilize cellular phones as both the subject and the medium.\n\nCell ph
 ones\, the place they hold in today’s culture\, and the lexicon specific to
  them have been favorite and reoccurring themes of the artist in question. 
 In the past Kennedy has brought these ideas on the subject to life on canva
 s. With two cell phone related series: “the patron saint of cell phone towe
 rs” (2004)\, “the queen of cell phone towers” (2003-2007)\, and a multitude
  of non series paintings\, he has never let go of this obsession. This coll
 ection\, however\, has finally allowed him the opportunity to work hands on
  with actual phones.\n\nMost of the phones have been physically altered thr
 ough a variety of processes. Others are shown in settings reflective of acc
 epted and absurd accident scenarios and humorous misconstruing of cell phon
 e terminology. The methods used to effectively “alter” the phones reads lik
 e a list of murderous techniques: shot\, smashed\, drowned\, run over by ca
 r\, and other types of carefully planned destruction.\n\nAside from answeri
 ng age old questions such as: “what happens when you microwave your phone?”
 \, this event will also transform the fuller projects space into an immersi
 ve environment of the cell phone persuasion. An exciting mix of elements re
 ferencing cell phone stores\, accident sites\, and science fairs will help 
 set the tone for the happening. To round things out\, Kennedy has also desi
 gned a cellular soundtrack for the evening.\n\nWhether you love cell phones
  or find them to be one of the more irritating advents of our time\, you’ll
  find some pleasure in this exhibition.\n\n-Tyco Riley (2009)\n\nwww.kneesh
 y.com\nwww.jinjonjim.com\ntaserfactory.blogspot.com
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T051127Z
LOCATION:the mccalla building (10th + indiana)
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Art Opening: "4 cell"
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
