DESCRIPTION:Matt & Shannon Heaton play traditional and updated Irish music.
  They have straight-ahead Irish music backgrounds and also bring in persona
 l\, American-tinged touches to their music. Call it Irish Americana\, or mo
 dern Celtic music\, Matt and Shannon’s shows feature stunning musicianship\
 , an easy rapport with audiences\, and a selection of music you won’t hear 
 anywhere else.\n\n“Irish music with a wonderfully rich and earthy sound—bri
 ght\, uplifting music that will make you smile.” –Tom Nelligan\, Dirty Line
 n\n\nMatt met Shannon when she was an undergrad at Northwestern University.
  She needed a guitar player for a friend’s wedding: she’d gotten three name
 s of grad students from the guitar teacher at the University. Matt was seco
 nd on the list\, but the first guy wasn’t home when Shannon called him.\n\n
 Though Shannon had a travelling background (she had lived in Thailand\, Nig
 eria\, throughout the Midwest\, and in American Indian reservations in the 
 Southwestern US) while Matt had grown up in Pittsburgh\, they both develope
 d a love for Irish traditional music—and each other. They began learning tu
 nes on the North side of the city with the support of mentors like John Wil
 liams\, Liz Carroll and Jimmy Keane.\n\nMatt and Shannon began blending tim
 eless traditional tunes and ballads with originals (combining Matt’s guitar
  and eventually bouzouki and harmony singing with Shannon’s passionate voca
 ls\, and her stunning Irish flute and whistle playing). They wanted to be r
 espectful of the tradition\, while being authentic about their own American
  music backgrounds. One fan called them Planxty-meets-Natalie-Merchant-meet
 s-Richard-Thompson.\n\n“Their playing is masterful and inventive\, their ar
 rangements city-smart and spacious.” —Scott Alarik\, Boston Globe\n\nIn lat
 e 1998 they moved to Boulder\, Colorado where they developed the band Siucr
 a with Beth Leachman\, which they had started in Chicago with singer Kat Eg
 gleston and fiddler Andrew Bird. In 2001 they moved to Boston and began wor
 king with Robbie O’Connell\, Aoife Clancy\, Childsplay\, and many others. M
 att did a few tours with Emily Smith and The Boys of the Lough. Shannon\, w
 ith fiddler/singer Laura Cortese\, founded BCMFest\, Boston’s Celtic Music 
 Fest.\n\nThe Heatons make traditional music accessible with fresh\, invigor
 ating material and a warm rapport with their audiences. Their music reflect
 s a strong devotion to traditional Irish music\, a passion for reaching out
  to the modern world around them\, and a deep respect and sweet affection f
 or each other. They uplift their audiences\, connecting with each other and
  their listeners.\n\n“Tight\, sweet\, and tasteful\, lacking nothing on eit
 her technical expertise or instrumental virtuosity.” —John O’Regan\, Irish 
 Music Magazine\n\n“If Matt’s solid guitar playing is the rock\, Shannon’s v
 oice is the sun: remarkably light yet powerful.” —Molly Snyder Edler\, OnMi
 lwaukee.com\nwww.MattandShannonHeaton.com Shannon@MattandShannonHeaton.com\
 n\nDISCOGRAPHY\nThe Heatons have released a number of fine albums. Of their
  debut disc\, “Dearga\,” (October 2003)\, Irish Music Magazine’s John O’Reg
 an noted\, “Song wise they hint at an older domestic sound\, the familiar d
 own home harmonies of The Carter Family and Tim and Mollie O’Brien.”\n\nThe
  Heatons included more Irish-inspired originals on their 2006 and 2007 foll
 ow ups\, “Blue Skies Above” and “Fine Winter’s Night.” Kerry Dexter’s revie
 w in Dirty Linen noted\, “The pair’s talents are grounded as much in Americ
 an folk as in the Celtic world… well balanced with songs and tunes in Irish
  and Americana styles and fresh\, creative musicianship.”\n\nMatt and Shann
 on’s Valentine’s Day release\, “Lover’s Well” (2009) is a collection of son
 gs for lovers\, and love-themed tunes for dancers. All of the songs on the 
 album have themes of love and romance\, and all of tunes on the album have 
 been assembled with dancers in mind (since dancing together is as sweet as 
 singing together).\n\nTICKETS:\n$10\n$7 (Students w/valid ID)\nChildren und
 er 12 - FREE\n\nhttp://www.MattandShannonHeaton.com Shannon@MattandShannonH
 eaton.com
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T051239Z
LOCATION:Rachael's Cafe
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Matt & Shannon Heaton
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
