DESCRIPTION:The Bishop presents:\n\nJOOKABOX (Asthmatic Kitty Records)\nNET
 TLES (members of Resting Rooster)\n@ The Bishop\nSaturday\, Jan 30\n11pm\n2
 1+\n$5\n\nJOOKABOX\nhttp://www.myspace.com/jookabox\n"The bone-on-bone drum
 beat that opens Dead Zone Boys pounds the sound of living death\, creeping 
 forward\, maw open wide. The beat is serving notice: you are about to be co
 nsumed.\nDead Zone Boys\, the third album from Jookabox (Indianapolis-born 
 David "Moose" Adamson and Co.)\, is love story meets psychedelic zombie-mus
 ical. The zombie part came easy: Moose grew up on the east side of Indianap
 olis in the 90s\, an area plagued by constant recession\, pandemic homicide
 \, and racial tension. A few strong tribes chose to stay in the area despit
 e constant warnings from fleeing acquaintances. It was this frantic energy 
 and violence that infused itself into the Jookabox experience. Since then\,
  the area struggles to revitalize and Adamson’s musical interests and excur
 sions have crystallized into a startlingly singular and eclectic songwritin
 g strategy. One thing is certain here: if vacant strip malls occupied only 
 by shitdragged liquor stores and fluorescent check cashing joints are forei
 gn to you\, then Dead Zone Boys will be your guidebook\, Jookabox your tour
  guide. This is more evident now than ever on what is sure to become a cult
  classic."\n(http://asthmatickitty.com/jookabox)\n\nNETTLES (members of Res
 ting Rooster)\nhttp://www.myspace.com/restingrooster\n\nhttp://www.thebisho
 pbar.com\nhttp://www.myspace.com/thebishopbar
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T051401Z
LOCATION:The Bishop
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Late Show: JOOKABOX (Asthmatic Kitty Records)\, with NETTLES
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
