DESCRIPTION:Holi\, one of the most festive holidays in India will be celebr
 ated at IU on March 25th\, 2011 at Dunn Meadow from 4:00pm – 6:00pm. Holi\,
  the festival of colors is a day to dance\, eat lots of delicious food\, an
 d throw colored powder to symbolize the coming of spring and bringing good 
 harvests. Holi typically falls on the day after the first full moon in the 
 month of march and is a day full of laughter and fun! For more questions pl
 ease contactacc@indiana.edu.  We invite to a free event to enjoy ethnic cui
 sine\,  performances\, henna\, and a color fight! So mark your calendars an
 d don't forget to wear something you don't mind getting color on!
