CREATED:20101124T193614Z
DESCRIPTION:\nCommunity Meeting and Info-Night:\nThe Case of Marie Mason\nD
 ecember 2 @ Boxcar Books (408 East 6th Street)\n7 pm\n\nFor years\, Marie M
 ason was a well-known activist and community organizer in\nBloomington.  Ma
 ny of us knew her as a solid\, caring friend\, and a\npassionate advocate f
 or the environment and social justice.  She moved\naway eight years ago to 
 Michigan\, and while there was a prominent\norganizer in the environmental 
 justice campaign against Ice Mountain's\nefforts to privatize and bottle lo
 cal water resources.  In 2008\,\nthough\, she was indicted for acts of\nsab
 otage against logging equipment and a genetic engineering research lab.\n\n
 Marie was arrested at the preschool where she worked and was then\nmoved be
 tween a series of jails and home detention systems.  Under the\nthreat of m
 ultiple life sentences if found guilty at trial\, she\neventually plead\ngu
 ilty and is now serving 22 years in a controversial isolation unit in\nTexa
 s designed specifically for political and Muslim prisoners.\n\nMany of us a
 re left with questions about her time here\, about her case and\nthe wider 
 FBI repression of environmental activists.  Despite her many\nties here\, B
 loomington has never organized systematic support for her\,\neven though sh
 e is now facing the longest prison sentence ever for an\nenvironmentalist.\
 n\nThree members of Marie's support crew in Cincinnati are visiting Thursda
 y\,\nDecember 2nd to help fill us in on her case and charges\, her current\
 nconditions and the broader campaign of repression\, which even targeted he
 r\ntwo children.  It's vital that we do better processing and honoring\nhis
 tories of resistance in Bloomington and supporting people like Marie\nwho c
 ontributed so much here.\n\nPlease forward.\nSponsored by Bloomington Frien
 ds of Marie
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T051228Z
LOCATION:Boxcar Books (408 East 6th Street)
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Community Meeting and Info-Night: The Case of Marie Mason
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
