UID:6esr78vlp7pk8ncub46keiulfs@google.com
CREATED:20081125T152040Z
DESCRIPTION:107 W. 9th\n\n\nCelebrating the most universal subjects known t
 o man\, the BPP presents the sixth annual installment of Sex/Death\, the th
 eatre’s late-night showcase that whimsically walks that fine line between h
 igh art and exploitation. Sex/Death unleashes a scintillating selection of 
 new short plays providing the adventurous theater-goer with a visceral rush
  that would make Alfred Kinsey blush. Sex/Death seeks to answer the questio
 n: "How far can theatre go?" \n\n\n\n \n\nThis year\, the BPP is offering 1
 0 selections weaving tales odd sexual fantasies\, homicide\, infidelity and
 … bird porn?  \n\n \n\n\n\nThanksgiving by Neal Utterback\n\n\nAn internet 
 date turns out to be “tastier” than one man ever bargained for.\n\n\n\nA Pu
 rposeful Life by Greg Ellis\n\n\nSWF seeks SM for leap into the great beyon
 d.\n\n \n\n\n\nThursday Routine by Rebecca Martin\n\n\nA married couple bat
 tle the doldrums of marriage using their wild imaginations.\n\n \n\n\n\nThe
  Becker Potential by Paul Kubin\n\n\nA Private Dick realizes what happens a
 t The Push/Pull Tavern stays at the Push/Pull Tavern.\n\n\n\nStreet Corner 
 by Mark Kingsbury\n\n\nA young woman finds it much harder to lose her virgi
 nity than she would have thought. Especially considering\, she’s standing o
 n the corner of Indiana and Kirkwood.\n\n\n\n \n\n100% Distracted by Joni M
 cGary\n\n\nA visit from the plumber has him fixing more than just that leak
 y faucet.\n\n \n\n\n\nThe Cock Robin Porn Shop by Janis Butler Holm\n\n\nFi
 nd out the favorite porn titles of the average “Jay”.\n\n \n\n\n\nDifferent
  Creatures by Dan Frey\n\n\nSex for the first time with a new lover sometim
 es exposes more than just their flesh.\n\n\n\nNaked In The Play by Nick Moo
 re\n\n\nLife imitates Art when a playwright writes roles for him and his ex
 -girlfriend\, just so he can see her naked again.\n\n \n\n\n\nLa Petite Mor
 t by Bethany Barber\n\n\nWhat happens when the sex is so good\, it almost k
 ills you?\n\n\n\n \n\nSex/Death is produced by BPP Artistic Director Richar
 d Perez and directed by BPP Ensemble Members Holly Holbrook and Jim Hettmer
 . \n\n\n\n \n\n“Sex/Death has become a very popular production for our thea
 tre.  This year we’ve made a concerted effort to continue to improve its pr
 oduction values\,“ explains Mr. Perez. “In order to keep the ticket price l
 ow\, we’ve added more performances.  We hope you enjoy this new and improve
 d showcase.”\n\n \n\n\n\nPerformances of Sex/Death are December 9 – 13 and 
 15 – 17 @ 10pm at the BPP (107 W. 9th).  Tickets are only $5\, available at
  the door the night of the event.  For more information\, call 334-1188 or 
 email bppwrite@newplays.org. \n\n\n\n \n\nSex/Death is presented as part of
  the BPP’s Dark Alley Series.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T050917Z
LOCATION:Bloomington Playwrights Project
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:SEX/DEATH - 6th annual BPP late-night short play showcase 
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
