DESCRIPTION:The Bishop presents:\n\nGrooms\nHard Candy Hearts\nThe Rolling 
 Blackouts\n@ The Bishop\nMonday Nov 16\n9pm\n$4\n\n18+\n\nGrooms\nhttp://ww
 w.myspace.com/groomsmusic\n"Grooms\, however\, have chosen to bring into th
 e future the foundational indie sounds that were arguably developed as a di
 rect protest against the nihilism\, hyper-individualism\, and hyper-consume
 rism of 80s pop culture. It was the latter that early indie bands like Blac
 k Flag and Sonic Youth detested\, for they knew that its apparent harmlessn
 ess was merely a cloak for political conservatism. These are the giants’ sh
 oulders that Grooms have chosen to stand upon\, and with Rejoicer they have
  done so excellently."\n\nHard Candy Hearts\nhttp://www.myspace.com/hardcan
 dyhearts\n"They would always keep coming up with something to be annoyed or
  excited about\, whether it was smashing vinyl in-between songs\, throwing 
 candy and firecrackers at the audience or shows ending in violence. You wou
 ld always see something that you wouldn’t forget"\n\nThe Rolling Blackouts\
 nhttp://www.myspace.com/therollingblackoutssuck\nThe Rolling Blackouts are 
 a new band on the block\, featuring members of Metal in the Microwave\, Hot
  Mess\, and other beloved and/or notorious and/or infamous and/or well-resp
 ected and/or under-appreciated Bloomington bands.\n\n\nhttp://www.myspace.c
 om/thebishopbar
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T051159Z
LOCATION:The Bishop
SEQUENCE:4
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Grooms\, Hard Candy Hearts\, Rolling Black Outs
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
