DESCRIPTION:The Midwest Pages to Prisoners Project is having a BOOK SALE!\n
 \nWe are an all volunteer effort that strives to encourage self-education a
 mong prisoners in the United States. By providing free reading materials up
 on request\, we hope to aid in the rehabilitation process and stimulate cri
 tical thinking behind bars.\n\nDue to limited space\, overstock in particul
 ar genres\, and the specific restrictions of state and federal prisons\, we
  have books we cannot store\, cannot immediately use\, and/or cannot send t
 o prisoners.\n\n9am - 12pm : $1 for hardbacks\, 50c for paperbacks.\n12pm -
  3pm : $3 per bag (common grocery paper-bag)\n\nAll proceeds go directly to
 ward restocking frequently requested genres and topics\, as well as general
  packing and letter writing materials.\n\nTables will be set up in the park
 ing lot in front our our office at\n118 S. Rogers St.\, Suite 2 (Cnr. 4th &
  Rogers)\n
