DESCRIPTION:Searle Slutzkin\, an Indiana University student in the Leadersh
 ip\, Ethics\, and Social Action (LESA) Capstone Seminar\, will be holding a
 n art showing\, featuring art created exclusively by prisoners\, to benefit
  the Midwest Pages to Prisoners Project (MWPP).\n\nThe MWPP was founded in 
 1995\, in Bloomington\, Indiana\, and is completely volunteer run. The proj
 ect “strives to encourage self-education among prisoners in the United Stat
 es. By providing free reading materials upon request\, [they] hope to aid i
 n the rehabilitation process and stimulate critical thinking behind bars.” 
 Additionally\, “the project exists to alleviate pain\, boredom\, and attrit
 ion and to provide a direct opportunity for self-education\,” because “pris
 oners are not strangers: they are brothers\, sisters\, friends\, cousins\, 
 mothers\, and children.” Furthermore\, the project serves prisoners in sixt
 een states\, and relies completely on donations and fundraisers.\n\nThe mai
 n goal of the art showing will be to raise awareness about the issues revol
 ving around incarceration\, as well as to highlight the work of the MWPP. \
 n\nAdmission to the event will be free\, but since it is in support of the 
 MWPP\, we would really appreciate monetary donations or book donations (use
 d or new)! These will help the organization continue to do the great work t
 hat it does!\n\nIt will be really awesome and we hope to see you there! For
  more information\, please visit www.pagestoprisoners.org or feel free to c
 ontact Searle Slutzkin at seaslutz@indiana.edu or at prisonersonpaper@gmail
 .com.\n\nPLEASE FORWARD THIS ON TO ALL OF YOUR FRIENDS AND COLLEAGUES! Than
 k you :)\n\n** WHILE THE EVENT STARTS AT 7PM\, PLEASE NOTE THAT WE WILL HAV
 E VARIOUS SPEAKERS COMMENCE AT 8PM - NAMES TO BE ANNOUNCED SOON ** \n\nhttp
 ://www.facebook.com/event.php?eid=114684378571610
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T051338Z
LOCATION:Space 101/The Lodge (above Subway on the Square)\, 101 E. 6th Stre
 et\, Bloomington\, IN
SEQUENCE:12531580
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Prisoners on Paper: An Art Showing
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
