CREATED:20100427T172348Z
DESCRIPTION:The Bishop Presents:\n\nWhippoorwill\nThe Hollows\nThrowing Sta
 rs\n\n@ the Bishop\nSaturday\, May 1\n9pm\n18+\n$4\n\n*****\n\nRising from 
 the ashes of The Decanters\, Whippoorwill took flight in 2004. Frontwoman N
 icole Evans Groth and keyboardist/trumpeter/saw player Mikey Kapinus joined
  forces with Jason Evans Groth on guitar and vocals\, Alex Mann on bass and
  Jonathan Cargill on drums. Jason and Mikey also played together in Magnoli
 a Electric Co.\, and everyone except Jason was a member of the popular Prin
 ce cover band\, Erotic City. Jason was also in The Coke Dares and The Impos
 sible Shapes. After a couple of years\, the band realized the only thing mi
 ssing from their sweet sound was some face-meltin' dual-lead guitar harmoni
 es\, so they recruited Chris Welz on guitar (who had also been in Erotic Ci
 ty as well as Frank Lloyd Wrong).\n\nNow the 6-piece hums along like a '69 
 Corvette with the windows rolled down\, blasting Loretta Lynn and Lee Hazel
 wood\, with a little T. Rex\, Neil Young & Willie Nelson thrown in for good
  measure. Banjos and harmonies\, rock with a little country\, beautiful fem
 ale vocals with a little growl\, growling male vocals with a bit of beauty.
 .. goes well with a generous dram of your favorite whiskey.\n\n*****\n\nThe
  Hollows formed in 2005 when neo-country songstress Kate Long and upright b
 assist Alex Mann started playing together. Known only as "Kate and Alex" fo
 r the first few months\, the duo played various venues in Bloomington and g
 ained a reputation for delivering sparse\, winsome arrangements that deftly
  supported Kate's compelling songwriting and arresting vocals.\n\nShortly a
 fter the name was adopted\, Evan Farrell joined the group as a 3rd member o
 n guitar\, lap steel and comic relief. Evan's musical stature was already m
 onstrous: apart from honkytonkin' in Grande Rouge (with Kate)\, he had been
  a member of The Japonize Elephants\, Magnolia Electric Co. and the popular
  indie rock group Rogue Wave. As a trio\, The Hollows continued to play all
  around Bloomington\, and recorded an album at Dan Burton's Home Grotto Stu
 dio.\n\nAfter losing Evan to a house fire in Oakland\, CA in December of 20
 07\, Kate and Alex stayed away from the stage except for a couple of perfor
 mances\, until late 2009 when The Hollows re-grouped with new members Brad 
 Baute on guitar\, lap steel\, fiddle and banjo and Pete Schreiner on drums.
  Brad had played in Grande Rouge with Kate and Evan as well as The Fatted C
 alf String Band with Alex\; and Pete has built a reputation in Bloomington 
 as one of the hardest-working multi-instrumentalists on the scene for well 
 over a decade\, playing in groups like Intro to Airlift\, Panoply Academy\,
  Turn Pale\, Magnolia Electric Co.\, Thousand Arrows and Old Flames.\n\nThe
  quartet has been hard at work over the past few months\, learning new song
 s and polishing up old ones. A solid live show schedule and new recording s
 essions are all on deck\, and The Hollows' understated\, riveting\, country
 -tinged reverberations have never sounded better.\n\n*******\n\nThrowing St
 ars have two sides to their personality basically. They are half nerd/geek\
 , and half rock n' roller. The nerd side of them stems from their love of r
 eading. Throwing Stars are a big time fan of greek philosophy and Aristotle
 . They are also objectivist epistemologist theorists (hehe bet most of you 
 don't know what that is). They are huge fans of the late Ayn Rand. On the f
 lip side Throwing Stars loves classic rock music\, motorcycles\, muscle car
 s\, hot rods\, martial arts\, extreme sports\, magic\, gold\, sports\, work
 ing dogs (dobermann pinschers)\, and anything else exciting. So basically t
 hey have a wide range of interests which allows them to relate to a wide ra
 nge of people. They are as comfortable talking to an outlaw motorcycle club
  member as they are talking to a quantum physics expert or ballerina. To th
 em\, that's what makes life so interesting and entertaining! 
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T051414Z
LOCATION:The Bishop
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Whippoorwill\, The Hollows\, and Throwing Stars
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
