DESCRIPTION:Middle Way House Childcare (Rise and Shine Daycare) needs your 
 help!! We've recently had a budget crunch and need to raise money to contin
 ue to serve our clients as well as we have always done.\n\n**IF YOU ARE NOT
  IN BLOOMINGTON YOU CAN STILL HELP!!**\n\nThere are three ways to help::\n\
 n1. Be a knitter.\n2. Be a sponsor.\n3. Sell your crafts at a silent auctio
 n held at Rhino's on January 31st {this comes a long with free brunch and f
 un:)}\nAny combination of these options would also be great!!\n\nHere's how
  it works::\n1. Be a knitter\nKnit scarves. On your own time\, whenever you
  have free time\, partner up with someone else you know is doing this and h
 ave knitting parties\, etc. Basically knit your socks off for the entire mo
 nth of January. Collect sponsors. Just like any other "A-Thon" event\, they
 'll donate for each milestone you work through. For this event we're sugges
 ting a nickel/dime per square inch of scarf (that's generally about $4.50 p
 er scarf knitted) and then sell your scarves at our silent auction at the e
 vent at Rhino's on January 31st.\n\n2. Be a sponsor\nFind someone who's kni
 tting and donate $0.05 per square inch of scarf. Donate a flat rate. Show u
 p at the end event at Rhino's and show your support.\n\n3. Sell your crafts
  at the silent auction\nPaint\, make textile crafts\, beaded jewelry\, etc.
  and donate these things to the cause. It's a great way to show your suppor
 t and get your art out into the public eye.\n\nAll proceeds go to benefit M
 iddle Way House Childcare at the Rise!\n\nGet with Elisabeth Squires (via F
 acebook or at Elisabeth.squires@gmail.com )\nOR\nStephanie L. Talarek (via 
 Facebook or at stalarek@indiana.edu)\nfor any questions about this event an
 d/or to be put on the list of participants to see the next step :)
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T051726Z
SEQUENCE:2
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:MWH Childcare Knit-a-thon!
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
