DESCRIPTION:The BPP presents the '09 Ballot Box Blizzard\, an evening of 30
  ultra-short plays about POLITICS in two hours. The Blizzard is short-atten
 tion span theatre at a breakneck pace. Hey\, if you don’t like one\, it’s a
 lready over!\n\nThe Blizzard is produced as part of ArtsWeek 2009. This yea
 r’s event will feature mini-masterpieces that explore politics on and beyon
 d the campaign trail. The plays tackle the politics of the office\, the sch
 ool and even the family\, proving that politics is a part of our everyday l
 ife\, whether we know it or not.\n\nThe ’09 Ballot Box Blizzard features th
 e work of 23 playwrights from around the state of Indiana. Twenty actors ha
 ve divided into three teams\, each under the guidance of a different direct
 or: April Smallwood\, Jim Hettmer & Jack Johnson. The plays\, as usual\, ru
 n the entire stylistic gamut: from noir drama to absurdist comedy and beyon
 d.\n\nThis year’s plays are:\n\nBedford by Greg Owens\nClick On It by April
  Smallwood\nThe Bumbling Bodyguard by Adam Schwartz\nStereotypical by Bradl
 ey Good\nHome of the Brave by Terri Klingelhoefer\nDouble Standards (Pts. 1
  & 2) by Bethany Barber\nElevator Politics by Adam Schwartz\nAn Election in
  the Cards by Phillip Addison\nThe Pants Party by Bradley Good\nDo It Right
  by April Smallwood\nJack Burkhead Is A Dickhead by Nick Moore\nThe Tragedy
  of McCain by Greg Ellis\nModern Dating by Alex Straiker\nHome Schooled by 
 Angeline Larimer\nBraerm by Scoti Pelnin\nA Choice to Make by Joni McGary\n
 The Conquest of Guernica by Evan Guilford-Blake\nThe Candidate by Mark Harv
 ey Levine\nFace(book) Off by Rachael Himsel\nThe Speech by Jim Poyser\nThe 
 17th District by Phillip Addison\nMan Law by Kaylee Spivey\nI Think I Love 
 Him by Steven Cole Hughes\nExit Poll by Jim Poyser\nChris and Jenny's Cross
 -Curtain Relationship by Devin Blankenship\nThe Takeover by Rachael Himsel\
 nSwirls by Mark Kingsbury\nEnlightenment by Tammy Dennis-Good\nAni Conquers
  the Martians by Derrick Krober\n\nAudience members are invited to particip
 ate by voting for the best plays\, and encouraged to buy additional votes f
 or $1 each and “stuff the ballot box” for their favorite. All proceeds will
  go to support the Bloomington Playwrights Project.\n\nThe ’09 Ballot Box B
 lizzard is produced by Holly Holbrook and Erin Sullivan.\n\nPerformances ar
 e February 19 – 21 & 26 – 28 @ 8pm and 22 @ 2pm. Tickets are $8 and availab
 le at the Sunrise Box Office or online at www.bloomingtonarts.info. Call 33
 4-1188 or email bppwrite@newplays.org for more information.
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T051108Z
LOCATION:Bloomington Playwrights Project
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Play: Ballot Box Blizzard
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
