CREATED:20081120T211557Z
DESCRIPTION:Boduf Songs (Southampton\, UK - Kranky Records) - http://bodufs
 ongs.com/\n"Hauntingly beautiful music that is oft mistakenly labeled "folk
 ." This is something darker\, something much more sinister\, and Mat Sweet'
 s songwriting muse dives into the troubled waters of a tormented soul and t
 he mysterious forests of the mind. This is the best record of the year\, pe
 riod." Mundane Sounds\n<br><br>\n"The spare use of his blurry instrumentati
 on is the secret ingredient to the horror in these songs. Sweet packs a pun
 ch for such a quiet fellow\, and his vortex is indeed a powerful one." Tiny
  Mix Tapes\n<Br><br>\n"Boduf Songs makes some of the duskiest\, autumnal\, 
 and beautiful loner psychedelia. On his second full-length he sticks to his
  stripped-down approach (one bedroom at night + a microphone\, acoustic gui
 tar\, field recordings\, and occasional percussion\, bass\, etc.\, accents)
 \, creating another collection of minimal\, deeply resonant compositions." 
 - Stereogum\n\n<br><Br>\nApache Dropout (Bton)\nGone are the days of broke 
 ass outfits of Hoosier weird-ohs spilling out twisted records and traveling
  the lands sharing our garbled back woods esoteric sounds. In times of cris
 is its basic human nature to search for a guiding light. Just this season\,
  we've seen our town\, state\, and country find Obama as their savior. Fill
 ed with frustration and nowhere to turn\, I'm looking at Apache Dropout to 
 be the active ingredient necessary to lead the local music scene to recover
 y. This desolute bunch has the "fuck your way" swagger to their sounds and 
 actions. Plenty of distortion and fuzz in these paranoid spine-tingling ant
 hems. Like all the truly adventerous\, Apache Dropout has an "out of its ti
 me" sound. We could mention the Velvet Underground or Television... however
  the Dropout provides a more dangerous vibration. Don't get too close - thi
 s unstable elixir is likely to implode at any time. Not unlike Canadian pro
 to-punk space pioneers Simply Saucer...or the Texan Lysergic fueled spiritu
 al madness of the 13th Floor Elevators... maybe even perhaps the absolutely
  deranged NY drop-outs the Fugs.\n- Lord Fyre (Magnetic South)\n<br><br>\n\
 nWhen We Might (Bton) - http://www.myspace.com/whenwemight\nThe life long p
 roject of When We Might began in a cramped built on room in the back of a g
 arage. Slowly building confidence a group of friends joined him to give the
  songs more texture and the experience could not have been any better. With
  a new group of musical players since his move to Bloomington ranging from 
 collegiate music students to gnarly punks and even the likes of shoegazing 
 ambient experimentalist folkies\, this is something to look forward too.
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T051132Z
LOCATION:The Cinemat
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Boduf Songs / Apache Dropout / When We Might
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
