DESCRIPTION:$15 General Admission\n<br><br>\nIf you have listened to The Mo
 ldy Peaches or to any of Kimya Dawson's first three solo albums (i'm sorry 
 that sometimes i'm mean (2002)\, knock-knock who?(2004)\, and my cute fiend
  sweet princess(2004)) you will be familiar with her beautiful use of casse
 tte four track to achieve an intimate sense of solitude. These home recordi
 ngs make it feel as though you have a friend there with you whispering in y
 our ear. And you do. Kimya is your friend.\n<br><Br>\nDawson became well kn
 own as the female counterpart to Adam Green in the band The Moldy Peaches. 
 Since the Moldy Peaches went on hiatus in 2004 Dawson has released a string
  of lo-fi homemade albums and toured widely in North America and Europe.\n<
 Br><br>\nDawson recently finished work on Alphabutt\, a new album of childr
 en's music that was released September 9\, 2008. Song titles include "The A
 lphabutt Song\," "Seven Hungry Tigers\," "Little Monster Babies\," "Wiggle 
 My Tooth" and "Pee Pee in the Potty\," and collaborators include former Thi
 rd Eye Blind guitarist Kevin Cadogan and a number of Dawson's other musical
  friends and their children. She has also been invited to participate in th
 e Sesame Street television program.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T051423Z
LOCATION:Buskirk-Chumley
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Kimya Dawson\, Matty Pop Chart\, & Erin Tobey
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
