UID:vol28il02fjig2ui8n4njori2c@google.com
CREATED:20100930T141200Z
DESCRIPTION:FREE ADMISSION\, which includes film screening\, pizza\, DQ ice
  cream cake\, refreshments\, and great conversation.\n \nDescription:\nOut 
 in the Silence is a documentary by Joe Wilson and Dean Hamer.  The film beg
 ins with the announcement in Joe Wilson’s hometown newspaper of his wedding
  to another man.  This simple event ignites a firestorm of controversy and 
 a quest for change in the small Pennsylvania hometown he left long ago.  Dr
 awn back by a plea for help from the mother of a gay teen being tormented a
 t school\, Wilson takes viewers on an exhilarating journey through love\, h
 ate\, and understanding in rural America.\nThis event is meant to stir comm
 unity dialogue about issues relating to acceptance and tolerance of differe
 nces within rural communities.  The community dialogue will be facilitated 
 by Indiana University Professor Mary Gray\, who is the author of the recent
 ly published book Out in the Country.\nWhether you know a gay\, lesbian\, b
 isexual\, or transgendered person or not\, you will find the information pr
 esented at the event to be thought-provoking.  Please join us.
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T050901Z
LOCATION:Spencer Presbyterian Church Cornerstone Hall (154 N. Main Street\,
  Spencer\, IN 47460)  
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Out in the Silence Film Screening\, Dinner\, Dessert\, & Dialogue
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
