DESCRIPTION:Join us in this celebratory spectacle and authentic demonstrati
 on of Brazilian Carnaval dance\, costuming\, people\, music\, and drink.\n\
 nThe much-anticipated\, annual Brazilian Carnaval will feature percussionis
 ts with the best of Samba Enredo and Batucada\, accompanied by 15 dancers i
 n their “barely there” costumes adorned in sequins\, beads and feathers. An
  acrobatic Capoeira and Maculelê show with Axé Capoeira Chicago. An eclecti
 c mix of Afro-Brazilian rhythms PLUS a Brazilian Jiu-Jitsu performance\, re
 al caipirinhas\, a photo booth with photographer Eddy Price\, and face pain
 ting (provided by DBR volunteers).\n\n21+\n$5 for the appropriately attired
  (masks\, feathers\, costumes etc...)\n$7 for the uninspired\n\n**1st 10 pe
 ople in costume get in FREE!!\n\nSponsors:\nBrazilian Association at Indian
 a University\nCenter for Latin American and Caribbean Studies\nAfrican Amer
 ican and African Diaspora Studies\nLa Casa Latino Cultural Center\nCostume 
 Delights\n\nLive Brazilian Music\nAxé Capoeira Chicago (Capoeira Regional a
 nd Maculelê)\n15 Samba dancers showcasing traditional carnaval costumes\nSa
 mba Performance\nBrazilian Jiu-Jitsu presentation\nCaipirinhas (with Cachaç
 a!)\nPhotobooth with photographer Eddy Price
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T051543Z
LOCATION:Bluebird
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Brazilian Carnaval 2009
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
