DESCRIPTION:The PRIDE Film Festival would like to invite you to “Steer Quee
 r” and come join us in a cinematic celebration of the gay\, lesbian\, bi-se
 xual and transgendered community in Bloomington\, IN. The 2010 7th Annual P
 RIDE Film Festival is part of the Indiana University GLBT Alumni Associatio
 n’s Homecoming Weekend and sponsored in part by the Bloomington Convention 
 & Visitors Bureau’s “Visit Gay Bloomington” initiative. This year’s theme f
 ocuses on LGBTQ life and energy in rural communities – a true celebration o
 f our Indiana pride!\n\nThis year’s highlights include:\n\nA new and exciti
 ng opportunity for budding area filmmakers to participate in the PRIDE Vide
 o Shoot Out\, creating thematic short films during a week-long production p
 eriod in January\, all having a common line of dialogue and prop. These new
 \, local films will be screened on opening night of the Festival\, Thursday
 \, Jan 28.\n\nA special free screening and community discussion of the film
  “Out in the Silence” by Joe Wilson and Dean Hamer on Saturday afternoon ex
 amining the challenges confronting gay\, lesbian\, bisexual and transgender
  individuals in rural and small town America.\n\nClosing Night Party\, Sat\
 , Jan 30th - Erotic Attire Encouraged – The LGBTQ event of the year\, this 
 extravaganza transforms the Buskirk-Chumley Theater and the street in front
  into a club atmosphere that would make big cities jealous!\n\nDiverse film
  programming\, including an international array of films\, many addressing 
 the issues specific to rural queer life.\n\nA program of the Buskirk-Chumle
 y Theater\, a historic downtown movie palace\, the Festival features over 2
 0 films from around the world – shorts and features\, animation\, documenta
 ries\, comedy\, and drama. Social gatherings and dance parties abound at di
 fferent restaurants and bars nearby\, while other community organizations a
 re involved from start to finish. Founded in 2004\, the PRIDE Film Festival
  is a program of the Buskirk-Chumley Theater\, guided by an all volunteer S
 teering Committee. Dedicated individuals from Indiana University and the Bl
 oomington community work year-round to create a welcoming\, City-wide\, car
 nival atmosphere. For ticket pricing\, schedule and updates\, please visit 
 www.pridefilmfestival.org.
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T051434Z
LOCATION:Buskirk-Chumley Theater
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:PRIDE Film Festival 2010
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
