DESCRIPTION:Admission:  General Admission: $12 - - - V.I.P: $15\n\nJimmie J
 .J Walker\, best known for coining the phrase “Dyn-o-mite!” on “Good Times 
 was named Comedian of the Decade by Time Magazine 1972. Walker currently to
 urs the country 25-30 weeks a year doing his stand-up comedy\, and also per
 forms on late night T.V. and game shows. In his spare time he writes script
 s for T.V. and movies. The Funny Bone: Bloomington is the first and only fu
 ll-time comedy club located in Bloomington\, IN. The club is dedicated to b
 ringing in nationally recognized comedic talent to perform every week.
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T051452Z
LOCATION:The Funny Bone
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Comedy: Jimmie J.J. Walker
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Let's Go! Bloomington
DTSTART:20100515T000000Z
DTEND:20100515T030000Z
DTSTAMP:20260905T041548Z
UID:5bv12sh1b0gjeocnt8v4bhbsks@google.com
CREATED:20100427T175410Z
DESCRIPTION:Featuring:\n\nHumans\nhttp://www.myspace.com/humansaredead\nA t
 hree-piece from Bloomington\, IN\, HUMANS are one part punk-rock fury mixed
  with an ever shifting\, unstable portion of carnival-esque madness. Bizarr
 e on so many fronts\, HUMANS manage to seamlessly blend audible spazz-outs 
 with creative instrument interaction and blazing lo-fi vocals...all in a ma
 tter of seconds.\n*Written by: Auris Apothecary\n\nOreo Jones\nhttp://myspa
 ce.com/oreojones\nfollowing the release of The Delicious EP\, the Indianapo
 lis based emcee has garnered a myriad of praise and interest\, including th
 ese words from NUVO.net: "All in all\, The Delicious EP is an impressive co
 llection of rhythmic rhymes and soulful\, vintage sounds. Only 12 days afte
 r their official debut\, the wicked team of “Oreo Jones and the amazin’ 90 
 Lbs” have quickly made a name for themselves. The dynamic duo\, who promise
  to “shake this whole damn town ‘til it wakes the hell up'\, guarantee Indi
 anapolis that this is only the beginning."\n\nFair Fjola\nhttp://www.myspac
 e.com/fairfjola\nQuite literally an Argentine family band with a cast of fr
 iends\, Fair Fjola are living proof that modern Americana is both alive and
  varied. A sound that at times evokes the most laid-back of groovy yesterye
 ar anthems\, it also manages to mix Golden-era rockabilly with dark tales o
 f treachery and indie-pop charm.\n*Written by: Auris Apothecary\n\nLaura K.
  Balke\nhttp://www.myspace.com/laurakbalke\nLaura is slowly but surely brin
 ging her songs out of her bedroom in Indianapolis and in to the world\, inc
 iting responses like this review on artsinirvington.com: "Ms. Balke's perfo
 rmance was simply unassumingly elegant. The songs she was performing from h
 er debut album\, Souvenirs\, seemed to draw everyone into her world\, almos
 t without being aware of it\, songs of mature\, subtle sophistication much 
 belying her young age." Laura will be joined by Zachary Jetter on percussio
 n\, and her Boss loop station.
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T051138Z
LOCATION:The Bishop
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Oreo Jones\, Humans\, Laura K. Balke & Fair Fjola
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
