CREATED:20090706T140137Z
DESCRIPTION:Join us Monday\, July 13th\, behind the store\, for an amazing 
 performance by The Sprockettes - an all female synchronized mini-bike dance
  troupe from Portland\, Oregon. The show starts at 8 p.m.\, for free or don
 ation.\nCheck out the site for more information - http://sprockettes.org\n\
 nCheck them out Tuesday\, July 14th at Bloomington's Tuesday Farmers Market
  at 6pm-- the near west side Bloomingfoods!\n\n\nSponsored by Bikesmiths\, 
 Bleeding Heartland Roller Girls\, Bloomingfoods\, BloomingOUT\, Bloomington
  Community Bike Project\, Fiore Magazine\, Planned Parenthood\, and with he
 lp from the city of Bloomington.\n\nWhat's pink and black\, has two wheels 
 and usually a few scabs? A Sprockette\, that's what. The Sprockettes\, base
 d in Portland Oregon\, are a synchronized dance troupe with a do-it-yoursel
 f work ethic. But instead of traditional dance moves\, their choreography f
 eatures pink and black BMX bicycles in a performance that's part dance and 
 part stunt biking. Join us for a rocking and shocking performance on Monday
  July 13th at 8pm behind Bloomington’s only volunteer powered\, non-profit 
 bookstore and community space- Boxcar Books!\n(Catch them again at Tuesday 
 the 14th at Bloomington’s Farmers Market)\n\nWebsite- http://sprockettes.or
 g/\nMyspace- http://www.myspace.com/sprockettes\nFeatured on NPR- http://ww
 w.npr.org/templates/story/story.php?storyId=5613188\nBikePortland.org Sproc
 kettes Archive- http://bikeportland.org/cats/the-scene/sprockettes/\nDocume
 ntary “Small Movements” by Nickey Robo about The Sprockettes- http://vimeo.
 com/1663322?pg=embed&amp\;sec=1663322\nVideo of The Sprockettes in action- 
 http://agentchaosproductions.blogspot.com/2009/04/paris-hilton-meets-sprock
 ettes.html\n\n\nThe Sprockettes began in the spring of 2004 when a pioneeri
 ng group of ladies decided to put together a performance for the Multnomah 
 County Bike Fair. The crowd response was so positive and we had so much fun
  that we thought it would be rad to stay together and see where it would ta
 ke us.\nSince then\, we’ve performed from San Francisco to Vancouver B.C.\,
  toured in a veggie oil powered bus\, held workshops and skill shares\, rec
 eived national media recognition and inspired international bike dance team
 s.\nThe journey of the Sprockettes has been amazing\, held together by our 
 passion for dancing\, bicycles\, DIY ideology\, and striving to promote a h
 ealthy body image.\nOur members are an eclectic group of women: we are teac
 hers\, artists\, gardeners\, social workers\, musicians\, mothers\, bankers
 \, nannies\, writers and students.\nWe work as a collective choreographing\
 , practicing\, making merchandise and performing. We are constantly evolvin
 g.\n\nSprockette’s Mission Statement\n-The Sprockettes are an all female sy
 nchronized mini-bike dance troupe.\nIn a basic sense it is our mission to e
 ntertain audiences by choreographing dances while using our bikes in our pe
 rformance.\nIn a broader sense\, it is our mission to:\n-Support and intera
 ct with the community around us.\n-Advocate bicycle riding.\n-Empower and i
 nspire people to live out their crazy and wildest dreams\, therefore embrac
 ing the badassocity of life and living their full potential.\n-Promote posi
 tive self-image for all body types\, offering an alternative to the dangero
 us mono-culture of what the ideal body type is\; and promote female positiv
 e perspective that celebrates women’s empowerment.\n-Encourage\, exercise\,
  movement\, health\, and pro-physical lifestyle.\n-Organize and operate our
  dance troupe in a collective fashion.\n\nAbout Boxcar Books and Community 
 Center\nBoxcar Books and Community Center\, Inc. is a volunteer run\, non-p
 rofit organization that exists to provide new and used books\, zines\, maga
 zines\, and comics on topics of social justice\, independent media\, and fi
 ction for the community\; send literature of all types free of charge to pr
 isoners in the midwest\; and to provide a meeting space for community and l
 iterary groups.\n____________________________________\nBoxcar Books and Com
 munity Center\nThe Midwest Pages to Prisoners Project\n408 East Sixth Stree
 t\nBloomington Indiana 47408\nsteven@boxcarbooks.org\n812.339.8710\nhttp://
 www.boxcarbooks.org/\nhttp://pagestoprisoners.org/\n\n\ncheck out these vid
 eos: http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8hkyryHCtE4\nhttp://vimeo.com/1663322?p
 g=embed&amp\;sec=1663322
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T051651Z
LOCATION:Boxcar Books
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:The Sprockettes!
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
