UID:c8qehorc1e6v5cfcif96cn1tvg@google.com
CREATED:20090706T140319Z
DESCRIPTION:Sponsored by Bikesmiths\, Bleeding Heartland Roller Girls\, Blo
 omingfoods\, BloomingOUT\, Bloomington Community Bike Project\, Fiore Magaz
 ine\, Planned Parenthood\, and with help from the city of Bloomington.\n\nW
 hat's pink and black\, has two wheels and usually a few scabs? A Sprockette
 \, that's what. The Sprockettes\, based in Portland Oregon\, are a synchron
 ized dance troupe with a do-it-yourself work ethic. But instead of traditio
 nal dance moves\, their choreography features pink and black BMX bicycles i
 n a performance that's part dance and part stunt biking. Join us for a rock
 ing and shocking performance on Monday July 13th at 8pm behind Bloomington’
 s only volunteer powered\, non-profit bookstore and community space- Boxcar
  Books!\n(Catch them again at Tuesday the 14th at Bloomington’s Farmers Mar
 ket)\n\nWebsite- http://sprockettes.org/\nMyspace- http://www.myspace.com/s
 prockettes\nFeatured on NPR- http://www.npr.org/templates/story/story.php?s
 toryId=5613188\nBikePortland.org Sprockettes Archive- http://bikeportland.o
 rg/cats/the-scene/sprockettes/\nDocumentary “Small Movements” by Nickey Rob
 o about The Sprockettes- http://vimeo.com/1663322?pg=embed&amp\;sec=1663322
 \nVideo of The Sprockettes in action- http://agentchaosproductions.blogspot
 .com/2009/04/paris-hilton-meets-sprockettes.html\n\n\nThe Sprockettes began
  in the spring of 2004 when a pioneering group of ladies decided to put tog
 ether a performance for the Multnomah County Bike Fair. The crowd response 
 was so positive and we had so much fun that we thought it would be rad to s
 tay together and see where it would take us.\nSince then\, we’ve performed 
 from San Francisco to Vancouver B.C.\, toured in a veggie oil powered bus\,
  held workshops and skill shares\, received national media recognition and 
 inspired international bike dance teams.\nThe journey of the Sprockettes ha
 s been amazing\, held together by our passion for dancing\, bicycles\, DIY 
 ideology\, and striving to promote a healthy body image.\nOur members are a
 n eclectic group of women: we are teachers\, artists\, gardeners\, social w
 orkers\, musicians\, mothers\, bankers\, nannies\, writers and students.\nW
 e work as a collective choreographing\, practicing\, making merchandise and
  performing. We are constantly evolving.\n\nSprockette’s Mission Statement\
 n-The Sprockettes are an all female synchronized mini-bike dance troupe.\nI
 n a basic sense it is our mission to entertain audiences by choreographing 
 dances while using our bikes in our performance.\nIn a broader sense\, it i
 s our mission to:\n-Support and interact with the community around us.\n-Ad
 vocate bicycle riding.\n-Empower and inspire people to live out their crazy
  and wildest dreams\, therefore embracing the badassocity of life and livin
 g their full potential.\n-Promote positive self-image for all body types\, 
 offering an alternative to the dangerous mono-culture of what the ideal bod
 y type is\; and promote female positive perspective that celebrates women’s
  empowerment.\n-Encourage\, exercise\, movement\, health\, and pro-physical
  lifestyle.\n-Organize and operate our dance troupe in a collective fashion
 .\n\nAbout Boxcar Books and Community Center\nBoxcar Books and Community Ce
 nter\, Inc. is a volunteer run\, non-profit organization that exists to pro
 vide new and used books\, zines\, magazines\, and comics on topics of socia
 l justice\, independent media\, and fiction for the community\; send litera
 ture of all types free of charge to prisoners in the midwest\; and to provi
 de a meeting space for community and literary groups.\n____________________
 ________________\nBoxcar Books and Community Center\nThe Midwest Pages to P
 risoners Project\n408 East Sixth Street\nBloomington Indiana 47408\nsteven@
 boxcarbooks.org\n812.339.8710\nhttp://www.boxcarbooks.org/\nhttp://pagestop
 risoners.org/\n\n\ncheck out these videos: http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8
 hkyryHCtE4\nhttp://vimeo.com/1663322?pg=embed&amp\;sec=1663322
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T051331Z
LOCATION:the near west side Bloomingfoods!
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:The Sprockettes!
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
