CREATED:20090323T204522Z
DESCRIPTION:Spirit of '68 Presents...\n\nSTARDEATH AND WHITE DWARFS\nw/ Sec
 rets Between Sailors\n@ Bear's Place\nFriday April 17\n10pm\n$6\n21+\n\nSta
 rdeath and White Dwarfs\nwww.myspace.com/stardeath\n--------------\nStardea
 th & White Dwarfs are an Oklahoma City based power-pop quartet. Members Den
 nis Coyne\, Casey Joseph\, Matt Duckworth\, and Philip Rice combine their p
 assion and various influences to make some of the most intense\, weirdest a
 nd gratifying indie rock out their today.\n\nThe Flaming Lips frontman Wayn
 e Coyne is Dennis Coyne’s uncle\, and Stardeath & White Dwarfs don’t shy aw
 ay from embracing this connection and influence and sound much like early-9
 0’s transitional-period Flaming Lips\, only with their unique and modern ta
 ke on the sound.\n\nSecrets Between Sailors\nwww.myspace.com/secretsbetween
 sailors\n--------------\nSecrets Between Sailors was formed in December\, 2
 005 and has been winning over crowds\, young and old\, ever since. Hailing 
 from Bloomington\, IN—home of Indiana University and cornerstone of the eme
 rging indie rock renaissance in the Midwest—SBS has established a reputatio
 n as one of Middle America’s loudest and most adventurous bands. Garnering 
 comparison to the Who\, Built To Spill\, Gang Of Four\, Fugazi\, and the Cl
 ash\, Secrets is know for wild stage acrobatics and furious drumming. Their
  long-awaited full-length debut album was recorded at Russian Recording by 
 Mike Bridavsky and mastered by Bob Weston at Chicago Mastering.
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T051041Z
LOCATION:Bear's Place
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Stardeath and White Dwarfs
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
