DESCRIPTION:NEON INDIAN\nw/ Spirit Spine & DJ Phenom\n@ The Bishop\nThursda
 y October 29\n9:30 pm\n$8\n18+\n\nAn elusive new project from composer Alan
  Palomo. Neon Indian delivers equal parts synthetic nostalgia\, Dreampop lu
 llabies\, and grinding guitar noise to create something eerier than the sum
  of its parts. Forged after a hazy winter gathering in Texas\, this initial
  batch of tracks were the result of field recordings\, record samples\, a c
 ollection of bizarre synth sounds. Soliciting the visual acrobatics of Vide
 o artist Alicia Scardetta\, this project is setting out to be a multimedia 
 maelstrom. Orbiting around the themes of drug induced heartbreak\, weary af
 ternoons\, and lost chances\, this music provides a lush soundtrack to the 
 deadbeat exploits of teenage ennui. Neon Indian’s bedroom ballads have alre
 ady forged the upcoming Psychic Chasms\, the debut full-length\, set for re
 lease this Fall. They’ve been compared to New Order\, Future Bible Heroes\,
  and most recently said to sound like a saw-wave cutting a Doobie Brother’s
  song in half. Expect much racket to be had from this fresh faced crew.\n\n
 "Neon Indian renders precisely these memories of chilled-out\, lazy days of
  youthful abandon in song" - Pitchfork.com\n\n"Neon Indian’s debut LP\, Psy
 chic Chasms\, sounds like Discovery-era Daft Punk if they were one awesome 
 kid and had zero money." - The Fader\n\nwww.myspace.com/neonindian\nwww.mys
 pace.com/spiritspine\nwww.dopecouture.com
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T051455Z
LOCATION:The Bishop
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:NEON INDIAN
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
