UID:h6jhukrbm1ilbg5n1hscjqce3c@google.com
CREATED:20081125T151945Z
DESCRIPTION:107 W. 9th<br><Br>\nCelebrating the most universal subjects kno
 wn to man\, the BPP presents the sixth annual installment of Sex/Death\, th
 e theatre’s late-night showcase that whimsically walks that fine line betwe
 en high art and exploitation. Sex/Death unleashes a scintillating selection
  of new short plays providing the adventurous theater-goer with a visceral 
 rush that would make Alfred Kinsey blush. Sex/Death seeks to answer the que
 stion: "How far can theatre go?" \n<br><br>\n \n\nThis year\, the BPP is of
 fering 10 selections weaving tales odd sexual fantasies\, homicide\, infide
 lity and… bird porn?  \n\n <Br><Br>\n\nThanksgiving by Neal Utterback\n<Br>
 \nAn internet date turns out to be “tastier” than one man ever bargained fo
 r.\n<br><br>\nA Purposeful Life by Greg Ellis\n<Br>\nSWF seeks SM for leap 
 into the great beyond.\n\n <Br><br>\n\nThursday Routine by Rebecca Martin\n
 <Br>\nA married couple battle the doldrums of marriage using their wild ima
 ginations.\n\n <Br><Br>\n\nThe Becker Potential by Paul Kubin\n<Br>\nA Priv
 ate Dick realizes what happens at The Push/Pull Tavern stays at the Push/Pu
 ll Tavern.\n<Br><Br>\nStreet Corner by Mark Kingsbury\n<Br>\nA young woman 
 finds it much harder to lose her virginity than she would have thought. Esp
 ecially considering\, she’s standing on the corner of Indiana and Kirkwood.
 \n<Br><Br>\n \n\n100% Distracted by Joni McGary\n<Br>\nA visit from the plu
 mber has him fixing more than just that leaky faucet.\n\n <Br><Br>\n\nThe C
 ock Robin Porn Shop by Janis Butler Holm\n<Br>\nFind out the favorite porn 
 titles of the average “Jay”.\n\n \n<Br><Br>\nDifferent Creatures by Dan Fre
 y\n<Br>\nSex for the first time with a new lover sometimes exposes more tha
 n just their flesh.\n<Br><Br>\nNaked In The Play by Nick Moore\n<Br>\nLife 
 imitates Art when a playwright writes roles for him and his ex-girlfriend\,
  just so he can see her naked again.\n\n <Br><Br>\n\nLa Petite Mort by Beth
 any Barber\n<Br>\nWhat happens when the sex is so good\, it almost kills yo
 u?\n<Br><Br>\n \n\nSex/Death is produced by BPP Artistic Director Richard P
 erez and directed by BPP Ensemble Members Holly Holbrook and Jim Hettmer. \
 n<Br><Br>\n \n\n“Sex/Death has become a very popular production for our the
 atre.  This year we’ve made a concerted effort to continue to improve its p
 roduction values\,“ explains Mr. Perez. “In order to keep the ticket price 
 low\, we’ve added more performances.  We hope you enjoy this new and improv
 ed showcase.”\n\n \n<Br><Br>\nPerformances of Sex/Death are December 9 – 13
  and 15 – 17 @ 10pm at the BPP (107 W. 9th).  Tickets are only $5\, availab
 le at the door the night of the event.  For more information\, call 334-118
 8 or email bppwrite@newplays.org. \n<Br><Br>\n \n\nSex/Death is presented a
 s part of the BPP’s Dark Alley Series.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T051555Z
LOCATION:Bloomington Playwrights Project
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:SEX/DEATH - 6th annual BPP late-night short play showcase 
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
