CREATED:20081107T173516Z
DESCRIPTION:Free Admission<br><br>\nOCEAN is a concert of new music for lar
 ge ensemble written for a group of about thirty musicians by composer Sulai
 man Zai.  It is an annual event and the fourth such project written by Sula
 iman Zai in the last three years. \n<br><br>\n \n\nThe approach is a "new" 
 approach of writing for the specific players involved in the group as was d
 one in earlier times.  The composer would find out what players were availa
 ble in the area and then write specifically for those players.\n<Br><br>\n 
 \n\nOCEAN is fun music to play and to listen to and is made up of players i
 ncluding strings\, classical guitars\, brass\, percussion\, voices\, piano 
 and more.  The music is written with the players and their skill levels kep
 t in mind by the composer.  The players are challenged to play music never 
 heard before\, knowing it was written for them specifically.  This creates 
 a wonderful sense of community between the players and the listeners as wel
 l.  It is created and performed with a sense of joy in presenting something
  brand new to the listener.\n<Br><br>\nDon't miss this satisfying and fun p
 erformance!\n<br><br>\nMany thanks to all the wonderful participating music
 ians and the support of the community in helping make this program happen! 
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T051417Z
LOCATION:4001 South Rogers St. (The Unity Building Chapel)
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Ocean Concert
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
