CREATED:20090107T144521Z
DESCRIPTION:FANCY FOOTWORK dance party returns! Presented by Scion\, Iheart
 comix Records\, and Rad Summer.\n<br><br>\nWith deejays...\n<br><br>\nACTIO
 N JACKSON (Rad Summer) http://www.myspace.com/actionjacksondj\n<br><br>\nPH
 ENOM (Sneak Attack) http://www.myspace.com/colinrebey\n<br><br>\n**********
 ************************************************\n<br><br>\nAND SPECIAL GUE
 ST FROM CHICAGO\, FRESH OFF OPENING FOR JUSTICE ON NYE....\n<br><br>\nZEBO 
 (Hot Dog Records / Chicago) http://www.myspace.com/djzebo\n<br><br>\n“This 
 boy is Chi to the core!!!” – Scottie B (the Godfather of Baltimore Club)\nP
 raised by rising stars such as Tittsworth\, this early collaborator with Fl
 osstradamus\nmember Autobot\, DJ Zebo is now spreading this schizophrenic d
 ance and hip-hop genre bending style known as “Baltimore Club”. Through his
  touring\, four Chicago residencies including Thursdays and Fridays at Evil
  Olive and Saturdays at Subterranean\, strong production work and faultless
  mixes\, Zebo has morphed into an eclectic\, crowd-pleasing\, multi-genre d
 ance DJ. He’s opened up for such acts as: Kool Herc\, Mixmaster Mike\, Gran
 dmaster Flash\, Moby\, Q-Bert and Spankrock among others.\n<br><br>\nIn 200
 7 his mix “My Style is Furious” was commissioned in conjuntion with the Spa
 rk’s company’s participation in the Detroit Electronic Music Festival\, and
  quickly found popularity through the influential Discobelle music blog\, d
 ownloaded via said sight 0ver 17\,000 times. The same year Zebo was also in
 terviewed by publications such as New City\, Trash Menagerie\, London’s Oh 
 Death blog and made Chicago based Novem.com’s featured artist for September
 . His “Grown Mix” was also the first of the Mixes 2007 series on Spankrock’
 s Fullyfitted blog. Zebo was also voted Chicago’s #2 Favorite DJ for 2007 o
 n local celebrity photo site Everyoneisfamous.com second only to fellow DJ 
 comrades\, Flosstradamus. “Zebo taught me how to spin and is by far the bes
 t all around DJ in the Chi!” – Autobot/Curtified of Flosstradamus. He was a
 lso hand selected as one of two exclusive DJs for Chicago’s Fashion Week\, 
 and made New City Magazine’s list of top 45 musicians that rock Chicago in 
 May of 2008.\n<br><br>\nWhile there are many hustling DJs in town\, Chicago
  is lucky to have Zebo rocking the likes of… well\, just about everywhere. 
 A seemingly omnipresent figure around West Side clubs and lounges\, Zebo pa
 cks a cut-up crateful of styles\, from hip-hop and B-more to French eletro-
 disco and even a nasty snippet of a techno track or throwback freestyle gem
 . While this maximal approach might be increasingly common among DJs who ca
 ter to ADD-riddled mash-up club casualties\, Zebo stays head-and shoulders 
 above the rest for knowing that just because you can\, doesn’t mean you sho
 uld. Skills can be honed\, but taste can’t be taught. Although he has launc
 hed his own label to put out mostly\nB-more-leaning beats\, it is his skill
 s as a DJ that draw the most water in this town.\n<br><br>\nAnd...Hosted by
  the inimitable GREY GRANITE (Indianapolis) http://www.myspace.com/greygran
 ite\n<br><br>\n**********************************************************\n
 <br><br>\nThis is also an official release party for MATT & KIM's new album
  "Grand" dropping January 20th on IHEARTCOMIX records. We will be playing t
 he album in its entirety to kick off the night.\n<br><br>\n****************
 ******************************************\n<br><br>\nAt the Bloomington Pl
 aywrights Project<br>\nOn 9th St between Walnut and College<br>\nALL AGES<b
 r>\n21+ to drink<br>\n$1 BEERS!<br>\n10pm<br>\n$5 cover <br>FREE BEFORE 11!
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T051535Z
LOCATION:The Bloomington Playwright's Project
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Fancy Footwork w/ djs Zebo\, Action Jackson\, & Phenom
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
