UID:2subrhghkvdgu4hlkol2pqh43g@google.com
CREATED:20080922T140534Z
DESCRIPTION:Spirit of '68 Presents:\n<Br><br>\nAwesome Color\,\nWax Fang\,\
 nThe Broderick\n@ Jakes Nightclub\nMonday September 29th\n9pm\n$6\n<Br><Br>
 \nTickets available at Landlocked Music and ticketmaster.com\n<br><Br>\nAwe
 some Color\nwww.myspace.com/awesomecolor\n--------------------------\nPsych
 -garage-noise purveyors Awesome Color coalesced after Michigan skater/musos
  Michael Troutman (aka Michael Awesome) and Allison Busch (aka Allison Awes
 ome) hooked up with fellow Great Lake State expat Derek Stanton (aka Derek 
 Awesome) in Brooklyn\, NY\, in 2004. Tired of the same old\, same old that 
 was passing for N.Y.C. underground punk at the time\, the trio set out to i
 nject a little Detroit rock know-how into the tired scene. Succeeding marve
 lously at channeling the grit and free abandon of the Stooges and MC5 into 
 a propulsive\, riff-based\, Black Sabbath-informed mule-kick of a live show
 \, the group soon caught the ear of Sonic Youth's Thurston Moore -- who was
 ted no time snatching the band up for his Ecstatic Peace! label.\n<Br><Br>\
 nWax Fang\nwww.myspace.com/waxfang\n----------------------\nImagine Stephen
  Malkmus impersonating Neil Diamond covering the Pixies\, playing a guitar 
 like Chuck Berry one second\, Robert Fripp the next\, backed by a thunderou
 s rhythm section ala Moon/ Entwistle or Bonham/ Jones\, but with the techno
 logical savvy and arrangements of\, say\, Eno- era Roxy Music.\n<Br><Br>\nT
 he Broderick\nwww.myspace.com/thebroderickband\n---------------------------
 --\nForged in Vincennes\, Indiana\, in the fire of their own discontent\, T
 he Broderick proves that even in the most unlikely of settings\, great indi
 e rock still survives. Formerly 806 Main St.\, the band is turning heads wi
 th its original blend of clever songwriting and jangly guitar work. The fiv
 e musicians that form The Broderick each bring a different piece of a puzzl
 e that shapes the band’s distinct sound. After two years of constant giggin
 g and critical acclaim the band has perfected its style of indie rock\, fol
 k and pop. With this interesting meshing of sound The Broderick is able tra
 nscend genres and find fans in all corners of the music world\, only adding
  to its already established fan base.
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T051215Z
LOCATION:Jakes
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Awesome Color\, Wax Fang\, The Broderick
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
