CREATED:20081001T132728Z
DESCRIPTION:Black Joe Lewis<br>\nThe Aaron Persinger Band<Br>\nLeon Chance 
 and The Longshots<Br>\n@ Bear's Place<Br>\nWednesday\, October 15th\n10 p.m
 .\n$6\n+21\n<Br><br>\nBlack Joe Lewis\n------------------\nwww.myspace.com/
 blackjoelewis\nSoul is alive and well in the River City\, but the old-timer
 s have nothing to do with it. J.J. Lewis\, aka Black Joe\, in his mid-20s a
 nd full of spunk\, stands tall and strong onstage with his band of gentleme
 n. He howls into the mic\, half James Brown\, half his own man\, and he spl
 ays blood and heart all over the guitar. It’s imperfect yet beautiful. Rein
 venting his roots of Lighting Hopkins and Sam Cooke\, Lewis adds a Red Rive
 r vibe to the true blues of generations past. Born in Tucson\, Ariz.\, Lewi
 s moved to the Austin area as a child\, attending Round Rock High School\, 
 if only temporarily. Starting out with his band Cool Breeze in 2002\, an od
 d combo of Weary Boys pickers and harp-blower Walter Daniels\, Lewis began 
 honing his craft slowly and steadily: more guitar\, more talkin’\, more cry
 in’\, more wailin’. In 2007\, he ditched the Breeze and formed the Honey Be
 ars\, releasing an EP of the same name that summer.
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T051500Z
LOCATION:Bear's Place
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Black Joe Lewis\, The Aaron Persinger Band\, Leon Chance and The Lo
 ngshots
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
