DESCRIPTION:Indiana Forest Alliance benefit show and call-out at Rachael's 
 Cafe!\n\n5:30-7:30PM:\n\nCall-out meeting: Learn more about the backcountry
  and the upcoming hearing in Indianapolis. If you're interested and/or want
  to get involved\, please come! An added bonus is that if you come early\, 
 we are only asking for donations\, so you can come early and learn stuff an
 d avoid the cover.\n\n8pm:\n\nThree amazing bands are playing. $3 cover. It
  all goes to Indiana Forest Alliance.\n\nCITY CENTER\n\nhttp://www.myspace.
 com/citycenternyc\n\nhttp://www.citycenternyc.blogspot.com/\n\nRyan Howard 
 & Fred Thomas. Brooklyn\, NY. You may remember Fred Thomas from such bands 
 as Saturday Looks Good To Me. City Center's self-titled debut came out earl
 ier this year\, and it's amazing. Check out their myspace page. They're bri
 lliant.\n\nFOUND OBJECTS\n\nhttp://www.myspace.com/foundobjectsisart\n\nPAN
 TREE OWL\n\nhttp://www.myspace.com/pantreeowl\n\nSo that's three bands for 
 three dollars. And it's free if you come to the call-out meeting. And it's 
 all-ages and they serve beer.\n\nAnd that's not all.\n\nSome other upcoming
  IFA benefit shows:\n\n10/31: Stand Tall Halloween Party: Nettles\, Mindfre
 ak\, Bishop of Norwich (Patrick from Found Objects) @ The Bishop. Cover = w
 hatever you want to donate. 18+\n\n11/14: Shedding\, Spirit Spine\, & 1 mor
 e TBA @ The Bishop. 18+\n\n11/21: DJ/ Rupture & Matt Shadetek\, openers TBA
  @ the Vid. 21+. $10.\n\n\n\nFor $20\, you can get admission to all four of
  these shows and an Indiana Forest Alliance membership. (The membership alo
 ne is usually $15.) Either e-mail me at jflannel@indiana.edu or come to Rac
 hael's cafe on October 21st if you're interested in getting the package dea
 l. While supplies last.
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T051600Z
LOCATION:Rachael's Cafe
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Stand Tall: City Center\, Found Objects\, Pantree Owl
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
