DESCRIPTION:A call to artists with some former or current connection to Blo
 omington\, Indiana to contribute to “Coming and Going: A Transient Collecti
 on of Bloomington Art.”  Bloomington affiliated artists from a diverse rang
 e of backgrounds are invited to submit one piece of original 2D or 3D art t
 o this multimedia show\, with opening night slated for March 5th\, 2011 at 
 the Lodge in Bloomington\, Indiana. \n\nThough Bloomington is noted for its
  transient nature\, the core of its arts community—both above and undergrou
 nd—is one that is lasting\, prolific and uniquely edgy for a town of its si
 ze.  To that end\, it is our hope that featured artists will thematically e
 xamine the play and contrast between the ephemeral and the enduring\, with 
 specific content focusing on some subjective representation of their time s
 pent in Bloomington. Examples include painted Video Saloon whispers\, scree
 n printed house show sex\, knitted slabs of limestone\, and midair shots of
  Bobby Knight-slung chairs sculpted from ice. But really\, these are just e
 xamples. You be the artist…and the judge\, remembering that this is a non-c
 ompetitive show and will thusly only include winners.  \n\nJust send us som
 ething Bloomingtoncentric\, however you define it.\n\nIMPORTANT DEADLINES/D
 ATES:\n\nOctober 15th by midnight\, please send statement of commitment to 
 either Lori Canada at locanada30@yahoo.com or Diane Knoll at dianeknoll@gma
 il.com\, or by writing either of us via Facebook. Please include in stateme
 nt a description of submission as well as digital image if available. \n\nF
 ebruary 15th by midnight\, please send actual submission  to: Diane Knoll\,
  1517 S. Nancy Street\, Bloomington\, IN 47401 or Lori Canada\, 933 N. Jack
 son St.\, Bloomington\, IN 47404\n\nMarch 11th\, 2011\, Opening reception f
 or “Coming and Going: A Transient Collection of Bloomington Art" at the Lod
 ge\, 6 p.m.-? More details to follow! \n\nFor those who wish to sell their 
 works\, please note that a 15% commission is requested to go toward reimbur
 sement for rental and promotional costs. \n\n\n\n\n\n\nhttp://www.facebook.
 com/event.php?eid=156599624351528
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T050919Z
LOCATION:The Lodge (above Subway) \, 101 E. 6th St. \, Bloomington\, IN
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Transient Bloomington Call for Artists
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
