DESCRIPTION:The program for International Visiting Artists (PIVA) and Fulle
 r Projects presents Adolfo Cifuentes in Dialogue with artists Amy Burrell\,
  Julian Hensarling and Jay Garst. Cifuentes presents his interactive "insta
 llation" of various levels and sundry surprises for one night only.\n\nExte
 nded hours!\n\nAdolfo Cifuentes:\nColombian artist Adolfo Cifuentes is curr
 ently working on his PhD. in Belo Horizonte\, Brazil\, entitled "The White 
 Cube and the Black Box: Two Traditions of Gazing" where he brings into ques
 tion traditional formats for viewing art. He has his Masters degree in Russ
 ian Culture\, Language and Literature from the Pushkin Institute of Russian
  Language and Literature\, and has been an art teacher in higher education 
 in Colombia for more than 10 years. He has been an active artist in various
  international events\, including: the Havana 2000 Biennial\, Jacarta Festi
 val of Art and Culture at the Kamang Center in 2001\, Vozes de Mestres (Voi
 ces of Masters) in Joinville\, Brazil in 2009\, Balsta Falkhausset in Stock
 holm\, and Café L’Ecume in Paris.\n\nWhat is PIVA?\nProgram for Internation
 al Visiting Artists (PIVA) brings emerging international visiting artists t
 o teach during the second eight-week session of fall and spring semesters. 
 The program is jointly sponsered by the Collins Living-Learning Center and 
 the Henry Radford Hope School of Fine Arts. Artists/scholars teach a theory
  course for Collins that focuses on contemporary and cultural criticism\, a
 nd a studio practice course for Fine Arts. They also hold an artist's talk 
 and present work made during their stay through a Fine Arts Fuller Project.
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T051251Z
LOCATION:Fuller Projects
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Art Opening: Dialogues
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
