BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Let's Go! Bloomington
DTSTART:20090402T020000Z
DTEND:20090402T050000Z
DTSTAMP:20260905T041548Z
UID:c78acmcpderr1l4no14tto56hc@google.com
CREATED:20090330T201250Z
DESCRIPTION:Spirit of '68 presents...\n\nDRAKKAR SAUNA\nw/ Busman's Holiday
 \, Thousand Arrows\nWednesday April 1\n@ Bear's Place\n10pm\n$6\n21+\n\nDra
 kkar Sauna\nwww.myspace.com/drakkansasauna\n--------------\nIf not the firs
 t\, then surely the most common question we are asked is how we came to nam
 e ourselves Drakkar Sauna. We want to tell you. We want you to know\, if on
 ly so that you’ll stop asking. It makes us feel vulnerable\, it makes us fe
 el judged.\n\nWe thought it sounded like a palindrome. What it comes down t
 o is we didn’t have any scratch paper handy and our understanding of what a
  palindrome is wasn’t accurate. But that’s what happened. ‘Drakkar’sounded 
 like a palindrome. So did ‘Sauna’. We thought that two palindromes would ma
 ke one bigger palindrome. Obviously\, we were\, in part\, mistaken. I hope 
 now your curiosity is satisfied and you will not think too poorly of us for
  our incomplete command of the language.\n\nWe live in Lawrence\, Kansas an
 d are fathers to three full-length recordings\, Rover\, Drakkansasauna\, & 
 Jabraham Lincoln.\n\nWe have recorded\, also\, an ep\, Hunger Overcame Us a
 nd helped produce a feature video\, "The Blood Feud\," a work of fiction. W
 e are\, in all things\, supported by our union with Marriage Records. We ha
 ve toured the U.S.A. a few times. We have toured with Dark Meat and the Vom
 it Lazers Family Galaxy\, Split Lip Rayfield\, The Impossible Shapes\, Two 
 Gallants\, Magnolia Electric Company and by ourselves.\n\nOur names are Jef
 f Stolz and Wallace Cochran and we get along well.\n\nBusman's Holiday\nwww
 .myspace.com/busmansholiday\n--------------\nBusman’s Holiday is a band of 
 brothers. This lends well to their affection towards barbershop style harmo
 nies and their ease of interacting on stage both musically and socially. Th
 ey have been influenced greatly by singing on the streets through much of t
 his country. Their melodica\, acoustic guitar\, upright bass and suitcase b
 ass drum compliments the genre hopping pop music. With their unpredictable 
 live shows they strive to leave their audiences entertained. Busman’s Holid
 ay is where mohawks and mullets meet harmoniously.\n\n"Busman’s Holiday\, w
 hich is a cool band out of Bloomington\, they actually\, like\, go busking\
 , or whatever it is\, on the streets of Bloomington. And it’s really a cute
  band. They write these really\, really cute\, you know\, sing-along\, kind
  of memorable songs. I’ve been following them for awhile. They’re connected
  to the band the Delicious\; which is\, I love the Delicious."\n-Jed Banner
 \, Musical Family Tree\n\nThousand Arrows\nwww.myspace.com/thousandarrows\n
 --------------
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T051410Z
LOCATION:Bear's Place
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:DRAKKAR SAUNA
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
