DESCRIPTION:On Friday\, May 13\, Tony Ardizzone reads from his latest book\
 , The Whale Chaser. There will be discussion time and book signing after th
 e reading.\n \n7:00 p.m.\nSweet Claire Bakery\n309 East Third Street\n \nFr
 ee\n \nArdizzone is the author of seven books of fiction and the winner of 
 the Flannery O'Connor Award for Short Fiction\, a Pushcart Prize\, and many
  other honors. His short stories have appeared in journals such as Ploughsh
 ares\, Black Warrior Review\, Epoch\, TriQuarterly\, The Georgia Review\, P
 rairie Schooner\, and Sonora Review. He is the recipient of two individual 
 artist fellowships in fiction from the National Endowment for the Arts\, an
 d he teaches in the MFA program at Indiana University.\n \nThe Lemonstone s
 eries includes three events in the spring\, and three events in the fall.\n
 The Writers Guild is a member of the Arts Alliance of Greater Bloomington.
