DESCRIPTION:JAVELIN\nw/ Totally Michael and DJ Phenom\nat The Bishop\nFrida
 y March 26\n11pm\n$8\n18+\n\nJavelin consists of two cousins\, Tom Van Busk
 irk and George Langford. They started making music together in Providence\,
  RI in 2004\, although their earliest collaborative tapes date back to a bu
 nk bedroom near the sea shore. They are signed to Luaka Bop records and liv
 e in New York.\n\nIn performance\, Javelin will use colorfully painted boom
 boxes that form large speaker totems (“boombaatas”) which can hang from the
  ceiling or stack up on the floor like pyramids. The signal from the show i
 s broadcast via FM transmitter\, thereby fostering audience participation (
 B.Y.O.Boombox) or fueling battery-powered\, mobile parties.\n\nThe duo has 
 played venues as diverse as the children’s branch of the Olneyville Public 
 Library (RI)\, to the Museum of Modern Art (NY)\, both of which happened in
  the same week. When not performing\, Javelin is busy producing. Together t
 hey have amassed a vast catalogue of music\, varying in its aesthetic range
 . Songs resemble the record collection from whence they spring\, if not lit
 erally as when sampling\, then figuratively as when past forms are cited an
 d recontextualized.\n\nSounds range from broken dance jams to relaxed instr
 umental cut-ups\, created with love on their MPCs. Long forgotten samples a
 re chopped and re-assembled with drums\, wooden recorders\, old keyboards\,
  handmade thumb pianos or whatever instruments are readily at hand. The res
 ult is a kind of mix tape fantasy (residing in the mythical “dollar bins of
  the future”)\, where R&B impresarios\, amateur booty bass producers and An
 dean flautists hold equal sway.\n\nwww.myspace.com/hotjamzofjavelin\nwww.my
 space.com/totallymichael
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T051716Z
LOCATION:The Bishop
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:JAVELIN
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
