CREATED:20090209T175454Z
DESCRIPTION:Spirit of '68 Presents...\nHi Red Center\nGood Luck\nPush-Pull\
 n@ Bear's Place\nFriday Feb. 13th\n10pm\n$5\n21+\n\nHi Red Center\nwww.mysp
 ace.com/hiredcenter\n--------------\nFormed in 2003\, Hi Red Center are an 
 endearingly odd and distorted version of a familiar instrumental quartet. C
 onsider a drummer who swings effortlessly between lurching off-time rhythms
  and anthemic beats\, a drummer/ vibraphone/electronic/synth player who add
 s everything from burbling noise to contagious melodies\, a bassist who lay
 s down the frenzied punch of post-punk with the melodic dexterity of krautr
 ock\, and a guitarist that creates a rich textural fuzz that makes it rock.
 \n\nHi Red Center released their debut album "Architectural Failures" on Pa
 ngaea Recordings (now Natural Selection Records) back in 2006. The band's s
 econd album (and Joyful Noise debut) Assemble moves in more clear\, concise
  direction while somehow containing instrumentation that\, here and there\,
  seems to slide of its track\, breaking into weirdly juxtaposed parallel tr
 ajectories. They layer melody upon melody\, and top it all off with vocal h
 armonies reminiscent of an asymmetrical barber-shop quartet. Their music is
  a dizzying mix of rhythmic smashes\, noisy harmonies\, and cultural innuen
 do that add up to graceful\, sculp- ture-like songs. Hi Red Center makes mu
 sic for folks who like to sing\, for people who like to dance\, and for eve
 ryone who likes their songs thoroughly mixed and mashed.\n\nGood Luck\nwww.
 myspace.com/wearegoodluck\n--------------\nHere are a number of things you 
 may want to know about us:\n# We wrote our first song on april 13th\, 2007\
 , in a Bloomington\, IN southeast side basement.\n# We played 16 shows in 2
 007\, and so far way more in 2008.\n# We decided on our name after reading 
 it on a sidewalk while walking home from a delicious Chinese Restaurant.\n#
  We are friends who knew each other from playing with each others past musi
 cal projects like Matty Pop Chart\, One Reason\, K-10 Prospect\, Abe Froman
 \, Mt. Gigantic\, Bodyhammer\, and Los Gatos Negros. We used to live in Mis
 sissippi\, Kentucky\, and Michigan before something drew us all to Blooming
 ton.\n# We first released a 6 song demo that we recorded with our friend Mi
 ke Dixon at Russian Recording here in Bloomington on 10/19/07 from 3pm to 3
 am.\n# We self-released our 13 song album "Into Lake Griffy" on cd May 10th
 \, 2008. It was recorded and mixed with our friend Mike Bridavsky at Russia
 n Recording in February and April of 2008. The release is packaged in a ful
 l color 100% recycled digipak with 100% recycled mini poster insert. We put
  a lot of time and energy and life into it.\n# No Idea Records is releasing
  the vinyl LP version of Into Lake Griffy sometime this winter. It will com
 e with a digital version of the album as well. The cd will still come from 
 us!\n# We toured the east coast last May and June and the west coast with o
 ur buddy Paul Baribeau in September and October.\n# We like to listen to Ha
 rry Potter books\, National Public Radio Podcasts\, and audio from Jurrasic
  Park in our vehicle.\n# We thank residents of Guilty Pleasures house past 
 and future for putting up with the incessant noise of practice.\n\nPush-Pul
 l\nwww.myspace.com/pushpull\n--------------\nAcross the street from an aban
 doned skiing facility in Nashville\, Indiana\, there stands an A-Frame. Fro
 m within come the sounds of a guitar amp set to "3"\, a bass dug deep\, and
  the snap of drum sticks. The chopped sticks are the clarifier of the guita
 r/bass relationship\, thus hearing protection is strictly enforced. Occasio
 nal bleeding and consistent sweating are par for the course. The music asso
 ciates itself with all conditions including: humans\, diseases\, books\, fi
 lms\, dead hearts\, events predating the big bang\, flight\, empty hands\, 
 breeding\, fire\, water\, the jesuses and how to not panic. The sound is ti
 ghtly wedged between a rock and a roll\, hard and compact\, but fresh and p
 iping hot. The final result is direct and spastic\; a bit cryptic\, while s
 imultaneously genuine like pay day. They are Mikes. Mikes are Push-Pull.
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T051745Z
LOCATION:Bear's Place
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Hi Red Center\, Good Luck\, Push-Pull
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
