UID:495rt97dcmtk6f02e297j5i8n8@google.com
CREATED:20091012T174053Z
DESCRIPTION:OLD CANES\nw/ Prayer Breakfast & Hanz Bronz\nSunday October 18\
 n@ The Video Saloon\n8pm\n$7\n\nOld Canes is the side project of Appleseed 
 cast front man Chris Crisci who has enlisted the aid of his friends in Minu
 s Story and Drakkar Sauna. While folk music at heart\, the presentation is 
 far from traditional\, with the songs drawing elements from different influ
 ences (such as indie and even punk rock)\, and the rulebook of contemporary
  recording thrown out the window. "Production value\, fidelity\, a low nois
 e floor\, whatever\, are all beside the point\," says Crisci. "The only thi
 ngs I care about are the idea and the energy. Music loses out when the focu
 s is on slick production\, and not on expressing what matters most in a son
 g."\n\nThe energy and ideas on Feral Harmonic are palpable starting with so
 ng one\, "Little Bird Courage"\, as the album launches with joyous\, barrel
 ing drums\, furiously strummed guitars\, and glistening toy piano that erup
 ts into a chorus of trumpets. Cautiously plucked banjo forewarns the ominou
 s lessons of "Trust"\, while cascading guitars\, trumpets\, and pounding dr
 ums build to a boisterous roar\, contrasting the lyrical lover's lament in 
 "Stuck". The album closes\, after all\, with wistful "Southern Radio"\, whi
 ch features only Crisci's weathered voice and an acoustic guitar.\n\nThe so
 ngs tackle the idea that fear can be transcended\, that the human spirit fl
 ies in the face of life's complications\, hurdles\, and pain. "The words ar
 e all over the place\, like life\, and half the time I don't know if I'm ha
 ppy or sad\, or both\," says Crisci. "I wrote what I was feeling at the tim
 e\, and so the songs go from one extreme to the other." All of life's energ
 ies\, contrasts and complements - strength and weakness\, courage and fear\
 , joy and despair - are in Feral Harmonic\, a wild state of musical harmony
  and sounds as unfettered and irrepressible as the intent with which it was
  crafted.\n\nwww.myspace.com/oldcanes\nwww.myspace.com/prayerbreakfast\nwww
 .myspace.com/hanzbronze
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T051427Z
LOCATION:The Vid
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Old Canes
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
