DESCRIPTION:Spirit of ’68 Promotions is proud to present Amo Joy!\, The Del
 icious\, Bunnygrunt\, and Red Bird performing live at The Cinemat on Septem
 ber 13\, 2008. The show will begin at 7:30 p.m. displaying a vibrant assort
 ment of what the Midwest indie/pop scene has to offer. This concert will co
 st $4 at the door. All ages.\n<br><br>\nAmo Joy!\nhttp://www.myspace.com/am
 ojoy\nRepresenting Indianapolis\, Amo Joy’s playful fun sound and harmoniou
 s vocals bring energy and artistry back to the stage. Comparable to the fun
 ky pop style of Of Montreal\, Amo Joy’s creative approach to the manipulati
 on of sound allows for some unusual noises such as kazoos\, a ukulele\, ban
 jo\, bells and even a toy piano\, giving this band a lively playful feel. I
 nfluenced by bands such as The Kinks\, ELO\, Dovovan\, and The Beatles\, Am
 o Joy! is pioneering new ways to contort sounds and create music that could
  put a smile on anyone’s face. With Adam Gross on guitar and vocals (and of
  course\, kazoo)\, Steve Trowbridge on drums and banjo\, Paul Cobb on bass\
 , Alison Pitt on flute and synth\, and James Furness in charge of the stran
 ge yet unique noises\, this bands’ innovative style makes then a must see\,
  not to mention the perfect soundtrack for any dance party.\n(Royal Rhino F
 lying Records)\n<br><br>\nThe Delicious\nhttp://www.myspace.com/thedeliciou
 s\nMade up of Ben Fowler\, David Woodruff\, and Matt and Nick Romy\, this l
 ocal Bloomington bands’ clever lyrics and mellow sound boldly represents a 
 new kind of pop music. With The Unicorns\, The Pixies\, and Andrew Bird as 
 some of their main influences\, The Delicious convey a smart and creative f
 eeling not only with their original sound but through their vocals as well.
 \n(Joyful Noise Recordings)\nContact- info@joyfulnoiserecordings.com\n<br><
 br>\nBunnygrunt\nhttp://www.myspace.com/bunnygrunt\nThe brainchild of Matt 
 Harnish and Karen Reid\, Bunnygrunt combines flirty colorful indie inspired
  lyrics with a grungy pop beat resulting in an indie/ grunge/ pop infused s
 ound straight from the Staint Louis music scene. Occasionally accompanied b
 y various members of band such as Eric Van Damage\, Jason Hutto\, Mario Vie
 le\, Jason Paul\, and K. Erik Seaver\, this band never fails to entertain.\
 n(hhbtm [happy birthday to me])\nContact- mike@hhbtm.com\n<br><br>\nRed Bir
 d\nhttp://www.myspace.com/redbirdredbird\nAlso native to the Bloomington ar
 ea\, Red Bird brings a softer side to pop music. With experimental sounds a
 nd poetic lyrics\, this bands’ slower approach to pop has a rather calming 
 effect. Michael Bushman\, Andrew Shaw\, and Alex Kuch create an almost euph
 oric atmosphere with their cool melodies and hushed tones. Soft yet confide
 nt\, this band contributes a sound that provides a truly exceptional experi
 ence.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T051559Z
LOCATION:The Cinemat
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Amo Joy!\, The Delicious\, Bunnygrunt
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
