DESCRIPTION:Monday\, September 28th 2009\n6pm. Free. Boxcar Books. 408 E 6t
 h St.\n\nRelative Discomfort: The Family Survival Guide by Jeremy Greenberg
 \nwww.relativediscomfort.com\n\nLet this holiday season be the first in whi
 ch you don’t dread seeing your loved ones...\n\nUnder the guise of a “guide
 book\,” Jeremy delights readers with hilarious\, original\, smart perspecti
 ves on the family dynamic. Readers will laugh out loud\, and come away with
  a richer understanding of what exactly makes their families tick\, and wha
 t about their families ticks them off.\n\nJeremy tells it like it is about 
 how to “survive” seeing family this upcoming holiday season\, as well as ho
 w to survive spending time with relatives of differing political views—a ti
 mely topic for this upcoming election season.\n\nSee Jeremy at Bear’s Place
  for Comedy Caravan in the Evening. www.bearsplacebar.com\n\nAbout the auth
 or:\n\nAn internationally headlining stand-up comedian\, columnist and auth
 or\, Jeremy Greenberg writes a column entitled “Eastside: Center of the Uni
 verse\,” which celebrates the elevated status of suburban Seattle. He has b
 een a contributor to the Complete Idiot’s Guide to Jokes (Alpha/Penguin)\, 
 a joke writer for Comics Unleashed with Byron Allen\, and has written for M
 SN\, Geek Monthly\, Twins Magazine\, and Pregnancy and Newborn Magazine. Wh
 en not traveling and writing\, Jeremy is home with his wife and twin sons i
 n Kirkland\, Washington\, a suburb of Seattle and center of the known unive
 rse.\n\nContact and Information:\n\nwww.relativediscomfort.com\n\nwww.jerem
 ygreenberg.com
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T051257Z
LOCATION:Boxcar Books
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Book Reading: "Relative Discomfort: The Family Survival Guide"
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
