DESCRIPTION:The past few years have been a screaming and shouting success t
 hanks to all of you! This will be no exception! We welcome you to join us i
 n another long evening of Sun Worshipping\, Dancing\, Drinking\, Merriment\
 , and "Bringing In The Light". An off kilter occasion dedicated to our plan
 et’s off kilter axis\, themed towards the days long ago when sun worship wa
 s a bit more socially important.\n<br><Br>\nBack by popular demand is the T
 HEME from last year's event: HEADDRESSES & ROBES!\n<Br><br>\nDue to overwhe
 lming enthusiasm\, we'll be repeating the theme this year. We’re sending th
 is out a little early\, so anyone who would like to build their own headdre
 ss or robe can get a head start on it!<Br>\nOnce again we'll be returning t
 o the age of pagans\, sun worshippers\, and archaic rituals. A time long ag
 o when the Sun ruled supreme and mass religion only seemed like a good idea
 . So\, don your finest headdress and/or robe\, and/or clothes\, and/or noth
 ing at all and come on over to our cave for some good times\, exotic sounds
 \, and hanging out.<Br>\nThink Polynesian Sun Mythology\, Saturnalia\, Toji
 \, X-mas Lights\, Hawkwind\, Sacred Animals\, Stonehenge\, Hyperborean Frea
 kout…think what you want!\nCheck out photos from previous solstice parties 
 here: www.myspace.com/kneeshy\n<br><Br>\nSun = Fun\n<Br><br>\nSunday (remem
 ber to purchase any booze you may want the day before)<BR>\nDecember 21st<B
 r>\n804 South Rogers Street<br>\nEvent: 8:00pm - who cares!<Br>\nsounds spu
 n by: honkey kong<Br>\nTell a friend!\n<Br><br>\nCheers-<Br>\nJeremy Kenned
 y\, j. Shelley Harrison\, and John Dawson\n<Br><Br>\n(Make sure to save som
 e energy for our New Years Eve celebration! j. Shelley Harrison\, Erin Brad
 y\, and Jeremy Kennedy have joined forces to throw down another rad New Yea
 rs Eve party. Like the one last year at Space 101\, except at the Waldron… 
 and funner! More details later…)\n<Br><br>\n*Making your own headdresses an
 d robes can be an enjoyable project!\n<Br><br>\n**There is limited off stre
 et parking behind the house. However\, it won’t last long. Parking is bette
 r on either Wylie St. or Dodds St.\n<Br><br>\n***Preplanning a way home may
  also be good\, we don’t want any car related run-ins with the cops or inju
 ries. Or feel free to pass out on the floor or couch.\n<bR><br>\n****Some l
 ibations will be provided\, but it’s a good idea to BYO. Especially if you 
 want something you really enjoy!
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T052122Z
LOCATION:804 s. rogers
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:7th annual winter solstice celebration
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
