DESCRIPTION:A Night of Tango - more than music and dance – an authentic cul
 tural experience you just can’t miss.\n\nStarting with a one-hour concert/s
 how\, the Tangamente ensemble will play a gorgeous selection of the tango r
 epertory\, interpreted by the world-renowned tenor Carlos Montané\, and by 
 Yuriria Rodríguez. This will be a rare opportunity for audiences to see and
  hear a bandoneón – the tango instrument per excellence.\n\nThe Bloomington
  Argentine Tango Organization (BATO) will dance to the evening’s music\, an
 d show the public what tango dance is all about. Following the intermission
 \, the evening will feature a Milonga\, in other words\, a dance event for 
 the audience. Tangamente will play live for those who dance or would like t
 o be introduced to this unique dance. Instructors and advanced dancers from
  BATO will be on the dance floor helping first-timers with the basic steps.
  A Night of Tango\, and its cathartic essence\, will restore our souls and 
 be a night to remember!\n\nTickets available at (812) 323-3020 or online at
 :\n\nhttps://www.efoliotickets.com/FolioProd/PickEvent.aspx?VId=19&EventId=
 09621\n\n$12 Student\, $20 General Admission\n\nTANGAMENTE’s members:\nSing
 er: Yuriria Rodríguez\nViolins: Laura Rubio and Daniel Stein\nBandoneón: Va
 leriano Fernandez\nCello: André Micheletti\nGuitar: Guido Sánchez\nContraba
 ss: Michael Mendelson\nPiano and Direction: Alfredo Minetti\n\nTangamente i
 s also available for concerts and to play live at milongas in the Midwest a
 nd beyond.\n\nArrangements are by:\n- Norberto Vogel: http://www.vogel.com.
 ar/\n- Alfredo Minetti\n- André Micheletti
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T052423Z
LOCATION: Buskirk-Chumley Theater
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:A Night of Tango
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
