DESCRIPTION:A SUNNY DAY IN GLASGOW\nat The Bishop\nWed November 18\n9pm\n$7
 \n21+\n\nPitchfork\n"8.3 - ...pop music masterfully puzzled together...from
  a group of writers strong enough to keep you humming and courageous enough
  to make you guess."\n\nBBC\n"Second album Ashes Grammar is a raising of th
 eir game\; a seamless\, symphonic 22 tracks that twist and glitter like a l
 ake of pristine morning mist. In effect one continuous movement of music\, 
 it has definition nonetheless\, the swirl of floaty electronics\, warm psyc
 hedelia...every so often crystallising into something approaching a pop son
 g...The artisan level of songcraft poured in is quite staggering."\n\nCoke 
 Machine Glow\n"88%...The songs hum like electricity and thump like groundsw
 ells\, surprising and shifting with innovative pacing and dynamics. But the
 y also sound natural and unhurried\, seamlessly patched...A Sunny Day in Gl
 asgow are writing years ahead of where they should be for such a young band
 \, forming gargantuan records of consistently enjoyable and inventive melod
 ic rock...Ashes is A Sunny Day’s stripes\, their first truly great album of
  scope. If it’s any indication the group’s potential scales enormous. "\n\n
 www.myspace.com/sunnydayinglasgow
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T051839Z
LOCATION:The Bishop
SEQUENCE:2
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:A SUNNY DAY IN GLASGOW
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
