CREATED:20090825T131853Z
DESCRIPTION:$5\n\nA hot and sweaty dance party for the 18+ fare looking to 
 cut a rug and enjoy the best from electro\, disco\, house\, hip-hop\, Brazi
 lian Baile and everything from here to Europe.\n\n\nAbout DJ DEMCHUK\n\nChi
 cago\, IL - DJ Demchuk is a FreeForm DJ whose music selection runs the genr
 e gamut\, grabbing Brazilian Funk\, Baltimore Booty Beats\, classic Soul br
 eaks\, and Electro cuts to create the perfect party atmosphere wherever he 
 performs.\n\nDJ Demchuk is resident DJ every Tuesday at Liar's Club\, locat
 ed at 1665 W Fullerton Ave.\n\nFor a Full Schedule of DJ Demchuk sets\, vis
 it his blog at\n\nhttp://www.djdemchuk.blogspot.com\n\nDJ Demchuk also host
 s the monthly End Of The World Dance Party happening the third Thursday of 
 every month at LAVA\, 1270 N Milwaukee Ave. featuring Live music and upper 
 echelon DJs and is in conjunction with Novem Studios' Hot Wax.\n\nVisit htt
 p://www.myspace.com/freeformshuffle for more information.\n\nDownload DJ De
 mchuk's mix of Brazilian Funk\, recorded LIVE on WZRD Chicago 88.3 FM and c
 heck out his interview with the Post Music blog here -\n\nhttp://www.postmu
 sic.org/wordpress/?p=1749\n\nDownload DJ Demchuk's JUKE Mix and read his in
 terview with Novem Studios here -\n\nhttp://novemlife.com/sounds/dj-demchuk
 \n\nAbout Thomas Crown Affair:\n\nNot very often does a DJ tag team come ac
 ross and melt faces by utilizing all genres of music in short bursts. The T
 homas Crown Affair are club-bangers that have been turning out parties and 
 specialize in keeping the sweat dripping. Comprised of DJs Phenom and Every
 thing Continues the collective recently performed with Wale and Colin Munro
 e on their Attention Deficit Tour stop in Bloomington\, Indiana on 4-20-09.
  They also recently performed at the Oaks Party Kentucky Derby Weekend alon
 gside established acts like Bird Peterson and Rob Threezy! If you get the c
 hance to catch these guys in your city do not miss out on the opportunity b
 efore they start playing sold-out clubs!\n\nAbout Andy D:\n\nAndy D fancies
  himself the anachronistic love child of Punky Brewster and Lee Van Cleef –
  the perfect amalgam of a fictional rogue and a real-life badass. He plays 
 music this like he lives life and it sounds like Andrew WK meets Grand Mast
 er Melle Mel or Like Prince if he couldn’t sing that well and if he weren’t
  a hyper-talented multi-instrumentalist. This is what his music is all abou
 t: part epicurean hip-hop-dance songs and part sincere dance rock songs\, b
 eing eclectic and catchy is the only goal. “God Loves Drunk Chicks” is a in
 fectious dance ditty lamenting date rape culture and “Just Push Play” is a 
 witty indictment of “the next big thing” trend in the music industry and po
 p culture in general (both tracks are from the debut album Choose Your Perv
 ersion). This is rap but not hip-hop. It rocks but it's not rap-rock. These
  songs are meaningful party songs but maximized! Andy D bends the genres bu
 t his influences are pretty apparent. And people take notice where ever he 
 goes. From rapping about having sex with Werewolves to singing about knife 
 fights in a roller rink\, no subject is taboo in an Andy D song\; and he ge
 ts raunchy with it. Half of the fun of Andy D is hearing what he will say n
 ext… the other half is dancing. Welcome to your new addiction!
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T052200Z
LOCATION:The Bishop
SEQUENCE:2
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:18+ DANCE PARTY!!! Demchuk! Thomas Crown affair! Andy D!  
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
