DESCRIPTION:Sections of the internationally celebrated AIDS Memorial Quilt 
 – the 54-ton\, handmade tapestry commemorating more than 91\,000 lives lost
  to AIDS – will be on display November 11-15 at Alumni Hall in the Indiana 
 Memorial Union in Bloomington. The exhibit of 65 squares (520 panels) will 
 be the largest AIDS Memorial Quilt display in Indiana history. Admission is
  free.\n\nAt 5pm\, there will be a reception held for the art photography e
 xhibit\, "Facing HIV/AIDS in the Heartland" by John Gevers of NEW MEDIA BRE
 W Inc
