UID:fmbm4lg6rmlr1kvgrh7fsvffqg@google.com
CREATED:20100125T160418Z
DESCRIPTION:EARLY SHOW this FRIDAY the 29th 7pm @ THE BISHOP: YER MOM LIKES
  TO PARTY 2010 - Featuring The Jefferson St Parade Band\, Smedley Jergins\,
  DM Stith\, and Community Currency (Matt Romy's new band) - It's a benefit 
 to help Ben's Mother continue to pay her mortgage and stay afloat financial
 ly while she wades through the drawn out Social Security Disability process
 . We are told there will be a decision in the next 4 months). Come enjoy th
 e music and buy a cookie\, cupcake\, etc.. The show will be over in time fo
 r the Ponyboy show that night at 11. Thanks\, read below for a short summat
 ion of Mom's situation...\n\nFurther Background:\n\nFour years ago\, my mom
  Deb received a Mild Traumatic Brain Injury after being rear-ended in her c
 ar by a 17-year old on his cell phone. Since that time\, she has had a long
  and arduous journey through the medical\, insurance\, social services\, an
 d legal systems. Before this accident\, my mom had a full work life\, maint
 ained her rural home and property\, came to my concerts\, cheered me on in 
 my musical endeavors\, advocated for green building in our area\, and was t
 ireless in her efforts to build awareness about the genocide in Darfur. She
 's the bomb.\nLast May she went through a trial to try to get a settlement 
 from the young guy's car insurance company: She won\, but the settlement is
  so small that the money has gone to her lawyers and her insurance company 
 (for past medical bills).\nSo we are picking up where we left off in August
 ! This is the return to a series of parties/concerts to help her with her m
 ortgage and monthly bills\, to keep her afloat as we try to get something e
 lse figured out. Thanks in advance for any help\, donations\, or ideas that
  you can send our way during this process. Now let's party!\n\nSincerely\, 
 Ben Fowler
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T052348Z
LOCATION:The Bishop
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Yer Mom Likes to Party
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
