DESCRIPTION:Rhino's Youth Center and All Ages Club presents the second annu
 al Rhino's GuitArt Auction.\n\nTen great Bloomington artists were given ele
 ctric guitars and asked to transform them into works of art that are also f
 unctional musical instruments. Come see these one-of-a-kind creations. Hear
  each piece played by talented local musicians. Or make a bid and you could
  take one of these home as your very own.\n\nFeaturing art by Sam Bartlett\
 , Mike Cagle\, Brad Fugate\, Lindsay Hine\, Jenny Kander\, Kurt Larsen\, MB
  Roska\, Matt Traughber\, Anna Witte\, and one of Rhino's own young artists
 .\n\nFeaturing music by Andy Cobine\, Jim Krause\, Jim Sprague\, Chris Gaal
 \, Ron Plecher\, and others.\n\nFeaturing tasty snacks from Finch's\, Mothe
 r Bear's\, FoodWorks\, Malibu\, Bombay House\, Bobby's Too\, and others.\n\
 nTickets are $10 in advance or $15 at the door. Advance tickets are availab
 le at Rhino's\, 331 S. Walnut Street. For more information\, call (812) 333
 -3430 or visit http://www.rhinosyouthcenter.org/\n\nAll proceeds from the G
 uitArt auction go to support Rhino's Youth Center after-school programs. Rh
 ino's offers innovative and successful programs which allow youth to use th
 eir own unique voices through a variety of media\, including video and radi
 o production\, a monthly print magazine\, mural art\, and (new this year) s
 creen printing. Rhino's also provides entertainment and engagement for the 
 youth of our community in a safe environment\, free from alcohol\, tobacco\
 , and other drugs.\n\nNOTE: all photos are from 2008 GuitArt submissions. Y
 ou'll have to come out to the event on Thursday\, April 16\, to see this ye
 ar's models.\n\nAND: Catch a sneak peek of GuitArt during this month's Bloo
 mington Gallery Walk at downtown art galleries on the evening of Friday\, A
 pril 3.
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T052216Z
LOCATION:The Lodge\,  101 E. 6th Street
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Rhino's GuitArt Auction
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
