DESCRIPTION:<br>The IU Libraries Open Tape Clinic hosted by Audio-Video Pre
 servation Services (AVPS) provides an opportunity to learn about archival a
 udio and video tape formats.<br><p>This event\, which is conducted by the t
 ape experts at AVPS\, will feature the following:</p><ul><li>hands-on exper
 ience in handling\, repairing\, cleaning\, baking\, and other physical rest
 oration tasks needed to prepare tapes for digitization</li><li>hands-on dia
 gnosis of preservation problems or potential issues with your tapes</li><li
 >hands-on diagnosis of format characteristics that impact the accuracy and 
 quality of playback including track configuration\, playback speed\, video 
 tracking\, play direction\, and others</li><li>discussions on how the techn
 ology works for both audio and video formats. How is the signal captured on
  tape? How is the signal retrieved?</li><li>advice and recommendations for 
 digitizing and preserving your audio and video tapes</li></ul><p>Bring:</p>
 <ul><li>Tapes that you want to have inspected or wish to learn more about.<
 /li><li>Tapes that you have no idea what (if anything) is recorded on them.
 </li><li>Questions about the various audio and video tape formats that you 
 want answered.</li><li>Or just stop by and try the hands-on activities!</li
 ></ul><br>Free\, all ages
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T185200Z
LOCATION:Herman B Wells Library\, 1320 E 10th St\, Bloomington\, IN 47405\,
  USA
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Open Tape Clinic
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
