DESCRIPTION:The Bishop presents:\n\nTheodore(Moon Jaw Records)\nDust From 1
 000 Years (Moon Jaw Records)\nThe Country Death\n\nMonday. Nov 9 8pm @The B
 ishop\n$5\n18+\n\nTheodore\nhttp://www.myspace.com/theodoreacoustic\n"The S
 t. Louis-based greenbelt-independent-folk-rockers have been madly touring t
 he countryside since 2006 making believers out of all who listen. Theirs is
  a true and haunting sound. It is one that many try to evoke\, but few mana
 ge to accomplish. Only a small\, unfeigned lot have ever been able to chann
 el a sound so eerie\, yet so comforting."\n\nDust from 1000 Years\nhttp://w
 ww.myspace.com/dustfrom1000yrs\n"The music of Dust From 1000 Years is analo
 gous to a wandering mystic giving you the middle finger. This hardworking\,
  Bloomington\, IN band has been making beautifully dirty\, honest\, etherea
 l\, hook-laden\, lo-fi recordings for a good 5 years now. They've toured th
 e countryside quite a few times\, playing intimate\, listener-friendly venu
 es\, and staunchly avoiding atmospheres (i.e. - many bars) where attendees 
 are more concerned with looking cool and getting drunk than with actually l
 istening to the music. It's a telling sign of their commitment to their cra
 ft\, a commitment that has yielded some truly gorgeous songs."\n\nThe Count
 ry Death\nhttp://www.myspace.com/countrydeath\nhttp://www.myspace.com/ryanh
 elling\n\n\nhttp://www.myspace.com/thebishopbar 
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T051852Z
LOCATION:The Bishop
SEQUENCE:2
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Theodore\,  Dust from 1000 Years\, and The Country Death
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
