DESCRIPTION:HOLIDAY HARVEST: A BENEFIT FOR HOOSIER HILLS FOOD BANK AND THE 
 AMERICAN RED CROSS NATIONAL DISASTER RELIEF FUND\n<br><br>\nCarlyn Lindsey 
 & Snake Doctor<Br>\nLeon Chance and the Long Shots<Br>\nUno Moss<Br>\nThrow
 ing Stars<Br>\nmembers of Whippoorwill<Br>\nmembers of The Fatted Calf Stri
 ng Band<Br>\na special holiday set from Rusty Zavitson<Br>\nFriday December
  19th<Br>\n@ Jake's Nightclub & Bar<Br>\n8pm doors<Br>\n$5 or 5 canned good
 s<br>\n<Br><Br>\nThe musical community of Bloomington is coming together th
 is holiday season to give to those most in need with Holiday Harvest\, a be
 nefit concert to collect much needed canned goods for Hoosier Hills Food Ba
 nk and vital funds for the American Red Cross National Relief Fund. The con
 cert takes place Friday\, December 19th at Jake’s Nightclub & Bar located a
 t 419 North Walnut Street. Doors open at 8pm and admission is $5 or 5 canne
 d goods.\n<Br><br>\nHoosier Hills Food Bank collects\, stores\, and distrib
 utes nutritious food products to non-profit organizations\, which provide f
 ree feeding programs that serve both ill and needy families and individuals
  in Monroe\, Martin\, Owen\, Orange\, Brown\, and Lawrence Counties in Cent
 ral Indiana. Since opening in 1982\, over 22 million pounds of food have be
 en distributed and since 1995\, the Meal Share Program has distributed over
  390\,000 healthy meals to members of the community.\n<Br><Br>\nGoverned by
  volunteers and supported by community donations\, the American Red Cross i
 s a nationwide network of 760 chapters and Blood Services regions dedicated
  to saving lives and helping people prevent\, prepare for\, and respond to 
 emergencies. Led by a million volunteers and 30\,000 employees\, the Red Cr
 oss annually mobilizes relief to families affected by more than 75\,000 dis
 asters\, trains almost 12 million people in lifesaving skills\, and exchang
 es more than a million emergency messages for U.S. military service personn
 el and their families. The Red Cross is the largest supplier of blood and b
 lood products to more than 3\,000 hospitals across the nation and also assi
 sts victims of international disasters and conflicts at locations worldwide
 .\n<Br><br>\nChartered in 1917\, the Monroe County Chapter of the American 
 Red Cross serves residents in Monroe and neighboring Owen County 24 hours a
  day\, 365 days a year with disaster relief\, services to Armed Forces\, em
 ergency preparedness and lifesaving programs\, and Lifeline services. We ar
 e located in the heart of Bloomington\, Indiana\, home of Indiana Universit
 y.
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T051848Z
LOCATION:Jake's
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Holiday Harvest: A benefit for Hoosier Hills Food Bank and Red Cros
 s
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
