UID:cf4k8hhbc8kdovat6a7ssp9oq4@google.com
CREATED:20080919T150141Z
DESCRIPTION:Spirit of 68’ Promotions is proud to present Voices and Organs 
 with Mom and Found Objects on September 26th. They will be performing an al
 l ages show at the Cinemat located at 123 S. Walnut St. in Bloomington\, In
 diana. Doors open at 8pm and tickets are $5 and are available at the door.\
 n<br><Br>\nVOICES AND ORGANS (from Sweden\, Western Vinyl Records)\nhttp://
 profile.myspace.com/voicesandorgans\nV&O is a Swedish group of indeterminat
 e membership whose blurred creations are rooted deep in the inexact memorie
 s and perceptions of distant childhood. The 18 songs on the group's debut O
 rphanage were initially conceived as short stories\, and each appears to ha
 ve been assembled directly upon that slim border that separates the impress
 ions of actual past events from those only imagined. And though Voices and 
 Organs' dreamy sound is predominantly centered on electronic instruments an
 d grainy\, processed tape effects\, the album frequently sounds akin to the
  hermetic psych-folk of Finnish artists like Islaja or Lau Nau\, capable of
  instantly transporting the listener into its insular\, alien landscape.” (
 Pitchfork.com)\n<Br><Br>\nMOM (Western Vinyl Records)\nhttp://www.myspace.c
 om/qewmusic\nMom members Joel North and Bruce Blay pride themselves on maki
 ng music that appeals to everyone from teens to North’s 70-year-old dad. Th
 eir music incorporates miscellaneous sounds like ice cubes clattering and c
 handeliers shaking along with cello\, violin and acoustic guitar. They meti
 culously selected “a mound of found sounds and jam session recordings and s
 pending hour upon hour recording\, re-recording\, composing\, mixing\, re-m
 ixing and mastering the six-song masterpiece of Little Brite.” Their OCD-li
 ke perfectionism in recording and practicing pays off as they consistently 
 deliver strikingly beautiful performances.\n<Br><Br>\nFOUND OBJECTS (Bloomi
 ngton)\nhttp://www.myspace.com/foundobjectsisart\nFound Objects (Shut up I 
 love you records) is a musical project from IU Jacobs School of Music stude
 nts Dan Morris Patrick McMinn. “Found Objects strikes a balance between dre
 amy shoegaze landscapes and feedback nightmares. Blissed out\, reverb drenc
 hed vocals meet up with looming keyboard pads. Habit Down the Day's beautif
 ul laptop glitches\, rumbling drum crescendos and warmed up guitar fuzz are
  such a beautiful start for a band destined for great things.” (SU!iLY Reco
 rds)
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T052331Z
LOCATION:The Cinemat
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Voices and Organs\, Mom\, & Found Objects
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
