DESCRIPTION:Brining a little bit of Hollywood to the small town. Support th
 e MCHA and the animals they work to protect by attending Hollywoof\, the th
 ird annual MCHA benefit auction gala.\n\nThis year’s event will feature sev
 eral hundred unique live and silent auction items including one of a kind b
 ehind the scenes experiences at Bloomington hidden treasures\, lunches with
  Bloomington celebrities\, sports memorabilia and autographed items from Ho
 llywood stars including Joan Crawford.\n\nSilent auctions feature a wide va
 riety of items donated from local businesses and individuals\, sure to find
  a match for any and all interests. Guests to Hollywoof can also stop on th
 e red carpet to have their picture snapped paparazzi style as a keepsake of
  the evening.\n\nAttendees will enjoy a gourmet\, California inspired veget
 arian and vegan meal artfully prepared by The Cake and The Caterer includin
 g appetizers\, delectable dessert\, complimentary Oliver Winery wine and ca
 sh bar. Even take home your own personal box of designer chocolates from Bl
 u Boy Café and Cakery.\n\nThis is a sell out event with tickets going quick
 ly.\n\nTickets can be purchased by visiting www.monroehumane.org/hollywoof 
 or call 812.333.6242.\n\nTickets are $50 each ($30 tax deductible)\n\nTable
 s of 8 are $400\, which includes $40 in "Woof Bucks" good towards auction i
 tems. ($240 tax deductible)\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T051855Z
LOCATION:KRC catering\,   216 South College Ave
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:HOLLYWOOF
TRANSP:OPAQUE
