DESCRIPTION:Reading and Signing with legendary comic artist John Porcellino
  of "King-Cat Comics"  (click here for website)\n\nJOHN PORCELLINO was born
  in Chicago\, in 1968\, and has been writing\, drawing\, and publishing min
 icomics\, comics\, and graphic novels for over twenty-five years. His celeb
 rated self-published series King-Cat Comics\, begun in 1989\, has inspired 
 a generation of cartoonists. Diary of a Mosquito Abatement Man\, a collecti
 on of King-Cat stories about Porcellino’s experiences as a pest control wor
 ker\, won an Ignatz Award in 2005\, and Perfect Example\, first published i
 n 2000\, chronicles his struggles with depression as a teenager. King-Cat C
 lassix\, published in 2007\, is a comprehensive overview of the zine's firs
 t fifty issues\, and his most recent book\, Thoreau at Walden\, is a poetic
  expression of the great philosopher’s experience and ideals. According to 
 cartoonist Chris Ware\, "John Porcellino's comics distill\, in just a few l
 ines and words\, the feeling of simply being alive."\n\nPorcellino's work h
 as been translated into French\, German\, Spanish\, Swedish\, Italian\, and
  Korean. He currently lives in Denver with his wife Misun\, and two Skweezi
 l-Cats named Liz and Charlie.\n\nWith a special musical performance by Patr
 ick Porter
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T051859Z
LOCATION:Boxcar Books
SEQUENCE:2
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Book Reading: John Porcellino of "King-Cat Comics"
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
