DTSTAMP:20260905T041548Z
UID:v8mbpqo7vdkoatjirh0sb8pbjk@google.com
CREATED:20100609T014320Z
DESCRIPTION:DESTINY & ESTHER’S MIDWEST MUSEUM of NATURAL HISTORY\nInteracti
 ve Midwestern-themed photography and crafts comedy happening debuts in Bloo
 mington.\nBLOOMINGTON\, INDIANA—Destiny and Esther’s Midwest Museum of Natu
 ral History—a Mountain Dew-drenched visual and interactive ethnographic exp
 loration of the American heartland’s most revered archetypes\, institutions
  and cultural mores—debuts in Bloomington from 5:00-10:00 p.m. on June 12th
  at 916 S. Rogers Street. Images focusing on adventurous misfits Destiny an
 d Esther\, as captured by local photographer Natasha Komoda\, will be on di
 splay\, along with other exhibits\, such as: dioramas\, a curiosity cabinet
 \, taxidermy\, nature exhibits\, religious iconography and other hand-craft
 ed arts and oddities. Destiny and Esther will be available for questions an
 d to serve bottomless bowls of corn chips.\nKomoda\, an enthusiastic admire
 r of Jane Goodall’s brand of qualitative anthropology\, states that after a
  long\, trust-building courtship\, she was permitted to photographically do
 cument Destiny and Esther’s peculiar\, gauche behaviors in a variety of nat
 ural settings and classic heartland contexts. The resulting previously unre
 corded images “will send shockwaves through Bloomington and beyond\,” state
 s Komoda\, “they really are startling…groundbreaking even.” In between bite
 s of undercooked Hamburger Helper\, Destiny and Esther exclaim in unison\, 
 “We’s real excitable to be in a pitcher show!”\nThe museum also boasts a la
 rge collection of inexplicably old photographs—indeed\, some apparently tak
 en during the Mesozoic Era\, predating the invention of cameras by about 65
 .5 million years—generously donated by the two subjects\, giving their scie
 nce-defying existences much-needed context. Indeed\, the collection\, Komod
 a asserts\, “will leave paleontologists and theologians alike befuddled…and
  maybe a little scared.” Examples of Destiny and Esther’s baroque aesthetic
  will also be in abundance in the form of lovingly handmade art works as ex
 ecuted by the wacky duo and their stable of sympathetic “friends.”\nDestiny
  and Esther’s Midwest Museum of Natural History invites anyone with an irre
 verent sense of humor to its grand opening on June 12th from 5:00-10:00 p.m
 . The museum will also be open on Saturday\, June 19th from 1:00-5:00 p.m. 
 and again on Sunday\, June 20th from 1:00-5:00 p.m. Please visit http://smo
 oveg.net/Site/Destiny-n-Esther.html or search for “Destiny & Esther’s Midwe
 st Museum of Natural History” on Facebook for more information.
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T052047Z
LOCATION:916 S. Rogers st
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Art Opening: DESTINY & ESTHER’S MIDWEST MUSEUM of NATURAL HISTORY
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
