DESCRIPTION:In honor of Women’s History Month the Monroe County History Cen
 ter is hosting a:\n<br><br>\nCRAFTACULAR\nCraft•ac•u•lar \\kraf-ˈta-kyə-lər
 \\\n1: An event where people come together to delight in all things craft. 
 2: When something is both crafty and spectacular.\n<br><Br>\nThis spectacul
 ar craft event will have live entertainment\, hands-on craft demonstrations
 \, make-and-take craft creations labs\, free museum admission\, and will se
 rve as a place for the community to come together while crafting.\n<Br><br>
 \nThe entire day will be feature free museum admission\, craft demonstratio
 ns\, information tables\, and hands-on learning opportunities. don't miss t
 he live performance by folk singer/songwriter Naomi Rae of the Craft Creati
 on Lab: Crocheted Chunky Bangles.\n<br><br>\nEvent schedule will be made av
 ailable both here on Facebook and at www.monroehistory.org\n<Br><br>\nSpons
 ored by: Boxcar Books & Community Center.\n<Br><br>\n***We Want You***\nThe
  History Center is looking for local crafters to practice their craft(s) at
  the Craftacular on Sunday\, March 29. For more information\, please contac
 t Lisa M. Simmons at education@monroehistory.org.\n<Br><br>\n***Don’t Miss*
 **\nLive performance by Naomi Rae—details to come.
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T052031Z
LOCATION:The Monroe County History Center\, 202 E. 6th St.
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Craftacular
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
