UID:s8q0atme44qonhmrjdt64tv05s@google.com
CREATED:20100129T165445Z
DESCRIPTION:Annie Palmer's tales of lost love\, long travels and hard night
 s recall the country and americana influences of her Tennessee upbringing\,
  as well as the folk and noise sounds of her geographical contemporaries in
  her current home of Ypsilanti\, Michigan.  When she's not working on her o
 wn material she frequently makes time with dozen of other musical projects\
 , including tours and guest appearances with the likes of Castanets\, Tiger
  Saw\, Brown Bird\, Phosphorescent\, Patrick Elkins\, White Pines\, Canada 
 and many others.\n\n"Like being the only audience at a house concert in you
 r bedroom\, all snuggly and warm under the covers." -Songs: Illinois\n"She 
 writes lyrics that make you want to savor each syllable." -Teeter Talk\n"An
 nie breaks the heart\, and reconstructs it at the same time...this is as go
 od as indie folk singer/songwriter music can get." -Ear Drugs\n"Annie Palme
 r manages to wring every ounce of impact from a slow-mo banjo and a creakin
 g violin\, her voice having great charm\, and when someone adds a few notes
  of glockenspiel it sends a shiver through me - I feel I could fall instant
 ly in love with her\, and even the violin seems to pine for her."  -America
 na UK\n"Annie Palmer is someone I want to know...criminally underplayed." -
 Slowcoustic\n\nAnnie's website: http://www.myspace.com/anniepalmermusic\n--
 \n\n\nAnna Vogelzang\, unavoidably soulful singer/songwriter and newly-tran
 splanted midwesterner sings the best kind of songs\, the ones about feeling
 s. She has shared stages with awesome folks like: Regina Spektor\, Franz Ni
 colay (The Hold Steady)\, Mirah (K Recs)\, Wye Oak (Merge Records)\, Casey 
 Dienel (White Hinterland)\, Amanda Palmer\, Kyp Malone (TV on the Radio)\, 
 and many other talented friends & mentors. She also spent some quality time
  performing as a vocalist with The Dresden Dolls around the country\, notab
 ly at Lollapalooza 2006 & on NPR's World Cafe.\nAnna is gearing up for the 
 release of her 5th solo album\, "Paper Boats"\, out on the Slothtrop Music 
 label in Madison\, WI. After shifting from her first two albums' lush studi
 o arrangements to a more DIY at-home & hand-pressed aesthetic\, Anna has st
 ruck a blanace of studio richness & raw\, fun musicianship in Paper Boats. 
 She is embarking on her 7th DIY tour in under two years this February and w
 ill continue setting up small\, intimate tours until her 98 Nissan falls ap
 art.\n\n"Her voice will blanket you with awe... Do whatever you can to see 
 her live." - The Deli Magazine\, Chicago\n“Anna Vogelzang is one of the pro
 mising young female artists who puts her money where her mouth is. This gir
 l won’t stop until she gets the attention she deserves\, and believe me\, s
 he deserves it." – Amanda Palmer\, The Dresden Dolls\n"Pittsburgh's indie-f
 olk scene said goodbye to one of its brightest singer-songwriters when Anna
  Vogelzang took off for Chicago." - Pittsburgh Post-Gazette\n"Combine sweet
 \, early-jazz warbling\, classic female singer-songwriter acoustics\, girl-
 with-a-guitar aesthetics\, and indie-folk quirk (imagine Kimya Dawson if sh
 e could really sing) with a dash of slightly angsty girl-rock (Ani DiFranco
  if she’d mellow out)\, and you’ll have an inkling of the unique style cult
 ivated by vocalist Anna Vogelzang." - Brick Weekly\, Richmond\, VA\n\nAnna'
 s full press kit: http://www.sonicbids.com/theanna
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T051828Z
LOCATION:The Bishop
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Early Show: Annie Palmer (Castanets) & Anna Vogelzang
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
