DESCRIPTION:his is the one you should show up to...\n\nDrekka: myspace.com/
 drekka\nAdrienne Anemone: myspace.com/adrienneanemone\ne.p. hall: myspace.c
 om/ephallmusic\n\nSome words about Adrienne and her bands...\n\nBitch Magaz
 ine The Tuna Helpers I'll Have What She's Having (Web of Mimicry)\n"Though 
 Adrienne may race around stage\, kicking and screaming\, her piercing eyes 
 bulging out of her head as she releases a glorious yowl\, you'd somehow fee
 l at ease leaving her with your children."\n\n\nVenus Online\, December 200
 5\n"...Adrienne's quivering\, soaring words melt against cascading guitar\,
  cello\, and Bethany's tinkling keyboards\, creating a dramatically melodic
  mood."\n\n\nSplendid Magazine The TunaHelpers: "I'll Have What She's Havin
 g"\n"...the key element\, however\, is Adrienne's alluring voice. She's cla
 ssically trained\, and can carry a tune as easily as she can stalk your spe
 akers with her siren-like performance. Weak-minded musical patrons beware: 
 it only takes a few notes to fall under the Helpers' hex."\n\n\nKNOX NEWS (
 Knoxville\, Tennessee)\n"...weaving gothic tales of toys gone wild and kitt
 ens and children in peril. And all the while\, strings and various "instrum
 ental affectations" escort Adrienne through mad-girl vocal flips and operat
 ic swells."\n\n\nNashville Scene: The TunaHelpers\n"...they recognize that 
 storybooks hinge on nightmarish fears and human yearnings-something that co
 mes through most keenly in the ache of Adrienne the Anemone's vocals."\n\n\
 nGirlstown Productions FracturedFairytales from the Sea (Interview)\n"Adrie
 nne's stunning voice soars above lush\, sparkling melodies and jagged guita
 r\, sometimes from the center of the stage\, her wild eyes shifting around 
 the audience\, or hidden behind a two-headed puppet..."
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T052033Z
LOCATION:The Cinemat
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Drekka\, e.p. hall\, Adrienne Anemone
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
