DESCRIPTION:The Cinemat and Spirit of '68 Promotions are proud to present:\
 n\nHere We Go Magic (Luke Temple)\nCallers (Western Vinyl Records)\nVollmar
 \n@ The Cinemat\nMarch 11\, 2009\n8pm\n$6\nALL AGES!\n\nHERE WE GO MAGIC\nh
 ttp://www.myspace.com/herewegomagic\nLuke Temple is the brilliant and under
 -appreciated songwriter who has been lauded by indie rock heavy-weights (Su
 fjan Stevens and Ben Gibbard have both been quoted\, for example) as having
  one of the most beautiful voices in pop music. Here We Go Magic is the nam
 e of Temple's new band\, which just released a new record through Western V
 inyl Records.\n\nCALLERS\nhttp://www.myspace.com/callers\n"Upon listening t
 o Fortune in the car on one of those days last month when the global econom
 y looked like it was going to collapse\, I actually had to shut it off beca
 use it got to be too much. And of course\, that's meant as high praise."\n–
  Pitchfork\n\nVOLLMAR\nhttp://www.vollmarmusic.com\nWest Virginia native an
 d Bloomington\, Indiana resident Justin Vollmar has been making leftfield f
 olk-rock for longer than most. He's toured the western world over with like
 -minded artists such as Half-Handed Cloud and Elephant Micah\, and released
  a small library of critically acclaimed home recordings both as a solo art
 ist and band (with brother/drummer Nathan and David Brant on bass). A mains
 tay in the Bloomington scene\, Vollmar has also lent his talents to countle
 ss local bands (Mt. Gigantic\, Bronze Float\, Prayer Breakfast\, etc.). !Vi
 va Vollmar!
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T052208Z
LOCATION:Cinemat
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Here We Go Magic\, Callers\, Vollmar
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
