DESCRIPTION:Join the Local Growers Guild in this very exciting night to vie
 w the\ndocumentary\, FRESH\, produced and directed by anna Sofia joane.\n\n
 Friday\, October 23 at 7pm at Boxcar Books located at 508 E. 6th Street\nin
  Bloomington.  $$ TBA.  Discussion will follow the screening.\n\nSynopsis o
 f the movie from the official website\, www.freshthemovie.com:\n\n"FRESH ce
 lebrates the farmers\, thinkers and business people across\nAmerica who are
  re-inventing our food system. Each has witnessed the\nrapid transformation
  of our agriculture into an industrial model\, and\nconfronted the conseque
 nces: food contamination\, environmental\npollution\, depletion of natural 
 resources\, and morbid obesity. Forging\nhealthier\, sustainable alternativ
 es\, they offer a practical vision for\na future of our food and our planet
 .\n\nAmong several main characters\, FRESH features urban farmer and\nactiv
 ist\, Will Allen\, the recipient of MacArthur’s 2008 Genius Award\;\nsustai
 nable farmer and entrepreneur\, Joel Salatin\, made famous by\nMichael Poll
 an’s book\, The Omnivore’s Dilemma\; and supermarket owner\,\nDavid Ball\, 
 challenging our Wal-Mart dominated economy."
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T052354Z
LOCATION:Boxcar Books
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Documentary: FRESH
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
