DESCRIPTION:The School of Fine Arts (SoFA) Gallery at Indiana University is
  pleased to announce Whiskey Tango Foxtrot\, a photography exhibition by As
 hley Gilbertson\, in conjunction with Arts Week. Ashley Gilbertson will giv
 e a lecture on his work Tuesday\, February 24 at 6:00pm in the SoFA Gallery
 . A book signing and opening reception for the exhibition will be held at t
 he SoFA Gallery following his lecture. This exhibition will run from Februa
 ry 24 until March 13th. All events are free and open to the public.\n\nWhis
 key Tango Foxtrot will feature 10 of Gilbertson’s photographs\, chronicling
  America’s early battles in Iraq\, the initial occupation of Baghdad\, the 
 insurgency that erupted shortly afterward\, the dramatic battle to overtake
  Fallujia\, and\, ultimately\, the country’s first national elections. This
  wide-ranging chronicle of the war from the viewpoint of the photographer i
 s the first of its kind. Gilbertson’s narratives convey the exhilaration an
 d terror of photographing war\, as well as the challenges of photojournalis
 m in our age of embedded reporting. The photographs of Whiskey Tango Foxtro
 t depict the full range of human experience called up by the war in Iraq.\n
 \nA photographer for the New York Times\, Newsweek\, and Time\, among other
 s\, Gilbertson will discuss his recent exhibit and book\, Whiskey\, Tango F
 oxtrot: A Photographer’s Chronicle of the Iraq War. Described as “harrowing
  snaphots of the American soul\,” Gilbertson’s book of photographs was chos
 en as a “Best Book of 2007” by Amazon.com. Following the lecture there will
  be a book signing and reception for the photographer.\n\n*Please note loca
 tion change for lecture. It will now be held in the SoFA Gallery at 6 pm.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T052229Z
LOCATION:SoFA Gallery
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Art Lecture: Whiskey Tango Foxtrot: Photographs by Ashley Gilbertso
 n
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
