DESCRIPTION:Irrepressible Urges and The Bishop present:\n\nRICHARD BUCKNER\
 nw/ Old Flames\n@ The Bishop\n123 S. Walnut St. Bloomington\, IN\nTuesday\,
  September 15\n8pm\n$10\n21+\n\nTickets on sale at Landlocked\, TD's\, Busk
 irk Chumley box office\, and online:\nhttp://www.buskirkchumley.org/\n\n\nR
 ICHARD BUCKNER\nhttp://www.mergerecords.com/artists/buckner\n"There are thr
 ee kinds of American folk artists: those who sit\, contented\, on a back po
 rch contemplating America's landscape and ways\; those for whom its landsca
 pe and ways are something to stand against or move boldly through\; and tho
 se whose America is a shadowy\, impressionistic place that moves inside of 
 them. This [latter] is the area that the sombre-voiced Richard Buckner has 
 been exploring since 1984." (Sylvie Simmons\; The Guardian\, 2004)\n\nOLD F
 LAMES\nhttp://www.myspace.com/oldflamesindiana\n"From the ashes of Uvula\, 
 with Members of Magnolia Electric Company\, Sardina\, and Gentleman Caller\
 , comes this thing."\n
