 \nSaturday\, June 26th\n8pm\n18+\n$15 in advance or $18 at the door\n\n*tic
 kets can be purchased at the Bishop\, TD's\, Landlocked\, the Buskirk Chuml
 ey box office\, or online at www.buskirkchumley.org\n\n\n\nTORTOISE\n\nTort
 oise originated in Chicago and the group has been making innovative music s
 ince the early 1990s. The band has released 11 full length albums and numer
 ous singles and EPs. Their latest release\, Beacons of Ancestorship\, is fu
 ll of “nods to techno\, punk\, electro\, lo-fi noise\, cut-up beats\, heavi
 ly processed synths\, and mournful\, elegiac dirges." What makes Tortoise s
 o endearing can be perfectly summated from the group’s MySpace page\, “Almo
 st alone among bands of the last two decades\, Tortoise is a group that res
 ists easy metaphors and analogies\, who can be described as sounding like o
 nly themselves and no one else.”\n\nhttp://www.myspace.com/tortoise\nhttp:/
