DESCRIPTION:HURRAY FOR THE RIFF RAFF\nw/ Naomi Rae & Tiddly Wink Toms'\n@ B
 ear's Place\nWed June 10\n9pm\n$5\n\nHurray For The Riff Raff\nwww.myspace.
 com/hurrayfortheriffraff\n--------------\nHurray for the Riff Raff is a rec
 ent addition to the explosive New Orleans music scene. Birthed in the summe
 r of 2007 and bred in the heat of the crescent city\, Riff Raff carries a s
 ound that has an innovative mixture of Appalachian old time and minor key w
 altzes\, without losing the grittiness of diy folk. The arrangement of Acco
 rdion\, Banjo\, Musical Saw and Upright Bass weaves you through heartbreak 
 and triumph. "Hurray for the Riff-Raff's junkyard folk is stubborn\, melanc
 holy and beautifully played. Alynda Lee sings like Jolie Holland or Leslie 
 Feist\, lit up with sorrows. They are the perfect soundtrack to your Southe
 rn gothic romance\, a junebug serenade\, a two-step bramble-bush waltz. (Se
 an Michaels\, The National Post\, Said the Gramophone)”\n\nNaomi Rae\nwww.m
 yspace.com/naomiraewolsieffer\n--------------\nAfter shyly approaching open
  mics\, standing (sometimes sitting) alone\, Naomi Rae slowly developed a t
 aste for performing the songs she'd been keeping hidden in stairwells and k
 itchens. Now living in Bloomington\, IN\, and reveling in the overwhelming 
 music scene there\, she's working on getting an album together as well as s
 ustaining a band. Most times playing live\, she's accompanied by a young ma
 n with a stand-up bass while she plays her guitar and sings songs about the
  ocean\, relationships\, islands\, and doorways.
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T051843Z
LOCATION:Bear's Place
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Hurray For The Riff Raff
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
