CREATED:20230326T155300Z
DESCRIPTION:"This month’s theme is Rebellion in Ohio! We’ll be highlighting
  2 people:\n\n\nBomani Shakur (Keith Lamar) was sentenced to death after th
 e Lucasville Uprising. In 1993\, hundreds of prisoners revolted against hor
 rific conditions and had control of part of the Southern Ohio Correctional 
 Facility for 11 days\, making demands\, and holding correctional officers h
 ostage. One officer was killed and that killing was pinned on Bomani. He ha
 s spent the last few decades writing\, painting\, and mentoring young peopl
 e. Despite popular calls for his release and exoneration\, Ohio plans to mu
 rder him later this year.\n\nSean Swain is an anarchist prisoner\, jailhous
 e lawyer\, and prolific writer. In 2011\, Sean was accused of affiliation w
 ith a guerilla sabotage movement called the Army of the 12 Monkeys\, who ci
 rculated manuals and propaganda among prisoners. In the following year Ohio
  has continued to harass him\, even sending him to Virginia for a time. He 
 is now back in Youngstown.\n\nWe will also send postcards to jailed forest 
 defenders in Atlanta." \nWrite a letter to an incarcerated person. Stamps\,
  paper\, envelopes\, pens and snacks provided. Send some solidarity.\n\n6:3
 0. Free. All Ages!
LAST-MODIFIED:20230403T142725Z
LOCATION:Vulture Video
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Anarchist Black Cross Monthly Letter Writing
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
