DESCRIPTION:Please join us for an exhibit at Bloomington Clay Studio:\nHype
 rborean\nPaintings and Sculpture by Sarah Pearce\nMarch 6- April 3\nOpening
  Reception March 6 from 5:00-8:00pm\n\nIn this show\, Sarah Pearce\, a Bloo
 mington artist\, strays far\, far North\, beyond the Arctic Circle\, with a
  series of new oil paintings and clay sculptures. Drawing inspiration from 
 the likes of Jacques Cousteau\, Herman Melville\, and mid-century Action pa
 inters\, she explores the relationship between the icy\, light-saturated la
 ndscape and its warm-bodied inhabitants (walruses\, whales\, seals). Pearce
  received her BFA from R.I.S.D. and her MFA from Indiana University in 2008
 . For more information about the artist\, visit http://sarahpearce.blogspot
 .com/\; for more information about (and directions to) Bloomington Clay Stu
 dios\, visit http://bloomingtonclaystudio.com/.\n\nHyperborean: of or perta
 ining to the fabled Hyperboreans\; an inhabitant of the extreme north of th
 e earth.
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T052157Z
LOCATION:6900 E. Gross Ln
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Art Opening: Hyperborean
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
