DESCRIPTION:This 30-minute\, multi-sensory performance piece is a productio
 n of Luminescence Project\, conceived by two IU graduate students\, Mark Do
 erries (School of Music) and Sean Smallman (Theater Department). The piece 
 integrates the light display of the IU Art Museum's Light Totem\, choral mu
 sic performed by an ensemble of IU Jacobs School of Music students\, and th
 eatrical movement performed by students from the IU Theater Department. A f
 ree reception in the Thomas T. Solley Atrium of the Art Museum will follow 
 the performance each evening. This project was made possible with support f
 rom the IU Art Museum's Arc Fund. Co-sponsors include the IU Jacobs School 
 of Music Choral Department and the IU Theatre and Drama Department. 
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T052108Z
LOCATION:IU Art Museum 
