CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20101016T030840Z
DESCRIPTION:Theoretically\, we're all afforded certain rights when dealing 
 with the cops or the courts. In practice\, however these rights are often n
 eglected or ignored. The grand jury witness learns this more blatantly than
  many who get tangled in the net of the "criminal justice system". What hap
 pens behind the closed doors of the grand jury room? From the knock-n-talk 
 to incarceration\, the CLDC will walk you down the hidden path of the grand
  jury witness. In the wake of animal rights activist Jordan Halliday facing
  years in prison for refusing to testify\, we present Know-Your-Grand Jury-
 Resistance training\, a presentation on the history of grand juries\, and a
  concluding discussion on how cooperation with the State affects us all. Th
 is event is apart of a call-out for solidarity with grand jury resistor and
  Utah animal rights activist Jordan Halliday. On October 19\, 2010\, Jordan
  will be sentenced to up to 2 years in a federal facility for refusing to t
 estify before a grand jury. Jordan faces as much prison time as those he wa
 s brought to testify against.\n\nPlus\, there will be free food.\n\nKnow Yo
 ur (Grand Jury) Resistance\n\nTuesday\, October 19th @ 6:30pm\n\nBoxcar Boo
 ks\, 408 E. 6th St. Bloomington\, Indiana\n\nIncludes:\nKnow Your Grand Jur
 y Rights Training from Civil Liberties Defense Center\nA Rad(ical) History 
 of Grand Juries\nA Reading of Post-Sentencing Statement from Jordan \nA Dis
 cussion on Cooperation\n\nFor More Information Go To:\n\nhttp://cldc.org/ab
 outgj.html\nhttp://www.supportjordan.com/\nhttp://www.boxcarbooks.org/News\
 n\nParking is available behind the bookstore.\n\n----\n\nCALL OUT FOR SOLID
 ARITY WITH GRAND JURY RESISTOR JORDAN HALLIDAY\n\nSALT LAKE CITY\, Utah  --
 -  On October 19\, 2010\, Jordan Halliday\, a Utah animal rights activist\,
  will be sentenced for refusing to testify before a grand jury.  The prosec
 utor is asking for 15-21 months\; consequently\, Jordan faces as much priso
 n time as those he was brought to testify against. We are calling for solid
 arity actions from October 16th to 19th to show support for Jordan and all 
 grand resistors.\n\nIn March 2009\, Jordan was subpoenaed to federal grand 
 jury investigating a series of mink liberations in Utah. He asserted his 5t
 h Amendment right against self-incrimination. The court jailed Jordan for n
 early 4 months under civil contempt of court. in an effort to compel him to
  testify. The day after Jordan refused to testify\, the grand jury indicted
  Alex Hall and William 'BJ' Viehl under the Animal Enterprise Terrorism Act
 .\n\nThe week following his first grand jury appearance Jordan (still in ja
 il) received a second subpoena\, which he again refused. While in jail\, Jo
 rdan also received thousands of letters of support from all over the world\
 , made friends\, and confidently reflected on his decision not to cooperate
 .\n\nUpon release the court charged Jordan with federal criminal contempt o
 f court\, to which he pleaded guilty in August of this year.\n\nThere are n
 o sentencing guidelines for criminal contempt. However\, the prosecution is
  trying to follow the guidelines of "obstruction of justice" and pursuing a
 n enhancement. These guidelines have a maximum of 2 years and allow the pro
 secutor to ask for an egregious sentence of between 15 and 21 months. Compa
 ratively\, BJ and Alex were sentenced to 24 months and 21 months respective
 ly.\n\nJordan is the first dissident in more than 2 decades to be charged w
 ith criminal contempt of court after already serving time for civil contemp
 t for the same act of recalcitrance.\n\nOver the past 20 years many animal 
 rights and otherwise rad kids have suffered subpoenas and coercive incarcer
 ation\, but rarely for more than a few weeks. But at present we are experie
 ncing an increase of pressure. Shortly after Jordan's incarceration an Iowa
  grand jury subpoenaed Carrie Feldman and Scott Demuth\, and held them in c
 ivil contempt for four months. Fortunately\, neither Carrie nor Scott has b
 een charged with criminal contempt.\n\nJordan's sentencing is set for Octob
 er 19th\, 2010\, 2 p.m.\, at the Frank E. Moss Federal Courthouse at 350 So
 uth Main Street in Salt Lake City\, Utah. We encourage any one in Salt Lake
  to attend this hearing (in conservative dress).\n\nLastly\, Jordan's heari
 ng presents only one moment for convergence\, and we call out for an erupti
 on of many more moments\, for acts of recalcitrance anywhere and everywhere
 \, for actions that show solidarity with grand jury resistance from October
  16-19\, 2010.\n\nFor More Information Go To:\nhttp://www.supportjordan.com
 \n\n\nhttp://www.facebook.com/event.php?eid=159891910705997
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T052027Z
LOCATION:Boxcar Books\, 408 E. 6th St.\, Bloomington\, IN
SEQUENCE:876985
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Know Your (Grand Jury) Resistance: in solidarity with Jordan Hallid
 ay!
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
