DESCRIPTION:Dear friends\,\n\ne.p. hall is *finally* releasing a full lengt
 h project: Mommy Crow\, after three years since the previous release\, The 
 Edge the Middle.\n\nTo celebrate things\, we're having a (free!) CD release
  show at the Bishop with The Native Young and more to be announced. Saturda
 y November 21. Save the date\, please. We really hope lots of people will c
 ome.\n\nAs my compulsive nature would dictate\, we've been keeping copious 
 records of our movements. You can satisfy voyeuristic desires here:\nhttp:w
 ww.ephall.com/goingson.html\n\nAlso\, to promote the show and release we've
  delivered a bunch of copies of The Edge the Middle (2006) to neat local pl
 aces to be given away on the free (e.g.\, The Bishop\, Landlocked\, T.D.'s\
 , Curiodrome). So if you don't have the last CD already\, now is the time t
 o stop by one of those places and pick it up recession-style.\n\nMore detai
 ls will be added as they work themselves out.\n\nYour friends\,\nElise (and
  Andy) / e.p. hall\n\nQuick links for listening:\nThe Native Young ( www.my
 space.com/thenativeyoung )\ne.p. hall ( www.myspace.com/ephallmusic )\n
