BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Let's Go! Bloomington
DTSTART:20080924T010000Z
DTEND:20080924T033000Z
DTSTAMP:20260905T041548Z
UID:ipl37rkbr1bb5elp4jc1ftqilg@google.com
CREATED:20080919T150548Z
DESCRIPTION:THE PACK A.D.\nhttp://www.myspace.com/thepackad\nhttp://thepack
 afterdeath.com/\nBecky Black and Maya Miller of The Pack A.D. mean business
 . They take life on the road\, Civil War stories\, coffee and cigarettes\, 
 stir them into a vicious concoction of garage rock and Jack Daniels and the
 n boil it alive in the blues. Tintype\, their debut album\, is 17 tracks of
  Becky and Maya rockin'\, handing out their blues the way they know best - 
 loud\, edgy and unforgiving. You can't help but respect their blunt\, no bu
 llshit approach. Enough with the flashy lightening-bolt haircuts of today\;
  The Pack A.D. is here to take over the world\, one town (and one cup of co
 ffee) at a time.\n<br><br>\nHARD CANDY HEARTS\nhttp://www.hardcandyhearts.c
 om/\nhttp://www.myspace.com/hardcandyhearts\nThe hard candy hearts started 
 by Birch as a one-man-band a few years back. He would play house parties\, 
 on the tops of buildings or on the street just to say he could. The shows g
 ot stranger and everyone thought it was a joke. “The audience never knew wh
 at to make of a guy with tambourines on his feet and a harmonica in his mou
 th screaming at the top of his lungs and playing sounds you only hear on me
 rzbow records while rolling about on the floor kissing everyone.”\n<Br><Br>
 \nAfter some time Birch got a drummer actually a new drummer every show for
  3 shows. “ I think they were into it but in the end no one wanted to play 
 2 piece Noise/Garage Rock until it was cool to like the White Stripes. “It 
 was good and bad\, good because before that people never gave us a chance b
 ut after everyone just compared us.”\n<Br><Br>\nBut the Hearts just kept do
 ing what they do. Rock. The Nicotones guitarist Tre joined the band on drum
 s and they recorded an album called “I’ll show you mine if you show me your
 s” Recorded in 2 hours on a 4 track they only used 4 tracks total. “We didn
 ’t cheat and put bass on like some bands would its just Guitar-Vocals-Harmo
 nica-Drums”.\n<Br><Br>\nThey would always keep coming up with something to 
 be annoyed or excited about\, whether it was smashing vinyl in-between song
 s\, throwing candy and firecrackers at the audience or shows ending in viol
 ence. You would always See something that you wouldn’t forget”\n<Br><Br>\nE
 DDY (from PHANTOM CRUISERS)\nhttp://www.myspace.com/phantomcruisers\n<Br><B
 r>\n9pm - $4 - All Ages w/ beers for those of age
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T051828Z
LOCATION:The Cinemat
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:THE PACK A.D. & HARD CANDY HEARTS
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
