BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Let's Go! Bloomington
DTSTART:20090416T010000Z
DTEND:20090416T040000Z
DTSTAMP:20260905T041548Z
UID:uqm694a0nmpp7uv8td7veg3ac0@google.com
CREATED:20090323T141241Z
DESCRIPTION:Spirit of '68 presents...\n\nChain and the Gang (featuring Ian 
 Svenonius)\nThe Hive Dwellers (featuring Calvin Johnson)\nCity Center\n@ Th
 e Russian Recording\nWednesday April 15\n9pm\n$8 adv/$10 door\nall ages\n\n
 Chain and the Gang (featuring Ian Svenonius)\nwww.myspace.com/chainandthega
 ng\n--------------\nIan Svenonius … a.k.a. Name Names is now with CHAIN and
  The GANG. They are tired of liberty … tired of being free … they say "if t
 his is 'freedom' then lock me up and throw away the key."\n\n"DOWN WITH LIB
 ERTY … UP WITH CHAINS! YEH YEH … SAY IT AGAIN … PUT THOSE HANDCUFFS ON MY H
 ANDS!"\n\nThey are concerned that the spread of liberty has been detrimenta
 l to the world.\n\nEverywhere liberty goes\, it leaves a path of destructio
 n. Fast food\, bad architecture\, militarism\, rampant greed\, environmenta
 l destruction\, imperial conquest\, class struggle\; these phenomena\, when
  combined\, seem to be synonymous with "Liberty."\n\nSo just as they call i
 t "liberty" or "freedom" when war and greed stalk the land\, Svenonius call
 s his band: CHAIN And The GANG …\n\nFor Svenonius \, this is another step i
 n a life spent trying to do as little as possible.\n\nHe's been seen on sta
 ge as a lecturer promoting his book "The Psychic Soviet"\, as a singer in t
 he groups Make-Up\, Scene Creamers\, Weird War\, and Nation of Ulysses\, an
 d also as interviewer of interesting people on the internet chat show Soft 
 Focus.\n\nThe Hive Dwellers (featuring Calvin Johnson)\nwww.myspace.com/kfa
 mily\n--------------\nBased in Olympia\, Wash.\, Calvin's work in undergrou
 nd culture started as a teenage fan volunteering at the local community rad
 io station\, KAOS-FM. He moved on to writing for fanzines\, organizing musi
 c and film events\, playing music in various ill-fated bands. Calvin establ
 ished K\, a locally oriented media outlet\, in 1982.\nIn 1993 Calvin founde
 d Dub Narcotic\, a recording studio\, in which he has documented the work o
 f the Somehow Is and Never Was\, such as Mirah\, the Blow\, Versus\, Built 
 to Spill\, Fitz of Depression\, Make-Up and Little Wings. It has also been 
 the incubator of many Calvin experiments in collaboration and self-expressi
 on\, such as Beat Happening\, Halo Benders and Dub Narcotic Sound System.\n
 \nThe decade of the double zeroes has seen Calvin Johnson set out into the 
 world\, acoustic guitar in hand\, as a solo artist of musical platitudes.\n
 \nCity Center\nwww.myspace.com/citycenternyc\n--------------\nSolo endeavor
  by Fred Thomas of Saturday Looks Good to Me\, His Name Is Alive\, Flashpap
 r and Lovesick since 2007. Pop-infused\, samples with Thomas’ signature sty
 le of sentiment lingering between the distortion\, loops and instruments. C
 urrently based out of NYC and playing out often\, a full-length is to be re
 leased in 2009\, though tracks are posted with frequency and for free by Th
 omas at the City Center blog\, http://citycenternyc.blogspot.com/. 
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T052023Z
LOCATION:Russian Recording\,  1021 S Walnut Street
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Ian Svenonius + Calvin Johnson
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
