DESCRIPTION:Cadmium Orange (the three-piece version: Jason Groth\, Lee Mant
 le\, and Chris Reinhart) reunite for the first time since 2004 to play The 
 Who's Tommy\, live. Deke Hager\, a staple of the Bloomington music scene\, 
 joins them as lead singer for the show. The version adapts The Who's incred
 ible 1969-1970 live performance of the album with some of the recorded trac
 ks that did not make it into their live set. Guitar\, bass\, drums\, and fo
 ur singers -- all electric.\n\nApache Dropout opens the show with their tru
 ly lyseric- high energy\, melodic\, and chaotic rock and roll.\n\nAt Russia
 n Recording on Saturday\, May 8th.\nAll ages.\n$5.00.\nDoors open at 8pm. S
 how to follow.\nBring earplugs.\n\n"Sickness will surely take the mind wher
 e minds can't usually go."
