CREATED:20090619T182451Z
DESCRIPTION:We would like to invite you to a gourmet\, vegan dinner to rais
 e funds for Hugh and Tiga’s legal defense. These committed activists are fa
 cing 12 years in prison for allegedly organizing protests against the const
 ruction of new-terrain I-69.\n\nDinner will feature multiple courses\, and 
 will be prepared using local\, organic and wild-gathered ingredients. All f
 unds raised will go towards their sizeable legal fees.\n\nOn Friday\, April
  24\, Hugh and Tiga were arrested by Indiana state troopers. The charges le
 vied against them include corrupt business influence (racketeering) and con
 spiracy\, and could carry up to 12 years of jail time. However\, the only “
 crimes” that they are accused of committing are organizing protests of busi
 nesses and planning offices involved in the new-terrain I-69 project. The l
 aw is being used as a tool of political repression\, to stifle the outcry a
 gainst a project that most residents of the state oppose. In the meantime\,
  families continue to be evicted from their homes to make way for the bulld
 ozers\, and forests and wetlands continue to be threatened with destruction
 .\n\nAs members of this community\, it is important that we stand up in sup
 port of Hugh and Tiga. To get more information about the case\, and to lear
 n about more ways you can help\, please visit http://mostlyeverything.net.\
 n\nDinner will be served on Saturday June 27th at 7:30\, above Roots Restau
 rant (126 ½ N. Walnut). Because space is limited\, we are selling tickets i
 n advance. They can be purchased at Boxcar Books (408 E. 6th St)\, or on Sa
 turdays at the Bloomington Farmers Market.\n\n\nThe minimum suggested donat
 ion is $25 per person\, or $45 for couples.\n\n**TICKETS MUST BE PURCHASED 
 IN ADVANCE AT BOXCAR BOOKS OR THE FARMERS MARKET ON SATURDAY FROM 8-NOON. S
 PACE IS LIMITED.**\n\n\n\n\n\nBe sure to check out other upcoming benefits 
 for Tiga and Hugh:\n\nJuly 18th Community Yard Sale\non 6th st between Rodg
 ers and Waldron\nhttp://mostlyeverything.net/REALfinalgaragesaleflier.jpg\n
 \nJuly 10 Midnight Snack Vegan Ice Cream\nat Roots Restaurant\, 11pm-2am
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T052442Z
LOCATION:Above Roots Restaurant\,  126 ½ N. Walnut 
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Benefit Dinner for Hugh and Tiga!
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
