DTSTAMP:20260905T041548Z
UID:k1gtr8fjrcl5coaav8g1j8jnus@google.com
CREATED:20091111T171524Z
DESCRIPTION:Transpanther and Joyful Noise Present:\n\nFriday\, November 13t
 h Double Feature!\n\nTwo Shows / One Price\nFREE CJ BOYD CD~!\n\nVollrath T
 avern\n118 E. Palmer St.\n21+ / $8 / 8:00\n\nPrizzy Prizzy Please - http://
 www.myspace.com/prizzyprizzyplease\nDr. Manhattan - http://www.myspace.com/
 drmanhattan\nElsinore - http://www.myspace.com/elsinoremusic\n\nCJ Boyd (CD
  Release!) - http://www.myspace.com/cjboyd\nBronze Float - http://www.myspa
 ce.com/bronzefloat\nBig Colour - http://www.myspace.com/bigcolourlifegoggle
 sbreathing\n\n8:30 - Big Colour\n9:15 - Bronze Float\n10:00 - CJ Boyd\n10:4
 5 - Elsinore\n11:45 - Dr. Manhattan\n12:45 - Prizzy Prizzy Please\n\nFriday
  the 13th of November will see a double header at Indianapolis' Vollrath Ta
 vern. Both distinct "shows" will be under one roof with one cover charge.\n
 \nThe first show is an album release show for nomadic bassplayer CJ Boyd. R
 ecently signed to Joyful Noise Recordings\, CJ is releasing his new album "
 Aerial Roots" on November 10\, 2009. CJ Boyd has mastered an ethereal\, pul
 sating approach to music which flows from singular\, meditative bass lines 
 into explosive\, layered\, and hugely complex walls of sound. CJ masterfull
 y orchestrates waves of bass loops coupled with Jazz-driven improvisational
  prowess\, building upon the foundation of great bassists like Charles Ming
 us and Edgar Meyer. CD copies of "Aerial Roots" are free with admission. LP
  copies will be sold at a discounted price of $5. Local folksmith Bronze Fl
 oat and Chicago-based Big Colour will open.\n\nThe second show will step up
  the volume a bit with the enigmatic Prizzy Prizzy Please (who recently rel
 ocated to Chicago). Prizzy's uniquely anthemic art punk has as much in comm
 on with Huey Lewis and the News as it does with their punk contemporaries. 
 The band is working on a new album\, slated for release on the Joyful Noise
  label in 2010. Two Illinois-based bands\, Elsinore and Dr. Manhattan\, wil
 l also contribute to the bill. Dr. Manhattan is a wild Indie/punk band with
  an amazing\, energetic party of a live show. They released their debut s/t
  full-length on Vagrant Records in 2008\, have endured two entire Warped To
