DESCRIPTION:Please join us for the opening of ALL POINTS BULLETIN: INTERVEN
 TIONS ON CLIMATE CHANGE at SoFA Gallery! The show is running from February 
 16 to March 12\, 2010 and the opening is on Friday the 19th.\n\nArt by Amy 
 Burrell\, Jay Garst\, Alexandra Lewis\, Emily Loehle\, Candace Peterson\, J
 ane Stewart\, Marine Tempels\, Erin Tobey and Cristina Vanko.\n\nThe works 
 on exhibit were made by students of The Making of Engaged Art: Response and
  Intervention on Climate Change\, an 8-week course in the fall of 2009. Dur
 ing this hybrid seminar / studio course\, students studied the ecological a
 nd cultural implications of climate change and then formulated the projects
  on view here. The course was taught by visiting artists\, Susannah Sayler 
 and Edward Morris of The Canary Project\, a collaborative based in Brooklyn
 \, New York that produces visual media\, events\, and artwork that build pu
 blic understanding of human-induced climate change and energize commitment 
 to solutions.
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T051934Z
LOCATION:SoFA
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Art Opening: All Points Bulletin: Interventions on Climate Change
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
