DESCRIPTION:THE WOES\nOTHER GIRLS\nHALF RATS\nat The Bishop\nTuesday Novemb
 er 17\n9pm\n$5\n\nBig fan of all of these bands so I'm making it cheap to e
 ntice you to take a chance on these bands. It's a Tuesday\, it's dirt cheap
 . What have you got to lose? Why do I love these bands?\n\nThe Woes\nwww.my
 space.com/thewoes\n--------------\nImagine if you will that Tom Waits is a 
 black Brooklynite who really digs New Orleans and decided to musically capt
 ure the mood of Deadwood. Basically it's bayou. jook joint\, party music/\n
 \nOther Girls\nwww.myspace.com/theothergirls\n--------------\nCatchy indie-
 pop from out neighbors to the east\, Ohio. Sometimes I need ear candy\, and
  Other Girls fills my ears with upbeat\, catchy as fuck aural stimulus.\n\n
 Half Rats\nwww.myspace.com/thehalfrats\n--------------\nLafayette doesn't h
 ave much going for it but they can make a damn fine garage rock band now an
 d again. Half Rats are good on record and Jason at Landlocked Music will no
 t stop talking about how good they were live at Greek's a few weeks back.
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T051902Z
LOCATION:The Bishop
SEQUENCE:2
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:The Woes\, Other Girl\, Half Rats
