DESCRIPTION:Sponsored by the IU Undergraduate Anthropoligical Society\n\nSa
 turday April 4th from noon until 3 pm.\n\nThe Cultural Dance Festival is a 
 showcase of the distinctive dances originating from anywhere around the wor
 ld that are performed by local Bloomington groups. There are two components
 : the performative and the optional teaching portion. The teaching portion 
 is to have the audience interact with the dancers and learn some basic rudi
 mentary steps of the dances in a relaxed atmosphere. The ultimate purpose o
 f the Cultural Dance Festival is to present and create an interest in the d
 iverse forms of physical expression that have been employed by various soci
 eties throughout time. Groups we've had in the past include Irish Step Danc
 e\, Swing\, South African Gumboot\, Folkdance\, Breakdance\, and Indian Cla
 ssical Dance. Help us make this event grow to be among some of the great th
 ings to do in Bloomington every year!\n\nTickets are $5 at the door\n\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T052043Z
LOCATION:The Waldron Auditorium
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:The Cultural Dance Festival
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
