DESCRIPTION:The Midwest Pages to Prisoners Project is an all volunteer effo
 rt that strives to encourage self-education among prisoners in the United S
 tates. By providing free reading materials upon request\, we hope to aid in
  the rehabilitation process and stimulate critical thinking behind bars.\n\
 nDue to limited space\, overstock in particular genres\, and the specific r
 estrictions of state and federal prisoners\, we have books we cannot store\
 , cannot immediately use\, and/or cannot send to prisoners. All proceeds go
  directly toward restocking frequently requested genres and topics\, as wel
 l as general packing and letter writing materials.\n\nTables will be set up
  in the parking lot in front of our office at 118 South Rogers Street\, Sui
 te 2 (Corner of Rogers and 4th).\n\n9am - 12pm : $1 for hardbacks\, 50c for
  paperbacks.\n12pm - 3pm : $3 per bag (common grocery paper-bag).\n\nWE HOP
 E TO SEE YOU THERE!
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T052314Z
LOCATION:118 S. Rogers\, Suite 2 (Cnr. 4th & Rogers)
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Midwest Pages to Prisoners Project Book Sale!
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
