DESCRIPTION:3rd Annual Naughty or Nice Party!\nA benefit for Boxcar Books a
 nd The Midwest Pages to Prisoners Project\nFriday\, December 18th\nAt The B
 luebird\nDoors at 9:30pm. $5 per person\nDJs\, Photobooth\, Dancing\, Burle
 sque!\n21+\n\nYou've been good all year\, now it's time to get hot and swea
 ty at Boxcar's 3rd Annual Naughty or Nice Benefit! Fulfill your fantasies w
 ith Dirty Santa and Mrs. Claus at the $1 photobooth. Head to the Island of 
 Misfit Toys with a sexy syndicate of DJs that will be providing the soundtr
 ack to the night of your life! And a special performance by the Bloomington
  Burlesque Brigade will make you get everything you've ever wanted and more
 \, all on Friday\, December 18th at the Bluebird as a benefit for Boxcar Bo
 oks and The Midwest Pages to Prisoners Project!\n\nHosted by Jada B of Verb
 al Terrorism Productions!\nDJ Dumptruck Molly\nDJ Dreamboat\nDJ Mason\nDJ A
 my Karr\nDJ Amber Hansen\n\nPerformances by Velvet Cherry\, Lolita Tart\, V
 iolet Phoenix & Tessa von Twinkle of the Bloomington Burlesque Brigade!\nDi
 rty Santa and Mrs. Claus Photobooth as shot by Sara Baldwin-$1 per session!
 \n\nAbout Boxcar Books: boxcarbooks.org\nBoxcar Books and Community Center\
 , Inc. is a volunteer run\, non-profitorganization that exists to provide n
 ew and used books\, zines\,magazines\, and comics on topics of social justi
 ce\, independent media\,and fiction for the community\; send literature of 
 all types free ofcharge to prisoners in the midwest\; and to provide a meet
 ing space forcommunity and literary groups.\n\nAbout The Midwest Pages to P
 risoners Project: pagestoprisoners.org\nThe Midwest Pages to Prisoners Proj
 ect is an all volunteer effort thatstrives to encourage self-education amon
 g prisoners in the UnitedStates. By providing free reading materials upon r
 equest\, we hope toaid in the rehabilitation process and stimulate critical
  thinkingbehind bars.
