CREATED:20101025T222604Z
DESCRIPTION:featuring:\nLAUGHTER HAS LONG LEGS\nDREKKA\nDAMON-DIXON DUO    
   \n \nLAUGHTER HAS LONG LEGS\nMichael Rings: guitars\, synth\, voice\nDan 
 Wick: drums\n\nThis duo rushes headlong into improv of a decidedly energeti
 c variety. Giddy loops and hyperkinetic percussion are stacked into dense a
 nd rushing blocks of sound - sometimes stretching out in motorik grooves\, 
 sometimes swerving across the median into noisy pileups.\n\nDREKKA\nMichael
  Anderson\, et al\n\nAt it's most organized\, a Drekka performance is a vol
 atile impromptu affair. Acutely aware of it's surroundings\, Drekka allows 
 sound and space to melt into a blurred union. And given the very nature of 
 the IMP series\, Drekka has decided to arrive to this event with only the b
 asic utensils in hand\; reverb\, recorders\, delays\, microphones... the ve
 nue will provide the building blocks and 'instruments'. What transpires wil
 l be up to the evening... the sonority of air conditioning or the sound of 
 one man gargling beer? October 25th will decide.\n\nDAMON-DIXON DUO\nTyler 
 Damon: drums\, percussion\nMike Dixon: guitar\n\nDamon and Dixon\, both vet
 eran musicians of the Bloomington scene\, will perform for the first time i
 n this particular configuration. IMP is proud to present the debut performa
 nce by this exciting improvisational team!\n\n\n\n\n\nhttp://www.facebook.c
 om/event.php?eid=112943878770325
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T051934Z
LOCATION:Rachael's Cafe\, 3rd and Lincoln\, Bloomington\, IN
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:IMProvised Music Project (IMP): Free Concert 
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
