DESCRIPTION:HENRY ROLLINS\nat The Buskirk-Chumley Theater\nMonday April 5\n
 8pm\n$15\n\nTickets available at the Buskirk-Chumley Box Office\, Landlocke
 d Music\, TD’s\, and online at www.buskirkchumley.org.\n\nIf Henry Rollins 
 were a question on a multiple-choice quiz\, the correct answer would be "D.
  All of the above." Best known to some as the frenetic frontman for punk ro
 ck legends Black Flag and later the Rollins Band\, and to others for his sh
 arp-tongued spoken performances\, Henry Rollins is an actor\, most recently
  on the acclaimed FX drama “Sons of Anarchy\,” author\, bringing his brand 
 of intellectual witticism to Vanity Fair as helmsman of the “Straight Talk 
 Espresso” blog and radio host on Los Angeles’ influential KCRW. He's a busi
 nessman and a philanthropist. He's a GRAMMY-nominated singer and a GRAMMY-w
 inning spoken word artist. He's an ad pitchman\, a USO veteran\, a world tr
 aveler and a TV host. And above all else\, he's a tireless performer\, aver
 aging more than 100 shows a year for the past two and a half decades.\n\nWi
 th only a glass of water and a microphone to guide him\, Rollins’ spoken wo
 rd performances are an aural marathon of insights on politics\, pop culture
 \, music\, climate change and his travels around the world.\n\n“After a lon
 g career as a firebrand musical fundamentalist\, Henry Rollins is sounding 
 remarkably like a voice of reason.” – The Guardian
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T052022Z
LOCATION:Buskirk-Chumley Theater
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Henry Rollins
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
