DESCRIPTION:Creative Voices\nOpening Reception: Friday\, March 4th\, 7pm-9p
 m\nExhibition Dates: March 2- March 13\n\nThis past fall\, Courtney Michell
 e Miller taught basic photography techniques to troubled women in Buenos Ai
 res\, Argentina.  For three weeks\, she worked with a group of eight women\
 , all of whom were victims of some form of abuse\, ranging from domestic vi
 olence to drug addictions.\nThe workshop went beyond teaching basic skills 
 and helped to give students a new language with which to tell their stories
 \, express their feelings and frustrations\, and connect with both one anot
 her and anyone who might see their photographs.\n \nUsing the medium of pho
 tography\, Courtney and her students discovered that artistic means of conv
 eying human emotions can also help overcome cultural and demographic bounda
 ries to create an international network of women.\n \n"Creative Voices\," o
 pening March 4\, is a step in process of creating this international discou
 rse about empowerment via photography among women\, Interspersing her own d
 ocumentary shots of the workshop along with the photographs of her students
 \, we get to experience Courtney's journey with her students as they find t
 heir own unique artistic voices.\n\nPaper Crane is located at 401 W. 6th St
 .\, diagonal from Bloomingfoods. Entrance is on the south side of the build
 ing\, off of the parking lot.\nFor more information\, visit www.papercraneg
 allery.org
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T052339Z
LOCATION:Paper Crane
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Art Opening: Creative Voices
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
