DESCRIPTION:Novelist and Bloomington Native David Agranoff Returns Home to 
 Promote His First Novel!\n\n\nDavid Agranoff is well known to long-time rad
 icals and environmentalists in Bloomington. As a vocal opponent of I-69\, a
 nd a lead organizer in the fight against the Lake Griffy golf course\, the 
 Bloomington native had a reputation as a trouble maker. Now living in Orego
 n\, he is stirring the pot with fiction. Agranoff is celebrating the releas
 e of his first novel\, The Vegan Revolution...with Zombies\, with readings 
 and book signings in Indianapolis and Bloomington during the week before Ha
 lloween.\n\nHis short story collection\, Screams From a Dying World\, relea
 sed last summer\, has recently been nominated for a Wonderland award for be
 st collection\, and his first novel was just released in September by a Por
 tland-based horror publisher\, Deadite Press.\n\n“The novel is a satire tha
 t takes place after genetically engineered and chemically altered forms of 
 animal flesh\, dairy and eggs turn everyone except the vegans into zombies.
  It pokes fun at the over done zombie genre while exploring the idea of a s
 uddenly-vegan world.”\n\nAgranoff himself directed a film-style trailer usi
 ng scenes from the book and released it on Youtube the day the book was rel
 eased. “The trailer looks great and has helped sell the book. It was quite 
 a surprise for an independent word-of-mouth book\, but we sold hundreds of 
 copies the day it was first available. The trailer is very funny\, and it j
 ust scratches the surface.”\n\nThe Vegan Revolution...with Zombies is avail
 able on amazon or from most distributors but Agranoff hopes Hoosiers will j
 oin him for the readings in Indiana. The Indy event is being organized by w
 ww.Indyvegans.com\, and will be held Thursday\, October 28th but the locati
 on is still to be announced. In Bloomington Agranoff will be returning to R
 hino's all ages club\, where he was one of the club's earliest volunteers.\
 n\n“Rhino's means a lot to me\, so it will be fun reading and signing there
 .”\n\nThe Bloomington signing will be held Friday\, October 29th at 6:30 pm
  at Rhinos all ages club. (331 S Walnut St in Bloomington)\n\n\nDavid Agran
 off is available for interviews the week before\, or the night of the event
 s.\n\nCount.agranoff@gmail.com\n\n(503)772-7983\n\n\n\nThe trailer can be s
 een here:\n\nhttp://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EQ3pxbn3OOs\n\n\nhttp://planetg
 reen.discovery.com/food-health/david-agranoff-vegan-revolution-zombies-inte
 rview.html\n\nhttp://www.ecorazzi.com/2010/10/13/the-vegan-revolution-will-
 start-with-zombies/\n\n\nhttp://www.facebook.com/event.php?eid=134732236578
 570
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T052334Z
LOCATION:Rhinos All-ages club \, 331 S. Walnut\, Bloomington\, IN
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Vegan Revolution with Zombies Reading with novelist David Agranoff 
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
