DESCRIPTION:The School of Fine Arts (SoFA) Gallery is pleased to announce S
 ilent Night: A Holiday Art Sale + Auction featuring current work donated by
  faculty and students from the Henry Radford Hope School of Fine Arts at In
 diana University. Additional works on display have been donated by a select
  group of local artists. This event is being held to help support the IU So
 FA Gallery’s visual art programming and the important advocacy programs\, i
 ncluding student scholarships administered by the Friends of Art. The sale 
 will open Thursday\, December 10th and end with a Silent Auction on Friday\
 , December 11th\, from 6:30 – 8:00pm in the SoFA Gallery.\n\nThe sale will 
 comprise works from the IU Fine Arts and select local artists including jew
 elry\, photography\, painting\, printmaking\, ceramics and textiles. There 
 will be special jewelry pieces made specifically for this event by Indiana 
 University metalsmithing and jewelry design students and faculty. Visitors 
 will have the opportunity to purchase beautiful wearable\, functional and n
 on-functional art pieces made by Indiana University and local artists for t
 hemselves or as holiday gifts for friends and family. Payments may be made 
 by credit card\, check\, or cash.\n\nOn Friday\, December 11\, Silent Night
  will be preceded by the Fine Arts Student Award Ceremony for IU Fine Arts 
 undergraduate students at 5:30 pm in Fine Arts room 015. There will be a ho
 liday party after the award ceremony held in the SoFA Gallery.\n\nFor furth
 er information\, please contact the SoFA Gallery at (812)-855-8490 or sofa@
 indiana.edu. We invite you to visit our website at http://sofa.fa.indiana.e
 du. The SoFA Gallery is accessible to people with disabilities. The SoFA ga
 llery is open Tuesday – Saturday\, noon – 4:00 pm. Closed Sunday and Monday
 .\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T051846Z
LOCATION:1201 E 7th St
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Silent Night Art Auction & Sale
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
