DESCRIPTION:ANIMAL SPIRIT/SPIRIT ANIMAL is a dynamic installation meant to 
 contextualize the work of the young artists on display. There are elaborate
  mixed media work from California artists MONICA CANILAO and SWAMPDONKEY\, 
 paintings from LIZZIE RENSCHLER\, NICK MANN\, and local gallerist RYAN WOOD
 S. Other local work in the show includes a photographic portrait by WILLIAM
  WINCHESTER CLAYTOR and several small photos and prints by curator REBECCA 
 GIORDANO. AMY KARR\, SHERRI MILLER\, ERIN BRADY and ANGELA LAMONICA each co
 ntributed a textile piece designed especially for a ceramic lawn goose. A c
 atalogue essay-zine made in conjunction with the show is also available. \n
 <br><Br>\nThe opening reception/costume party will be December 5\, 2008 sta
 rting at 7 pm and is open to the public. Everyone is encouraged to dress as
  their favorite animal. There will be an informal gallery talk at 8. THE VE
 GAN BAKE EASY will be serving delicious baked goods to benefit the DEEP ROO
 TS ANIMAL SANCTUARY.
