DESCRIPTION:MAPS & ATLASES\nw/ Tera Melos and The Globes\nat The Bishop\nTu
 esday November 2\n9pm\n$10\n18+\n\nTickets available at The Bishop\, Landlo
 cked Music\, The Buskirk-Chumley Box Office and www.spiritof68promotions.co
 m.\n\nDave Davison\, Shiraz Dada\, Chris Hainey\, and Erin Elders met while
  attending art school in Chicago and formed Maps & Atlases in 2004. The ban
 ds unique style melds the technicality of progressive rock and the idiosync
 rasies of Art Rock into a fascinating and oddly accessible sound all their 
 own. Known for their virtuosic musical ability\, Maps & Atlases write pop s
 ongs with a magnificent aptitude for texture and a distinctive blend of bot
 h the intricate and organic. While 2007’s Tree\, Swallows\, Houses showcase
 s the bands more technical side\, their latest offering You And Me And The 
 Mountain\, presents more earthly and digestible songs that has earned compa
 risons to TV On The Radio\, Deerhoof\, Minus The Bear\, and Foals.\n\nwww.m
 yspace.com/mapsandatlases\nwww.myspace.com/teramelos\nwww.myspace.com/thegl
 obes\n\nhttp://www.facebook.com/event.php?eid=154556007896357
