CREATED:20100609T013209Z
DESCRIPTION:THE BISHOP presents:\n\nBREATHE OWL BREATHE\nw/ ELEPHANT MICAH\
 nWednesday\, June 9\n@ The Bishop\n9pm.\n$5.\n18+.\n\n\nBREATHE OWL BREATHE
 \nBreathe Owl Breathe sing of folklore and homespun miracles\, oral histori
 es left to thaw in the earth's crust until pre-history's giant ice cubes ro
 lled their wet bulk down the North Pole and into Canada\, finally settling 
 into extinction in what we now call the Great Lakes. The music is very econ
 omical — guitar\, cello\, drums\, piano\, other organic sounds — and the vo
 cals float between folk and country. The Michigan trio\, comprised of Micah
  Middaugh\, Andrea Moreno-Beals\, and Trevor Hobbs\, plan to release a new 
 album this summer. This will be their second appearance at The Bishop.\nhtt
 p://www.myspace.com/breatheowlbreathe\n\nELEPHANT MICAH\nElephant Micah is 
 local singer-songwriter and folklorist Joseph O’Connell. Taking cues from t
 he best of 1970s folk song-craft (Townes Van Zandt\, Joni Mitchell) as well
  as midwestern lo-fi rock (Guided by Voices)\, and emphasizing the importan
 ce of musicianship and engaging live performances\, Joe has developed a uni
 que and significant artistic voice. Elephant Micah has gradually built a de
 dicated audience after over a decade of DIY releases and tours. O’Connell’s
  most recent album Echoer’s Intent was released earlier this year. Echoer's
  Intent effectively showcases Joe’s talents as a solo performer. Beyond Bro
 oklyn says "Joe O'Connell has consistently churned out some of the best fol
 k and folk rock music out there." Interestingly\, Howard Wolfson (yes\, the
  deputy mayor of NYC and Communications Director for Hillary Clinton's 2006
  Senate campaign) named Elephant Micah's Exiled Musicians as one of his top
  14 albums of 2008\, on his music and politics blog.\nhttp://www.elephantmi
 cah.com/\n\n\nhttp://www.myspace.com/thebishopbar
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T051835Z
LOCATION:The Bishop 
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:ELEPHANT MICAH\, with BREATHE OWL BREATHE
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Let's Go! Bloomington
DTSTART:20090710T230000Z
DTEND:20090711T020000Z
DTSTAMP:20260905T041548Z
UID:if687nfg3a8l0405vicp6ip9eo@google.com
CREATED:20090706T141017Z
DESCRIPTION:(knee shy) presents:\n\n“5 | 7 | 5”\nFriday\, July 10th\n@ Gree
 k’s Pizzeria\n(211 N. Walnut St.)\n7:00 pm – 10:00 pm\n\n\nAs a duo operati
 ng under the moniker (knee shy) this will be there last foray in Bloomingto
 n (at least for awhile). It might be a reinterpretation of haiku or an obse
 ssion with the number seventeen\, or both? Call it what you will as “5 | 7 
 | 5” pins the above as the spool from which this collection is spun.\nThe b
 ody of work is seventeen pieces strong\, and represented in a storm of medi
 ums. Each work is constructed based on a haiku written in regards to the nu
 mber seventeen. The “haiku” itself is presented along with the piece to all
 ow the viewer a deeper reach into the full circle process synonymous with (
 knee shy)’s previous work.\nThe most direct past incarnation of this style 
 of number play and relativity is probably (knee shy)’s “pardon our eleven f
 ragile titles” collection from 2006. Wherein\, the number eleven was put on
  the spot and squeezed for it’s value in a myriad of ways. including the fa
 ct of the collection being made up of eleven pieces and each piece being pr
 iced at $111.11.\nIn a user friendly path\, the concept of “5 | 7 | 5” can 
 be dissected in the following way:\n\nhaiku = 5 syllable line\, 7 syllable 
 line\, 5 syllable line = 17 syllables |\nhaiku written in reflection of the
  significance of things concerning 17 |\n17 pieces of art work created as a
  response to the haikus.\n\nTo place a piece as an example\, the artist’s s
 uggest this:\n\ntitle: “17 year cicada year”\nhaiku:\n“a cicada year\njust 
 enough time for a snack\ncould be late for work”\nart piece: an hour glass 
 filled with crushed cicada shells which runs for 17 seconds.\n\netc.\n\n(kn
 ee shy)’s art work for this show involves a variety of forms including: sil
 k screen\, sculpture\, prepared objects\, audio\, and an array of other con
 structs.\n\nalso.\n\nSoundtrack for the evening courtesy of DJ LVX.
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T051825Z
LOCATION:Greek's Pizzeria
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Art Opening: "5 | 7 | 5"
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
