CREATED:20100118T182029Z
DESCRIPTION:On Friday\, February 5th\, Bear’s Place will host the live musi
 c of The Shams Band\, The Future Laureates\, and Knifey Spoonie. The show w
 ill begin at 10:00PM\, and everyone 21 years of age and older is welcome. T
 he show is hosted by the Chicago Roots Collective\, a collaboration of musi
 cians working together to help bring music to the people. Admission will be
  $5.\n\nThe Chicago Roots Collective is a new entity with roots from an old
  idea: working together can accomplish more than working alone. With ten ac
 ts in all\, each group utilizes social networking together to nourish a tig
 ht-knit community of musicians and fans.\n\nhttp://www.myspace.com/chicagor
 ootscollective\n\nThe Shams Band is the epitome of a do-it-yourself band wh
 ose music reflects its hard-working spirit. Matt David of Chicago Examiner 
 had this to say\, "The Shams Band stepped up and supplied this year's break
 out performance at the 2009 Chicago Bluegrass and Blues Festival. Their ene
 rgy\, passion\, and damn-good songwriting captured the crowd's attention\, 
 set feet dancing\, and triggered more than one sing-along." The Shams Band 
 features three songwriters trapezing the line between blues\, country\, and
  folk music. They have opened for national touring acts The Avett Brothers\
 , Bela Fleck\, Dr. Dog and David Grisman\, and are part of the Chicago Root
 s Collective.\n\nhttp://www.myspace.com/theshamsband\n\nAlso part of the Ch
 icago Roots Collective\, The Future Laureates guarantee a fun and aggressiv
 e live show. Performing at venues and major events across the Midwest—inclu
 ding Chicago’s Nike Human Race in front of 12\,000 people—TFL is known for 
 engaging audiences and leaving them clamoring for more. The band’s debut al
 bum\, Your Mom Would Like Us\, has been making waves as well. Don Thrasher 
 of the Dayton Daily News calls it “a sunny collection of pop songs with inf
 ectious sing-along choruses and a strong melodic core.” Sing along at:\n\nh
 ttp://www.myspace.com/thefuturelaureates\n\n\nWith a band name taken from a
  Simpsons episode\, Knifey Spoonie capture the jolly fun and charisma of th
 e animated cartoon\, minus the legions of fans. While other bands may look 
 serious and contemplative on stage\, KS sweat and drool. With bits of jazz\
 , post-punk\, hard rock\, and southern boogie all put together\, Knifey Spo
 onie is THE choice for the ADD music fan. The band’s first album\, Knifey S
 poonie\, was released in December 2009\, and the group toured the Midwest i
 n January in support of the record.\n\nhttp://www.myspace.com/knifeyspoonie
 \n\nBear's Place Ale House and Eatery\, located in beautiful\, Bloomington\
 , IN\, is the home for good food\, good music\, and frosty Libations. If yo
 u would like more information about this event\, please call Bear’s Place a
 t 812-339-3460.
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T051829Z
LOCATION:Bear's Place
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:CRC Presents: The Shams Band\, The Future Laureates and Knifey Spoo
 nie
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Let's Go! Bloomington
DTSTART:20100304T013000Z
DTEND:20100304T043000Z
DTSTAMP:20260905T041548Z
UID:0uic0rg32369o5tqv1j4ga7fdc@google.com
CREATED:20100301T013925Z
DESCRIPTION:WFHB'S LOCAL LIVE FROM RUSSIAN RECORDING is a monthly live broa
 dcast open to the public at Russian Recording in Bloomington - broadcasting
  live over WFHB 91.3FM\, 98.1FM\, 100.7FM\, 106.3FM across south-central In
 diana and streaming live at www.wfhb.org.\n\nDOORS OPEN @ 8:30PM\, COVER IS
  $3.00\nLIVE BROADCAST STARTS @ 9PM SHARP\n\nWFHB is excited to welcome Bow
 ery Boy Blue back to Bloomington along with local faves Whippoorwill and Pe
 te Schreiner's Thousand Arrows project. Tune in from wherever you are or jo
 in us at Russian Recording.\n\n• Bowery Boy Blue’s official beginning can b
 e traced back to the winter of 2005 when Zeb Gould released the five song E
 P Bowery Boy Blue Gives the Kids What They Want\, on the NYC-based Space Ph
 oto Records (SPR-LTD 004). However\, the release of the EP and the subseque
 nt shows that followed were the culmination of the years prior to 2005\, in
  which Gould\, newly arrived in New York City\, began writing songs and rel
 easing albums under the moniker Stereofan with his partner in crime (and no
 w wife) Megan Gould. The two self-released four albums in just under one ye
 ar before signing on with the Chicago based label Lelp Recordings to releas
 e their first official CD Stain My Heart (Lelp 1985) in early 2005.\n\nIt i
 s around this time\, mid 2005\, when a subtle shift in songwriting led Goul
 d to a new project and a new identity\, Bowery Boy Blue. Although mostly an
  acoustic project at it’s outset\, it quickly became apparent that more sat
 urated sounds and textures were close at hand. Following a solo release of 
 American Primitive style acoustic guitar compositions (All of the Morningbi
 rds\, SPR 819)\, and a second full length Stereofan CD (You Can’t Go Home A
 gain\, SPR 821)\, Gould began writing the songs that would comprise the bul
 k of the latest Bowery Boy Blue offering\, Stalk That Myth.\n\nArmed with t
 hese new songs\, Zeb and Megan Gould\, along with longtime friend and colla
 borator Sam Crawford\, headed to Chicago to record the album at Steve Albin
 i’s recording studio\, Electrical Audio\, in August of 2007. They were fort
 unate to be joined by a talented cast of characters for the session\, inclu
 ding Jason Toth (Edith Frost\, Manishevitz\, The Zincs) on drums and Marika
  Hughes on Cello.\n\nUpon completion of the recording\, Bowery Boy Blue beg
 an another transformation\, this time expanding from a solo recording proje
 ct to a full-fledged Band\, when Gould officially joined forces with the af
 orementioned Sam Crawford on lap slide and lead guitar\, Christian Rutledge
  on drums\, and Michael Trepagnier on Bass. In anticipation of the release 
 of Stalk that Myth the quartet has continued to forge it’s own sound and so
 lidify it’s standing as a collaboration intent on creating an identity as a
  foursome. With this in mind they have already begun writing and recording 
 the collection of songs that will comprise their follow-up to Stalk That My
 th.
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T051854Z
LOCATION:Russian Recording
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:WFHB LOCAL LIVE FROM RUSSIAN RECORDING
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
