CREATED:20091016T193039Z
DESCRIPTION:The School of Fine Arts (SoFA) Gallery at Indiana University is
  proud to present Surface Structures\, an exhibition of new work by Martha 
 MacLeish. This exhibition will open Friday\, October 16 and continue throug
 h Friday\, November 20\, 2009. The Opening Reception will be Friday\, Octob
 er 16\, 6:30-8:30pm in the SoFA Gallery. MacLeish will give a gallery talk 
 about her work Friday\, November 13\, at Noon. All events are free and open
  to the public.\n\nSurface Structures features curvilinear wall constructio
 ns that represent an idea about universal experiences. MacLeish’s sculpture
 s originate through painting\, working to isolate the spatial quirks and am
 biguities that she finds so compelling in painting\, and understanding how 
 these can be experienced as forms that inhabit our space. McLeish also inve
 stigates how the strong\, localized color of the plastics she uses can be m
 ade to behave more lithely through optical mixture of stripes and through t
 he overlay of transparent shadows as the forms bend in space. Her use of ma
 terials encourages associations with amorphous thought or ephemeral gesture
 s. MacLeish creates forms that animate our life experiences\, creating a se
 nse of vitality and movement\, at times comic or melodramatic.\n\nMartha Ma
 cLeish is currently the head of the Fundamentals Studio at the Henry Radfor
 d School of Fine Arts. She recently exhibited in New York\, Chicago\, Montr
 eal and other venues. MacLeish received her MFA in painting from Yale Unive
 rsity School of Art.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T052352Z
LOCATION:SoFA Gallery
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Art Opening: Surface Structures: Recent Work by Martha MacLeish Ope
 ning Reception
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
