DESCRIPTION:Love Factory Art Collective Call for Community Project Proposal
 s\n\nAttention: Creative Individuals and Groups!\nApply for the March Soup 
 Stock Community Micro-Grant!\n\nLove Factory proudly invites you to submit 
 your community-enhancing\, creative project ideas. Projects will be display
 ed and voted upon at a Soup Stock in March. Selected ideas will be funded b
 y a community micro-grant.\n\nWhat kind of creative project is Love Factory
  looking for? Anything that facilitates community interaction in a way that
  makes people pause--in a good way.\n\n- Design a treasure map (you define 
 treasure).\n- Create a neighborhood newsletter (you define neighborhood).\n
 - Make an encouraging banner.*\n\n*Idea from "Learning to Love you More\," 
 a great collection of group projects by Miranda July and Harrell Fletcher.\
 n(http://learningtoloveyoumore.com/index.php)\n\nThese ideas will be collec
 ted and discussed at a Soup Stock\, a monthly soup event where guests contr
 ibute a donation in return for a bowl of soup and the opportunity to decide
  how they'll use their funds to support the local creative community.\nThe 
 first 10 proposals submitted will be reviewed at the next Soup Stock event 
 on March 5th at Fuller Projects and voted on by those in attendance.\n\nIf 
 your project is funded\, you will be expected to provide a report of your p
 rogress to be displayed on the Love Factory blog.\n\nName:\nE-mail:\nAddres
 s:\n\nProject Summary (150 words):\nHow will you use the Soup Grant to real
 ize this project? (50 words):\nHow will this project benefit the community?
  (100 words):\nHow will you document this project? (100 words):\n\nPlease i
 nclude 4 images\, with one-sentence captions\, to better illustrate your pr
 oject summary via preparatory sketches\, diagrams\, etc.\n\nSubmit complete
 d proposals and address any questions to lovefactorycollective@gmail.com\n\
 nProposals must be received by 5pm on Friday\, February 26th\, 2010.\n\nLov
 e Factory is an ever-growing\, ever-changing collective of common people wi
 th an uncommon goal to enhance their enjoyment of art\, life\, and one anot
 her on a day-to-day basis. Through a series of orchestrated events\, Love F
 actory strives to stimulate human interaction and exploration while fosteri
 ng communication and a disruption of its participants’ everyday routines.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T052036Z
LOCATION:lovefactorycollective@gmail.com
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Love Factory Art Collective: Soup Stock Call for Proposals
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
