UID:g25eq7mh1e2qheiqh7551n938k@google.com
CREATED:20090318T175116Z
DESCRIPTION:CASPER AND THE GOOKIES (Athens\, GA)\nhttp://www.casperfandango
 .com/news.html\nhttp://www.myspace.com/casperthecookies\nJason NeSmith (ex-
 of Montreal) doesn’t know why his band is still called Casper & the Cookies
  and doesn’t care. He and Kay Stanton (also of Supercluster including membe
 rs of Pylon and Olivia Tremor Control) used to make lists of alternate\, le
 ss cutesy names\, but they’ve been so busy kicking ass that the moniker has
  ceased to be of any concern.\n\n“If The Apples in Stereo hadn’t been so go
 ddamn exciting\, Casper’s Cookies would have stolen the show. I’ll take Cas
 per & The Cookies’ charming\, exuberant\, multi-effects-pedal pop any day a
 nd consider the eyeshadow a bonus..”—Tiny Mix Tapes\n\n“With the modest suc
 cess of The Optimist’s Club\, a string of dates opening for Apples In Stere
 o and a growing reputation for wildly entertaining shows\, Casper & The Coo
 kies are poised to reach more ears than ever.”—Relix\n\n“The band of the ho
 ur\, however\, was unquestionably Casper and the Cookies\, who brought a de
 gree of unabashed rock pomposity that far outsized the tiny Tavern stage. T
 hings really got crazy when members from the band Antibalas\, which was per
 forming in the Ballroom\, literally ran in to catch the rest of the Casper 
 set after finishing their own show.”—Cleveland Free Times\n\nGOSPEL GOSSIP 
 (Northfield\, MN)\nhttp://www.myspace.com/gospelgossip\n"....a searing new 
 single that finds the Northfield\, Minn.\, band firmly in command. The feed
 back is denser\, angrier\, but it's the drumming-- a blunt weapon as oppose
 d to mere ballast-- that really makes the difference."\n-Pitchfork Media\n\
 nFIRST COMMUNION AFTERPARTY (Minneapolis\, MN)\nhttp://www.myspace.com/firs
 tcommunionafterparty\nWhile it’s important for any young group of musicians
  experimenting with neo-psychedelica to spend time cultivating an air of la
 nguid\, acid-drenched debauchery\, it was unclear whether this one\, FCAP\,
  felt it was as important to\, you know\, actually make a record. After add
 ing veteran guitar player Joey Werner\, Liam Watkins’s band of merry cranks
 ters have capitalized on the promise of their stage show with an album of d
 roned-out psych-pop\, highlighted by the opening track\, “2CB.”\n-Mpls St P
 aul Magazine ~ Best Local Rock Album of 2008!!!\n\n9pm - $4
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T052324Z
LOCATION:The Cinemat
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Casper and the Cookies
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
