DESCRIPTION:3 days of music and food!\n\nDAY 1!\n7:30pm -Open Mic Night. \n
 Come and do 10 minutes of anything you can do acoustically or with one micr
 ophone. There will be free coffee! There will be vegan snacks for sale (for
  cheap). \n\nDAY 2!\n6:00pm -Vegan potluck. Bring some food over and we wil
 l all eat it together. The theme is SOUL FOOD and GRANNY'S SWEETS.\n\n7:30p
 m (sharp) -Punk show. \nSara Cilantro (solo\, just moved to town). \nHunger
  Strike Riot (60's style poppy punk from WI)\nEric Ayotte (local folk cake)
 \n+ 1 acts TBA\n$3.00 donation required \n\n\nDAY 3!\n11:11am  -vegan panca
 ke breakfast. You pay $2 and get 3 big vegan pancakes made fresh to order (
 with berries and whatnot). Gluten free pancakes are available. Coffee is fr
 ee with pancake purchase. \n\n7:30pm -Punk show! \n\nGood Luck\n(local pop 
 music on no idea\, that shreds..no really) They don't get the chance to pla
 y local all ages shows very often and even less often are they house shows\
 n\n\nArt Vanduhlay\n(Every episode of Seinfield on DVD + healthy dose of 80
 's dc and boston hardcore = A/V.) izzy's back in town for about 5 days\, wh
 y not play a show a show?\n\nMountain Asleep\n(from louisville\, one of the
 ir last shows. loud/screamy/odd time signatures/interesting guitar parts/fu
 n. for fans of tiny hawks/pop punk/melodramatic frontmen and the kinsella b
 rothers)\n\nRest Assured\n(also from louisville\, noodly instrumental stuff
  for fans of chicago...the city\, not the band)\n\n\n\n\n\nboring stuff:\n\
 n$5 donation (don't be one of those people that avoids eye contact and trie
 s to hide from me when i'm asking for donations\, seriously..everyone hates
  that person)\n\nStarts at 7:30\, (don't be fashionably late)\n\nThis show 
 is also at a house\, so be mindful of that and respectful to the inhabitant
 s/our belongings and our neighbors or you'll be asked to leave.\n\n\n\nhttp
 ://www.facebook.com/event.php?eid=162150860464659
