DESCRIPTION:Proceeds from the Spencer PRIDE Festival go to Spencer PRIDE\, 
 a not-for-profit organization with the following mission statement: to prom
 ote and support the gay\, lesbian\, bisexual\, transgendered community in S
 outh Central Indiana by holding an annual Spencer PRIDE event that proudly 
 and honestly reflects GLBT values and diversity. The Spencer PRIDE Festival
  is also affiliated with the White River Valley PFLAG\, a not-for-profit or
 ganization aimed at promoting the well-being of GLBT individuals\, family\,
  and friends through support\, advocacy\, and education. Part of the missio
 n statement of White River Valley PFLAG states: PFLAG promotes opportunity 
 for dialogue about sexual orientation and gender identity\, and acts to cre
 ate a society that is healthy and respectful of human diversity.\n\nProbabl
 y one of the smallest towns in the nation to hold a pride festival\, Spence
 r\, Indiana is a diverse community with a rich history and beautiful locati
 on nestled in the rolling hills of Southern Indiana. McCormick’s Creek\, In
 diana’s first State Park\, finds its home in Spencer. While Spencer’s popul
 ation is a mere 3500 residents\, it serves as both the Owen County seat as 
 well as a main source of employment for several nearby counties whose resid
 ents travel to Spencer to work for one of the major medical manufacturers w
 ith a footprint in town. Spencer is located just 17 miles west of Indiana U
 niversity in nearby Bloomington and is less than one hour away from Indiana
 polis.\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T052233Z
LOCATION:Spincer\, IN
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:2009 Spencer PRIDE Festival
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
