CREATED:20100609T014658Z
DESCRIPTION:----------------------------------------\nThis year's INDIEana 
 Handicraft Exchange summer show will be held once again in conjunction with
  the Independent Music + Art Festival\, on the same day as the Talbot Stree
 t Art Fair (right across the street from our venue). With so much going on 
 in the area\, and all for FREE\, you'd be crazy to miss it!\n\nThe IHE will
  run from noon to 8 p.m. on Saturday\, June 12\, at the Harrison Center for
  the Arts\, located at 1505 North Delaware Street. The event will include o
 ver 100 vendors selling their modern handmade goods\, live music by A Squar
 ed DJs\, Shirtless Biddles\, Mandy Marie & the Cool Hand Lukes\, Pholly\, D
 . Mark & Jules\, and The Jack Davies\, as well as giveaways of great prizes
  donated by our vendors and local\, independent business sponsors. AND\, as
  a bonus for those who arrive early\, the first 50 patrons to come to the I
 HE booth in the gymnasium will receive a FREE swag bag filled with IHE merc
 handise\, treats from sponsors and vendors and exclusive discount deals fro
 m specific booths available only on the day of the event! Don't miss out - 
 be there at noon to get in line to get yours!\n----------------------------
 ------------\n\n----------------------------------------\nSummer 2010 Enter
 tainment Schedule - These bands will be playing indoors during the INDIEana
  Handicraft Exchange:\n\nIn the gymnasium:\n12:30-1:30 p.m. - D. Mark & Jul
 es\n2:30-3:30 p.m. - Pholly\n4:30-5:30 p.m. - Shirtless Biddles\n5:30-6:30 
 p.m. - The Jack Davies\n7:00-8:00 p.m. - Mandy Marie & the Cool Hand Lukes\
 n\nA Squared DJ's Annie & Andy Skinner will also be spinning records in The
  A Squared Underground all day long\, from noon to 8 p.m.\n\nIn addition\, 
 there will be twelve other bands playing on two outdoor stages courtesy of 
 the Independent Music + Art Festival.\n------------------------------------
 ----\n\n----------------------------------------\nThe INDIEana Handicraft E
 xchange is a contemporary craft fair that consciously celebrates modern han
 dmade goods\, the relationship between creator and consumer\, and local\, a
 lternative economies. The IHE is quickly becoming a notable stop on the ind
 ie craft fair circuit\, which includes events such as the Renegade Craft Fa
 irs in Chicago\, Brooklyn\, Austin\, San Francisco and Los Angeles\, Indie 
 Craft Experience in Atlanta\, Stitch Rock in Delray Beach\, Florida\, Art v
 s. Craft in Milwaukee\, Detroit Urban Craft Fair in Michigan and Art Star C
 raft Bazaar in Philadelphia\, among others. The IHE began in 2007 as a way 
 to highlight local crafters and artisans as well as to expose Indianapolis 
 to some of the best vendors on the national indie craft fair map.\n\nMost o
 f the products sold by IHE artists serve the dual purpose of art and functi
 on and range from the beautiful to the irreverent\, from the adorable to th
 e slightly sinister\, from the hysterical to the just plain bizarre. Vendor
 s may use traditional crafting techniques but they express contemporary the
 mes and design. Vendors offer a range of unique handmade goods from wooden 
 jewelry to fanciful undergarments\, from custom vintage-inspired western we
 ar to stationery\, from plush animals to natural bath and body goodies\, fr
 om hand-screened rock ‘n' roll poster art to pop culture icon finger puppet
 s and much\, much more.\n\nAdmission into the fair is FREE to the public. R
 affle tickets are sold for $2 each\, three for $5 or 7 for $10. Money made 
 from raffle ticket sales is used to purchase arts and craft supplies for se
 lect Indianapolis area public school art programs. Prizes for the raffle ar
 e donated by our vendors and local\, independent business sponsors.\n\nThe 
 event is kid-friendly\, but some artists’ work features the occasional dirt
 y word or sexual image\, so parents might want to take a gander before thei
 r little ones get an eye full.\n\nThe INDIEana Handicraft Exchange is the f
 irst and only of its kind in Indianapolis and is currently held biannually.
 \n----------------------------------------
LAST-MODIFIED:20230221T052427Z
LOCATION:Harrison Center for the Arts\, 1505 North Delaware Street
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:INDIEana Handicraft Exchange
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
