UID:4sngfcroon9k7mpgcsiofqj1u9@google.com
CREATED:20230910T184359Z
DESCRIPTION:Bloomington Poetry Slam Open Mic featuring Ellise Smith.<br> <b
 r>"Join the Bloomington Poetry Slam with your local wordsmiths for a night 
 of poetry\, libations\, and passion! The night will begin with an open mic 
 featuring local artists\, singers\, and writers\, and end with a poetry sla
 m.<br>This month\, our featured artist is Ellise Smith!<br>Ellise is a Detr
 oit native who won her first slam here in Bloomington. After receiving her 
 masters\, she continued her education by perusing her Ph.D. in Urban Educat
 ion Studies at IUPUI where she researches the experiences of fat bodies. El
 lise uses spoken word as a platform to share the narratives she has experie
 nces as a fat\, Black woman. Her style of spoken word adapts freestyle lyri
 cism and humor to capture moments of her life while engaging the audience. 
 In 2024\, Ellise will release two bodies of work: a chapbook titled "Do Fat
  Girls\, Run?" and a novel with original poetry and narratives titled "+Plu
 s Size Magic". The overall goal of Ellise's work is to share the experience
 s of bodies that are often silenced.<br>Sign up for the open mic or poetry 
 slam below by commenting below or emailing bloomingtonpoetryslam@gmail.com 
 <br>Hosted by Dan "Sully" Sullivan &amp\; Andrea M. Sterling<br>Grooves bro
 ught to you by DJ Good Peoples<br>Venue is wheel chair accessible.<br>For c
 omplete rules\, click here: <a href="https://www.facebook.com/notes/bloomin
 gton-slam-poetry/2019-2020-bloomington-poetry-slam-info/1880222695376326/">
 https://www.facebook.com/notes/bloomington-slam-poetry/2019-2020-bloomingto
 n-poetry-slam-info/1880222695376326/</a><br>Performers should arrive by 8:1
 5pm so we can get everyone signed in. "<br> <br>$5 18+. 8:30pm<br><a href="
 http://thebishopbar.com/events/poetry-slam-50">Event Page</a>
LAST-MODIFIED:20230910T184359Z
LOCATION:The Bishop Bar\, 123 S Walnut St\, Bloomington\, IN 47404
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Bloomington Poetry Slam Open Mic featuring Ellise Smith 18+
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
