DESCRIPTION:Organizing Everywhere – a panel discussion part of Care Not Cag
 es' ongoing abolitionist film series. <br> <br>Panel guests include…<br><br
 >Brett Story\, whose films are showing at IU Cinema throughout the weekend\
 , and see an excerpt from her acclaimed new film\, Union\, about the drive 
 to organize workers at Amazon.<br><br>Judah Schept\, author of Progressive 
 Punishment – the book about our own county’s fight against a new jail in 20
 08. Judah’s new book is titled The Jail is Everywhere: Fighting the New Geo
 graphy of Mass Incarceration.<br><br>Emmanuel Ortiz is a celebrated activis
 t and spoken-word poet. Emmanuel has worked with the Minnesota Alliance for
  the Indigenous Zapatistas\, Estación Libre\, and most recently\, Help Not 
 Handcuffs – a carceral expansion resistance group very similar to Care not 
 Cages based out of Fort Wayne\, IN.<br><br>Sam Holdeman is a member of Care
  Not Cages and has been actively in the struggle against the construction o
 f a new jail and for the investment instead in the care and wellbeing of Mo
 nroe County community members.<br><br>Jess Zhang is a research analyst with
  Vera’s Beyond Jails initiative\, where she is supporting research and advo
 cacy work on electronic monitoring and jail incarceration. Jess was a co-au
 thor of The Fox Designing the Henhouse\, which you may have seen on Care No
 t Cage’s zine table!<br> <br>Free\, All Ages\, 3pm<br><a href="https://www.
 instagram.com/p/C4lKe_1OjPL/">Instagram post </a>
LAST-MODIFIED:20240318T155326Z
LOCATION:Redbud Books\, 408 W Kirkwood Ave\, Bloomington\, IN 47404\, USA
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Care Not Cages - Organizing Everywhere panel discussion
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
