CREATED:20231112T134908Z
DESCRIPTION:From the website: <br>"In a conversation with IU faculty and st
 udents\, <strong>Pussy Riot</strong> co-founder <strong>Nadya Tolokonnikova
 </strong> will talk about art\, activism\, truth in media\, and the fight a
 gainst authoritarianism. The interview-style conversation with a student an
 d faculty members affiliated with the university’s Russian and East Europea
 n Institute will be followed by an audience Q&amp\;A.<p>Following the discu
 ssion\, Tolokonnikova will present a DJ set.</p><p>Known for incorporating 
 punk rock in some of its works\, Pussy Riot is a feminist conceptual art co
 llective that also founded the independent news site Mediazona. The group u
 ses provocative art of all kinds to speak truth to power and bring corrupti
 on and human rights violations to light.</p><p>Pussy Riot came to world-wid
 e attention in 2012\, when Tolokonnikova and other members of the group wer
 e imprisoned in labor camps for two years after a protest performance in Ru
 ssia. Recently\, Pussy Riot won the 2023 <a href="https://woodyguthriecente
 r.org/about/woody-guthrie-prize/">Woody Guthrie Prize</a>\, which is given 
 annually to an artist that best exemplifies Guthrie’s spirt and work by spe
 aking for the less fortunate. Also this year\, Tolokonnikova was placed on 
 Vladimir Putin’s Most Wanted Criminal Suspects List.</p><p>The conversation
  with Nadya Tolokonnikova may include troubling content about war\, violenc
 e\, and imprisonment. The DJ set will have flashing lights and haze and may
  be provocative."</p><p>7:pm Free but ticketed. (Sold out) All Ages!  <br><
 /p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20231112T134908Z
LOCATION:Buskirk-Chumley Theater\, 114 E Kirkwood Ave\, Bloomington\, IN 47
 408
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Pussy Riot: Light and Truth (Sold out)
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
