DESCRIPTION:From an Email: <br> <br>Sounds From the Black Hole is a concert
  series featuring experimentalmusic and explorations of sound\, occurring e
 very 4th Saturday of themonth. <br> <br> The final show of the 2023 series.
  It's been a good year forBloomington experimental music and there will be 
 more sounds coming in2024! <br> <br>Without Whom is the trio of Hazel Bento
 n on electronics/synth\, BenMyers on guitar/menagerie and Joseph Trahan on 
 sax/samples. They havebeen creating music independently as Stroking Vines (
 Hazel)\, Lather(Ben)\, and Spiral (Joseph) and recently played their first 
 gig as partof WFHB's Local Live Remote with Technicolor Band. <br> <br> Hea
 ven's Gape is an "abrasive and unlistenable noise" trio fromChicago. a good
  example of the "noise not music" mindset that willleave you with feelings 
 akin to watching this cute animal video:<a href="https://youtu.be/JTDVq-ayE
 4M?si=K669Ub4nn1Zf9znd">https://youtu.be/JTDVq-ayE4M?si=K669Ub4nn1Zf9znd</a
 >Harmful Linguistics is the psychotic power electronics guise of MattCobaug
 h (Hideous Figure) focusing on self pity and mental insanity.<a href="https
 ://hideousfigure.bandcamp.com/album/worse-with-time">https://hideousfigure.
 bandcamp.com/album/worse-with-time</a><br> <br>7:pm $7 All Ages! <br><a hre
 f="https://www.orbitbtown.com/events/sounds-from-the-black-hole-without-who
 m-heavens-gape-harmful-linguistics">Event Page</a>
LAST-MODIFIED:20231206T154839Z
