UID:1thve5iv16q4536q2c4uha5jpg@google.com
CREATED:20240102T031526Z
DESCRIPTION:"Since 1989\, the slowest metal band on the planet has conjured
  some of music’s most striking tectonic changes. Not only did the band Eart
 h create a glacially paced subgenre of metal and play a pivotal role in the
  popularization of grunge\, but visionary leader Dylan Carlson also did it 
 while battling small-town boredom\, heroin addiction\, and the tragic death
  of his roommate and best friend\, Kurt Cobain.<p>Despite the high volume o
 f its beloved and beautiful drone metal\, Earth has rarely had much to say 
 for itself. For the first time\, in a moving saga that respects the music a
 s much as the ragtag cast of eccentrics and surreal Pacific Northwest majes
 ty that shaped it\, Clyde Petersen gets to the core of the could-have-been-
 tragic triumph of Earth\, the slow band that changed everything it touched.
 "</p><br><br>8:pm $8 18+<br><a href="https://vimeo.com/787167814">Trailer</
 a><br><br><a href="https://cicadacinema.com/products/even-hell-has-its-hero
 es-january-18-the-bishop-8pm">Event Page</a>
LAST-MODIFIED:20240102T031526Z
LOCATION:The Bishop Bar\, 123 S Walnut St\, Bloomington\, IN 47404
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Cicada Cinema: Even Hell Has It's Heroes (2023) 18+
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
