DTSTART:20151021T170000Z
DTEND:20151022T030000Z
DTSTAMP:20260905T041548Z
UID:q218fj4e1ekvc142d4h7a5k2fg@google.com
CREATED:20150726T200337Z
DESCRIPTION:ALL AGES\n\nIn the ‘80s\, it seemed too far in the future. But 
 the date is now upon us. Celebrate Back to the Future Day\, October 21\, 20
 15\, at the IU Cinema. We will be screening all three films. You decide if 
 you want to start in the future and work your way backwards\, or vice versa
 . You can see all three films or just one. Start times are approximate.\n\n
 October 21 – Wednesday\n1:00 p.m. Back to the Future (1985) Directed by Rob
 ert Zemeckis\n3:00 p.m. Back to the Future Part II (1989) Directed by Rober
 t Zemeckis\n5:00 p.m. Back to the Future Part III (1990) Directed by Robert
  Zemeckis\n7:00 p.m. Back to the Future Part II (1989) Directed by Robert Z
 emeckis\n9:00 p.m. Back to the Future (1985) Directed by Robert Zemeckis\n\
 n\nBack to the Future (1985) Directed by Robert Zemeckis\nOctober 21 – Wedn
 esday – 1:00 p.m.\nOctober 21 – Wednesday – 9:00 p.m.\nFrom the Academy Awa
 rd-winning filmmakers Steven Spielberg and Robert Zemeckis comes Back to th
 e Future—the original\, groundbreaking adventure that sparked one of the mo
 st successful trilogies ever. When teenager Marty McFly (Michael J. Fox) is
  blasted to 1955 in the DeLorean time machine created by the eccentric Doc 
 Brown (Christopher Lloyd)\, he finds himself mixed up in a time-shattering 
 chain reaction that could vaporize his future—and leave him trapped in the 
 past. (2K DCP. 116 min. Rated PG.)\n\nBack to the Future Part II (1989) Dir
 ected by Robert Zemeckis\nOctober 21 – Wednesday – 3:00 p.m.\nOctober 21 – 
 Wednesday – 7:00 p.m.\nGetting back was only the beginning as the most spec
 tacular time-travel adventure ever continues in Back to the Future Part II—
 the sequel that proves that lightning can strike twice! Picking up precisel
 y where they left off\, Marty and Doc launch themselves to the year 2015 to
  fine-tune the future and inadvertently disrupt the space time continuum. N
 ow\, their only chance to fix the present is by going back to 1955 all over
  again before it is too late. (2K DCP. 108 min. Rated PG.)\n\nBack to the F
 uture Part III (1990) Directed by Robert Zemeckis\nOctober 21 – Wednesday –
  5:00 p.m.\nThey've saved the biggest trip for last as the most popular tim
 e-traveling movie trilogy ever comes to a rousing conclusion in Back to the
  Future Part III. Stranded in 1955 after a freak accident\, Marty McFly dis
 covers he must travel back to 1885 to rescue Doc Brown before he becomes sm
 itten with school teacher Clara Clayton (Mary Steenburgen). Now\, it’s up t
 o Marty to keep Doc out of trouble\, get the DeLorean running\, and put the
  past\, present\, and future on track so they can all get back to where—and
  when—they belong. (2K DCP. 118 min. Rated PG.)\n\nhttp://www.cinema.indian
 a.edu/\nhttps://www.facebook.com/events/1408489486148041/
LAST-MODIFIED:20260414T193237Z
LOCATION:IU Cinema
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Back to the Future Marathon
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
